    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501860/certified-medical-assistant-cma-neuromusculoskeletal-institute-nmi-rowanvirtua-som-stratford-nj": {
      "title": "Certified Medical Assistant (CMA), NeuroMusculoskeletal Institute (NMI), Rowan-Virtua SOM (Stratford, NJ)",
      "description": "Certified Medical Assistant (CMA), NeuroMusculoskeletal Institute (NMI), Rowan-Virtua SOM (Stratford, NJ) Apply now Job no: 501860 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Clinical, Professional Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) Rowan Medicine – Rowan ‑ Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Affiliate of Virtua Medical Group Location: Stratford, NJ Department: NeuroMusculoskeletal Institute (NMI) Reports to: Practice Supervisor Summary: The Certified Medical Assistant plays a vital role in delivering high‑quality, patient‑centered care in a busy outpatient practice. This position supports physicians and clinical staff through a blend of medical, clerical, and reception responsibilities. The CMA ensures smooth patient flow, accurate documentation, and compassionate service aligned with Rowan Medicine’s mission and regulatory standards. Under physician direction and within State Regulations, the CMA may administer vaccinations and intramuscular/subcutaneous injections. Clinical Responsibilities Prepare exam rooms and sterilize instruments and equipment. Prepare patients for visits, including: Escorting patients to exam rooms Obtaining history and chief complaint Recording vitals (height, weight, temperature, blood pressure, pulse) Perform diagnostic tests per standing orders: EKGs, blood draws, vision/hearing screenings, urine dips, PFTs. Administer vaccines and injections as delegated under State Regulations. Maintain clinical supply inventory and notify supervisor when ordering is needed. Assist physicians and nurses during examinations and procedures. Collect, label, and prepare laboratory specimens. Support minor surgical procedures and wound care. Ensure outside test results are available for physician review. Document all clinical information accurately in the EMR. Provide clinical services within scope and training, including: Laboratory testing Vision and audiology screenings ECGs Phlebotomy and specimen processing Allergy screening Clean and maintain medical equipment. Administrative Responsibilities Schedule appointments and manage patient flow. Maintain accurate patient records and verify demographics and insurance. Answer phones and assist patients with professionalism and warmth. Handle billing, coding, co‑pay collection, batching, and deposit preparation. Obtain referrals, pre‑authorizations, and pre‑certifications. Coordinate prescription requests and document physician‑directed refills. Manage incoming/outgoing mail and prepare charts for next‑day visits. Open/close the office and manage security systems as assigned. Maintain a clean, organized, and professional front office environment. Arrange patient services at outside facilities (surgeries, testing, etc.). Sign in/out of answering service daily. Professional Expectations Demonstrate compassion, dignity, and respect in all interactions. Maintain a customer‑focused approach to patient care. Attend mandatory trainings and maintain competency in all office systems. Uphold HIPAA and confidentiality standards. Assist with onboarding and training of new staff. Perform additional duties as assigned. Qualifications Required High school diploma or equivalent. Completion of an accredited Medical Assistant program. Current CMA certification (AAMA, AMT, NHA, NCCT). Eligibility under NJ regulations to administer intramuscular/subcutaneous injections. Demonstrated competency in injection techniques. Proficiency in phlebotomy. Current BLS certification. Strong knowledge of medical terminology and clinical procedures. Experience with electronic health records. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to multitask in a fast‑paced environment. Compassionate, patient‑focused demeanor. Preferred One year of experience as a Medical Assistant in a clinical setting. Pediatrics: knowledge of pediatric vaccines, schedules, administration, and triage. Familiarity with EPIC. Physical Requirements Ability to stand and walk for extended periods. Ability to lift/move medical equipment and supplies. Manual dexterity for clinical procedures. Ability to communicate effectively under occasional stress. Working Conditions Clinical environment with exposure to infectious diseases and bodily fluids. May require evening, weekend, or holiday shifts. Occasional travel to another office within the department due to operational needs. Travel time will be compensated, and mileage reimbursed per company policy. Salary & Benefits Starting Rate: $21.92/hour (Probationary Rate) Job Rate: $22.57/hour after six‑month probationary period Candidates with relevant experience may start at the Job Rate. Comprehensive State health and dental benefits State pension Generous paid time off and holidays Tuition reimbursement for employees, spouses, and dependents attending Rowan University (Glassboro campus; undergraduate only for spouse/dependents) For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTES: Only completed online applications submitted by the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S.; Rowan University does not sponsor visas for this position. Advertised: Oct 9 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 23 2026 01:15 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501859/staff-assistant-student-affairs-department-rowanvirtua-som-stratford-nj": {
      "title": "Staff Assistant,  - Student Affairs Department, Rowan-Virtua SOM (Stratford, NJ)",
      "description": "Staff Assistant, - Student Affairs Department, Rowan-Virtua SOM (Stratford, NJ) Apply now Job no: 501859 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Administrative - Clerical, Professional Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Job Title: Staff Assistant Department: Academic Affairs & Student Services, Student Affairs & Alumni Engagement Facility: Stratford Reports To: Associate Director of Student & Alumni Programs SUMMARY Rowan-Virtua SOM is searching for a dedicated employee to join their team as a staff assistant. This position will serve as the primary administrative support for the Office of Student Affairs and Alumni Engagement, which serves the Stratford and Sewell campuses. They will be required to perform a wide variety of administrative and support services to maximize efficient workflow, including assisting in the planning and implementation of student programs and activities, coordinating and supporting campus events and programs, working with campus partners, and helping to manage efforts to address food insecurity among students. Leadership, staff, and faculty identified diversity, equity, and inclusion as core values for Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine. We believe promoting these values cultivates a more diverse physician workforce and develops skillful, culturally competent physicians to improve health and eradicate health disparities. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Oversee student organization event requests for approval through University Events and provide planning guidelines for both the Stratford and Sewell campuses, ensuring compliance with university policies and deadlines. This includes room reservations and correspondence with University Events, University support services, food services and student leaders. Serve as the primary point of contact at the front desk for the Office of Student Affairs and Alumni Engagement to welcome students and visitors and provide professional administrative support as needed. Provides administrative support to the Student Affairs Division of Academic Affairs & Student Services, including calendar management, scheduling, meeting logistics, travel arrangements, copying/collating, etc. as needed. Assist in the implementation and administration of programs that support School of Osteopathic Medicine (SOM) students experiencing food insecurity, including program coordination and resource distribution. Update and maintain leadership lists for all student organizations to support communication, compliance, and organizational continuity. Assists Student Affairs team in planning, executing, and staffing signature events for SOM students. Supports the coordination of student organization events, collections, and sales, as needed. Provides support as needed for Sewell Campus events and programs. Manage the Student Club Storage Closets and ensure compliance with student guidelines. Assist with the coordination of the sales, distribution, and inventory tracking of student white coats and medical kits. Prepares and/or compiles special reports, meeting minutes, and other related reports within prescribed guidelines. Provides timely and accurate responses to student, alumni, staff and faculty inquiries. As needed, assist with official student correspondence. Maintains essential records as needed. Keeps abreast of all federal, state, and Rowan University regulations, laws, and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified. Performs other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE Bachelor’s degree in liberal arts, public or business administration, social sciences, or a related field, plus one (1) year of professional level experience in a business office, government agency, or university setting. Applicants must possess strong interpersonal, writing, and organization skills and have the ability to perform assigned tasks with minimal supervision. Experience working with student populations is preferred. Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Excel, Word, and PowerPoint and the Google platform is required as well as the capacity to learn required university software programs and systems. The candidate for this position will be expected to travel regularly between campuses to support food insecurity initiatives and, on occasion, to support Student Affairs programs (mileage reimbursed). Awareness of own attitudes, beliefs, biases, and assumptions about others; respect and openness towards people whose social and cultural background is different from one’s own. Ability to recognize and manage one’s behaviors and communication to create an inclusive, equitable, and welcoming environment within the department/organization. SALARY INFORMATION In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $50,000-$54,573.83, with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. BENEFIT INFORMATION Eligible employees receive: Comprehensive NJ State health, dental, and retirement benefits Generous paid time off and holidays Tuition reimbursement for employees, spouses, and dependents attending Rowan University (Glassboro campus; undergraduate only for spouse/dependents) For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTES Only completed, online applications submitted on or before the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Oct 9 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 23 2026 01:00 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501747/certified-medical-assistant-cma-department-of-family-medicine-rowanvirtua-som-mt-laurel-nj": {
      "title": "Certified Medical Assistant (CMA), Department of Family Medicine, Rowan-Virtua SOM (Mt. Laurel, NJ)",
      "description": "Certified Medical Assistant (CMA), Department of Family Medicine, Rowan-Virtua SOM (Mt. Laurel, NJ) Apply now Job no: 501747 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Mount Laurel, New Jersey Categories: Clinical, Professional Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan Medicine, an affiliate of Virtua Medical Group Location: Mt. Laurel, NJ Department: Family Medicine Reports to: Practice Supervisor Summary: Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is searching for a certified medical assistant to join their growing team. This position performs medical, clerical and reception duties to support the physician in the examination and treatment of patients in an outpatient setting in support of the University’s and school’s mission and in accordance with all applicable policies and procedures. As directed by a physician, this position will also administer vaccinations and intramuscular and subcutaneous injections in limited circumstances, which may be delegated under State Regulations. Key Responsibilities: Clinical Duties: Prepares exam room and sterilize medical instruments and equipment for tests and procedures. Prepares patients for visits including: Putting patient in exam room Taking history and chief complaint Taking vitals including height, weight, temperature, blood pressure and pulse Performs diagnostic tests per physicians’ standing orders such as EKG, Blood work, Vision and hearing screening, Urine dip, PFT’s. As directed by physician, prepares and/or administers vaccines and intramuscular and subcutaneous injections in limited circumstances, which may be delegated under State Regulations Notifies supervisor to orders clinical supplies including injectables and vaccines, as needed. Assist physicians and nurses during examinations and procedures. Collect and prepare laboratory specimens for analysis. Assist with minor surgical procedures and wound care. Assures patient’s outside testing results are in the chart for physician review with patient. Documents clinical information in chart or EMR system. Provides clinical care in accordance with training and under supervisor’s direction: Laboratory tests Vision screening Audiograms ECGs Phlebotomy and processing of specimens Allergy Screening Maintains and cleans office medical equipment as required. Administrative Duties: Schedule patient appointments and manage patient flow. Maintain accurate and up-to-date patient medical records. Answer phone calls and address patient inquiries with a pleasant and helpful demeanor. Handle billing and coding for insurance purposes. Verifies demographics and insurance information and updates in billing system. Verifies patient’s insurance through insurance lists and/or via insurance websites. Collects appropriate co-pays from patients. Completes batches as scheduled prepares the deposit for pickup. Retrieves referrals for appropriate visits and enters in to billing system. Ensure the cleanliness and organization of the exam rooms and clinic areas. Maintains inventory of front office supplies and notifies supervisor when supplies need to be ordered. Signs in and out to the answering service daily as directed. Arranges for patient care services at other facilities, including surgeries, preadmission testing, etc. Calls for pre-authorizations and pre-certifications as required by the patient’s insurer. Coordinates requests for prescriptions from patients, provides chart to physician, telephones prescriptions at the direction of the physicians, and makes notation in the patient chart with date and signature. Handles incoming and outgoing mail. Pulls patient charts for next day and prepares chart. Opens and closes offices as assigned by supervisor. Activates and deactivates security system as assigned by supervisor. Maintains a professional and orderly office appearance. Other duties Always treats others with compassion, dignity, and respect. Maintains a customer-focused approach to all responsibilities. Attends all mandatory in-service and trainings as directed. Maintains competence in all applicable office computer systems. Supports and adheres to the University policies regarding HIPAA and confidentiality. Assists with the orientation and training of new employees as requested. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. High school diploma or equivalent. Completion of an accredited Medical Assistant program. Certification from a recognized certifying body (e.g., AAMA, AMT, NHA, NCCT). Applicants may be licensed in the State of New Jersey in another classification permitted by regulations to give intramuscular and subcutaneous injections. Must have attained a satisfactory level of comprehension and experience in the administration of intramuscular and subcutaneous injection techniques. Proficiency in phlebotomy techniques required. Current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Strong knowledge of medical terminology and procedures. Proficiency in using electronic health records (EHR) systems. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to multitask and work efficiently in a fast-paced environment. Compassionate and patient-focused attitude. Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of previous experience working as a Medical Assistant in a clinical setting. *If in Pediatrics: knowledge of pediatric vaccine, knowledge of the vaccine schedule, experience of pediatric administration of vaccines, and pediatric triage preferred. Familiarity with EPIC Physical Requirements: Ability to stand and walk for extended periods. Ability to lift and move medical equipment and supplies. Manual dexterity to handle instruments and perform medical procedures. Must be able to communicate well with internal and external customers, sometimes under stressful circumstances. Working Conditions: Work is performed in a clinical environment. Exposure to infectious diseases and bodily fluids. May require evening, weekend, or holiday shifts depending on the clinic's hours of operation. May require occasional travel to another office within the department due to operational needs. Travel time will be compensated, and mileage reimbursed per company policy. Salary/Benefits: The starting rate is $21.92 per hour ( Probationary Rate ). After completion of a six-month probationary period, the employee's pay will increase to the Job Rate of $22.57. Depending on experience, candidate may be hired at the \"Job Rate\" to start. For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents).” For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTES: Only completed, online applications submitted on or before the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Oct 8 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 22 2026 03:00 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501808/certified-medical-assistant-cma-department-of-family-medicine-rowanvirtua-som-stratford-nj": {
