    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501830/veterinary-cardiologist-fulltime-parttime-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine": {
      "title": "Veterinary Cardiologist (Full-time & Part-Time), Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine",
      "description": "Veterinary Cardiologist (Full-time & Part-Time), Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine Apply now Job no: 501830 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Join the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine Advance Veterinary Cardiology in a Growing Academic Specialty Practice The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM) at Rowan University is seeking an experienced Veterinary Cardiologist to join our growing Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital. Full-time and part-time appointments will be considered , offering flexibility for candidates seeking a clinical, academic, or blended professional role. This is an exciting opportunity to join an established and thriving Cardiology Service within one of the nation's newest veterinary schools. The successful candidate will become part of an active specialty practice with a growing clinical caseload while contributing to the continued development of SSVM's clinical education mission. As an additional member of the Cardiology Service, you will provide advanced cardiovascular care, collaborate with a multidisciplinary team of specialists, and play an important role in educating future veterinarians while helping shape the culture and academic mission of a new veterinary program. Whether you are an experienced academic cardiologist, a private specialty practitioner seeking a collaborative academic environment, or a clinician interested in a flexible faculty appointment, SSVM offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on patients, students, and the veterinary profession. Position Summary The successful candidate will provide comprehensive veterinary cardiology services within the SSVM Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital while contributing to clinical teaching, student mentorship, and continued service excellence. The Cardiology Service is actively seeing patients and has established clinical workflows, referral relationships, and hospital support systems. The successful candidate will join a functioning specialty service with the opportunity to expand clinical capabilities, collaborate with colleagues, and contribute to the continued growth and success of the program. SSVM recognizes that exceptional faculty bring diverse career goals and practice models. We welcome applications from candidates interested in full-time or part-time appointments and are committed to working with successful applicants to develop schedules that support both institutional needs and individual professional interests. As the DVM program matures, this position will include increasing opportunities for structured clinical teaching and supervision, with anticipated student involvement throughout the clinical curriculum. Previous academic experience is welcome but not required. We are seeking a collaborative cardiologist with excellent clinical skills, strong communication abilities, and enthusiasm for mentoring the next generation of veterinarians. This role is ideal for veterinarians who: Thrive in a collaborative specialty practice Enjoy delivering advanced cardiovascular care Value teaching and mentorship Appreciate multidisciplinary patient management Enjoy building relationships with colleagues and referring veterinarians Are energized by innovation, growth, and contributing to an evolving academic community Why Join SSVM? Faculty joining SSVM have a unique opportunity to: Become part of one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine Join an established Cardiology Service with an active and growing clinical caseload Practice advanced cardiovascular medicine in a modern Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Collaborate with board-certified specialists across multiple disciplines Contribute to continued specialty service growth and innovation Help develop innovative approaches to veterinary clinical education Teach and mentor veterinary students, interns, residents, and veterinary technology students Maintain an active clinical practice while participating in academic medicine Benefit from flexible appointment options, including consideration of part-time faculty appointments Join a collaborative, mission-driven culture committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research About the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University is one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine and is committed to advancing veterinary education, patient care, research, and community engagement. Since welcoming its inaugural DVM class in 2025 and second class in 2026, SSVM has experienced rapid growth and continues to expand its academic programs, clinical services, research enterprise, and faculty. Our Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Our state-of-the-art Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital provides advanced diagnostic and therapeutic capabilities and supports collaborative specialty and primary care. Current services include: Primary Care Urgent Care Cardiology Neurology Ophthalmology Dentistry & Oral Surgery Anesthesia & Pain Management Exotics Clinical Pathology Pharmacy Advanced Diagnostic Imaging, including a GE 3 Tesla MRI and 128-slice CT scanner The hospital is designed to support comprehensive multidisciplinary care, allowing cardiology patients to benefit from collaboration with specialists across multiple disciplines. Faculty joining SSVM have access to advanced diagnostic capabilities, specialty support, and a growing clinical environment designed to optimize patient care and educational opportunities. Cardiology at SSVM The Cardiology Service provides advanced cardiovascular care for companion animal patients while supporting SSVM's mission to develop confident, practice-ready veterinarians. Our service is designed to: Deliver compassionate, evidence-based cardiovascular care Provide advanced diagnostic evaluation and management of cardiac disease Collaborate closely with primary care and specialty clinicians Support referring veterinarians throughout the region Provide outstanding clinical learning experiences for students and trainees Advance clinical scholarship, research, and innovation The Cardiology Service is supported by a multidisciplinary Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital equipped with: Advanced diagnostic imaging capabilities Echocardiography support Digital radiography GE 3 Tesla MRI 128-slice CT scanner Clinical pathology support On-site pharmacy Anesthesia and pain management support Specialty consultation across multiple disciplines The successful candidate will join an established service and have opportunities to contribute to continued clinical growth, educational programming, and advancement of cardiology within an innovative academic environment. Key Responsibilities Provide comprehensive cardiology consultation and treatment for companion animal patients Perform advanced cardiovascular diagnostics and procedures Collaborate with primary care and specialty clinicians to provide integrated patient care Support communication and relationships with referring veterinarians Participate in clinical teaching and mentorship of veterinary students, interns, residents, and veterinary technology students Contribute to cardiology curriculum development and clinical skills training Participate in quality improvement initiatives and service development Engage in scholarly activity or clinical research consistent with individual interests Contribute positively to a collaborative and supportive hospital culture Required Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree Completion of a cardiology residency training program Board certification or board eligibility through the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM) Cardiology or equivalent Eligibility for veterinary licensure in New Jersey Demonstrated expertise in companion animal cardiology Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate within a multidisciplinary specialty hospital Strong interest in clinical teaching and mentorship Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching, mentoring, or academic experience Interest in veterinary cardiology education Interest in clinical research or scholarly activity Experience developing clinical protocols or quality improvement initiatives Interest in advancing academic specialty practice within a collaborative environment Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $150,000–$200,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, appointment track, and appointment percentage. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits eligibility is based on appointment percentage and applicable University policies. Benefits may include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Both full-time and part-time appointments will be considered. Faculty rank, appointment track, responsibilities, and effort allocation will be determined at the time of appointment based on the successful candidate's qualifications, career interests, and the needs of the School. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and an outstanding quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note: Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Oct 8 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 31 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501837/associate-professor-department-of-cell-molecular-biology-rowan-virtua-som": {
      "title": "Associate Professor- Department of Cell & Molecular Biology, Rowan Virtua SOM",
      "description": "Associate Professor- Department of Cell & Molecular Biology, Rowan Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501837 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine The Department of Cell and Molecular Biology at Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine invites applications for an Associate Professor position. We seek an accomplished investigator with an established, independent research program focused on understanding the cellular and molecular mechanisms that contribute to chronic human disease pathogenesis. We especially encourage candidates whose research bridges fundamental cell and molecular biology with disease mechanisms, such as translational biology, model systems, or emerging experimental and computational approaches. The successful candidate will join a productive, collaborative department with expertise in cardiovascular disease, carcinogenesis, immunology, organelle biology, and genetics. The position is research-intensive, with limited teaching responsibilities for graduate or medical education. Salary, start-up funds, and other considerations will be commensurate with experience. Rowan also provides a comprehensive benefits package. Rowan University is a comprehensive public research university with a growing portfolio of biomedical, clinical, engineering, and translational research. The University offers a distinctive interdisciplinary research environment that brings together investigators across medicine, biomedical sciences, engineering, data science, and other fields. Rowan is one of only a small number of universities in the United States with both M.D. and D.O. medical education programs, providing exceptional opportunities for collaboration across basic, translational, and clinical research. Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (Rowan-Virtua SOM) is located on the University’s Stratford, New Jersey campus, within the greater Philadelphia metropolitan region. The location provides access to a rich biomedical and academic research environment while offering convenient proximity to Philadelphia, the New Jersey shore, and New York City. The Department of Cell and Molecular Biology at Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is committed to advancing fundamental and translational research to define the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying human disease. The Department brings together investigators studying diverse aspects of cell biology, molecular biology, metabolism, organelle function, neuroscience, and disease pathogenesis. The Department is expanding its research enterprise and seeks to recruit outstanding investigators who will complement and strengthen existing areas of expertise while establishing new interdisciplinary collaborations across Rowan-Virtua SOM and Rowan University. Faculty have access to modern research facilities, advanced instrumentation, shared research resources, and opportunities for collaboration with basic scientists, physician-scientists, clinicians, computational investigators, and engineers across the University. The Department particularly values research programs that integrate innovative experimental models and emerging technologies. Required Qualifications Successful candidates are expected to have: A PhD, MD, DO or equivalent doctoral degree in a relevant biomedical discipline. An established record of independent and productive research in cell and molecular biology or mechanisms of disease. A strong record of peer-reviewed publications and scientific contributions appropriate for appointment at the Associate Professor level. A demonstrated history of extramural research funding and evidence of the ability to sustain an externally funded research program. Evidence of effective mentorship and a commitment to the education and professional development of graduate, medical, or postdoctoral trainees. A demonstrated ability to contribute to collaborative and interdisciplinary research programs. Preferred Research Expertise We will consider any outstanding candidate, but are particularly interested in those whose research incorporates one or more of the following areas or approaches: Molecular mechanisms underlying disease. Metabolism, mitochondrial biology, and organellar function. Molecular virology and virus-host interactions. Immunology, inflammation, and immune regulation of disease processes. Computational biology and bioinformatics. Mouse or human genetics, transgenic mouse models, or other model organisms. Human induced pluripotent stem cell (iPSC)-derived models. Three-dimensional (3D) cell culture and organoid systems. Organ-on-chip or other advanced human disease-modeling platforms. Expectations The successful candidate will be expected to maintain a vigorous, externally funded independent research program; publish high-impact scholarly work; mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and other trainees; contribute to graduate and/or medical education; and participate in departmental, institutional, and professional service. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute to the Department’s collaborative research environment and to develop interdisciplinary interactions across Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine and the broader Rowan University research community. Applications should include: A letter of interest describing the applicant’s qualifications and suitability for the position. A current curriculum vitae. A 2-3 page statement of research interests, accomplishments, and future research plans. A 0.5-1 page statement of teaching philosophy and mentoring approach. The names, institutional affiliations, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references. Salary: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is $125,000 to $150,000. Placement into the range is determined by the candidate’s qualifications, professional experience and other factors. Benefits : For eligible employees, benefits include comprehensive NJ state health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents attending Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. This faculty appointment is Tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. Faculty Rank of Associate Professor is pending review and recommendation made by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Oct 8 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 11 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501888/director-of-veterinary-junior-surgical-education": {
      "title": "Director of Veterinary Junior Surgical Education",
      "description": "Director of Veterinary Junior Surgical Education Apply now Job no: 501888 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Director of Veterinary Junior Surgical Education Work type : Regular Full-Time Location : Glassboro, NJ Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Shape the Future of Veterinary Surgical Education The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM) at Rowan University invites applications for the position of Director of Veterinary Junior Surgical Education . This is an exciting opportunity to lead one of the school's signature hands-on educational experiences and help shape the next generation of veterinarians through innovative, competency-based surgical training. As one of the nation's newest veterinary schools, SSVM is redefining veterinary education through collaboration, innovation, and a commitment to excellence. Our state-of-the-art Veterinary Teaching Hospital is thriving with a growing caseload, expanding specialty services, and a highly collaborative faculty dedicated to preparing practice-ready graduates. The Director of Veterinary Junior Surgical Education will play a central role in developing and delivering a comprehensive surgical curriculum that provides students with meaningful clinical experiences while maintaining the highest standards of patient care, biosecurity, and animal welfare. If you are passionate about teaching, mentoring students, and advancing veterinary surgical education, we invite you to join us in building one of the country's most innovative veterinary programs. Position Summary The Director of Veterinary Junior Surgical Education provides leadership for the planning, coordination, and delivery of the third-year junior surgery curriculum. Working collaboratively with faculty, veterinary nurses, staff, and external partners, this individual will oversee all aspects of the junior surgical program, ensuring students develop essential surgical competencies through hands-on learning experiences. The successful candidate will be responsible for curriculum development, instructional excellence, operational coordination, external partnerships, and oversight of patient care associated with junior surgery laboratories. This role is ideal for an educator who enjoys developing innovative learning experiences while fostering student confidence, professionalism, and technical proficiency. Why Join SSVM? At SSVM, you'll become part of a collaborative community that is building something extraordinary. Our faculty enjoy the unique opportunity to shape programs from the ground up while working alongside colleagues who value innovation, teamwork, and educational excellence. We offer: A collaborative, supportive faculty culture. A rapidly growing Veterinary Teaching Hospital with expanding clinical programs. Opportunities to develop innovative educational initiatives. Engagement with motivated students in a modern, competency-based curriculum. Strong institutional support for professional development, scholarship, and academic advancement. The opportunity to leave a lasting impact on veterinary education and the profession. About the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University is one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine and is committed to advancing veterinary education, patient care, research, and community engagement. Since welcoming its inaugural DVM class in 2025 and second class in 2026, SSVM has experienced rapid growth and continues to expand its academic programs, clinical services, research enterprise, and faculty. Key Responsibilities Curriculum Leadership Coordinate and oversee the third-year surgical skills and surgery curriculum. Ensure learning objectives align with institutional competencies and accreditation standards. Develop, evaluate, and continuously improve instructional materials, laboratory exercises, and student assessments. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines to integrate surgical principles throughout the curriculum. Monitor student performance and identify opportunities to enhance learning outcomes. Surgical Program Management Coordinate scheduling, staffing, and resource allocation for junior surgery curriculum. Work closely with faculty, veterinary nurses, and support staff to ensure efficient course delivery. Assist in developing standard operating procedures and educational protocols that support consistency and quality. Maintain appropriate equipment, supplies, and instructional resources required for laboratory and surgical training. External Partnership Coordination Serve as the primary liaison with external organizations and clinical partners that provide student surgical opportunities for junior surgery labs. Develop and maintain collaborative agreements with external partners to ensure student learning experiences are met. Ensure junior surgery curriculum meets educational objectives, animal welfare standards, and institutional expectations. Biosecurity and Patient Care Oversight Develop and implement biosecurity protocols for all junior surgical activities. Ensure compliance with institutional policies, animal welfare standards, and applicable regulatory requirements. Establish processes for patient intake, perioperative care, and postoperative follow-up for junior surgery patients. Monitor surgical outcomes and assist in quality improvement initiatives related to student junior surgical training. Collaborate with partner organizations to ensure appropriate case management and continuity of care. Teaching and Mentorship Provide instruction in surgical principles, aseptic technique, perioperative patient management, and clinical decision-making within the junior surgery curriculum. Mentor students in the development of technical surgical skills and professional competencies. Support faculty development and instructional consistency within the surgical curriculum. Foster a positive, inclusive, and supportive learning environment. Required Qualifications DVM (or equivalent veterinary degree). Eligibility for veterinary licensure in the State of New Jersey. Excellent organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience in small animal surgery, surgical instruction, or clinical skills education. Board certification or advanced training in surgery or a related discipline. Experience with veterinary curriculum development or educational program leadership. Knowledge of veterinary biosecurity and perioperative patient management. Experience establishing and maintaining partnerships with external veterinary organizations. Demonstrated commitment to educational innovation, mentorship, and student success. Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $120,000–$175,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, and appointment track. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Benefits are administered in accordance with applicable collective bargaining agreements and University policies. For detailed benefits information, visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Faculty rank and appointment track will be determined at the time of appointment. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and a high quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note: Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Oct 8 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 31 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501882/temporary-part-time-hourly-accounts-payable-assistant-accounts-payable": {
      "title": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Accounts Payable Assistant (Accounts Payable)",
      "description": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Accounts Payable Assistant (Accounts Payable) Apply now Job no: 501882 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Administrative - Clerical The Accounts Payable Department within the Finance Division is seeking a dependable, detail-oriented individual to assist with daily accounts payable operations. Under the supervision of the Accounts Payable Supervisor, this position supports the review, processing, and maintenance of financial transactions while ensuring compliance with University policies and IRS regulations. This position provides valuable hands-on experience in financial operations, document processing, compliance procedures, and enterprise financial systems. The successful candidate will demonstrate accuracy, dependability, and strong organizational skills while contributing to the efficient operation of the University's accounts payable function. Primary Responsibilities Process and coordinate the review of 250 to 300 invoices and payment requests daily through ProConnect and Banner. Manage vendor statements, direct payment requests, and electronic funds transfer (EFT) transactions. Research and resolve returned checks. Prepare weekly cash disbursements for approval. Scan and index accounts payable documents. Maintain vendor records and support IRS compliance requirements. Assist with departmental projects and other duties as assigned. Handle sensitive financial information with professionalism and confidentiality. Communicate with faculty, staff and outside vendors both verbally and in writing on matters relating to accounts payable transactions; acts as a liaison between departments and vendors. Minimum Requirements Graduated from an accredited college with an Associate’s degree, preferably in Finance, Accounting or other related field. Ability to work 20 to 25 hours per week. Preferred Qualifications and Skills At least one year of experience in finance, accounts payable, accounting, or a related field. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Professional, reliable, and customer service oriented. Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (especially Excel) and detailed knowledge of advancement information systems (preferably Banner) Rate: $21- $25 per hour Hours: This temporary, part-time position is assigned no more than twenty-five (25) hours per week and is not to exceed 944 hours per fiscal year. Work is contracted annually to coincide with the fiscal year and is contingent upon budget appropriations. Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Advertised: Oct 6 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 20 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501844/associate-dean-william-g-rohrer-college-of-business": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, William G. Rohrer College of Business",
      "description": "Associate Dean, William G. Rohrer College of Business Apply now Job no: 501844 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Business Associate Dean, William G. Rohrer College of Business Job no: 018909 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Business Position: Associate Dean, William G. Rohrer College of Business – 12 month full-time position Position Description: Rowan University invites applications for an Associate Dean of the William G. Rohrer College of Business (RCB). RCB seeks an inspiring, visible, and collaborative individual who is comfortable working in a growing, innovative environment. The Associate Dean will be instrumental in helping to steer the College through the next phase of strategic transformation in support of Rowan University’s path to an R1 institution. This individual will support the Dean in crafting and implementing strategic initiatives, working directly with faculty and staff to drive excellence in all facets of the College. This position provides the opportunity to work closely with leaders across the university as well as key stakeholders. The anticipated start date is January 2027. Qualifications: Ph.D. in a business discipline from an AACSB accredited institution. Demonstrated evidence of leadership in a collegiate business school setting as well as excellence in teaching, research, and service. Familiarity with AACSB accreditation standards and practices. An understanding of undergraduate and graduate business programs, curriculum development, curriculum evaluation, and student learning in today’s business environment. Success working with different student populations and supporting their progress. Willingness and capability to take initiative to drive excellence in all facets of College operations. Demonstrated experience interacting with external constituents, including alumni, employers, and potential donors. Industry experience outside of a university is desirable. Candidates with the appropriate academic qualifications may be considered for a concurrent appointment as either an associate professor or a full professor in a tenured position. Rohrer College of Business: The William G. Rohrer College of Business is a growing, vibrant community of nearly 3,000 undergraduate and master’s-level students. Our state-of-the-art, 100,000-square-foot building brings together the latest technology, collaboration and creative spaces, career services, academic advising, and dining, all designed to create an exceptional student experience. RCB is one of a small number of business schools in the U.S. to hold accreditations from the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) for its business programs and from the Computing Accreditation Commission of the Accreditation Board of Engineering and Technology (ABET) for its Information Systems & Analytics program. RCB offers eight undergraduate majors and nine minors, along with concentrations and certificates. Graduate programs include the 30-credit MBA, a STEM MBA, a Master’s in Organizational Leadership, and an MS in Finance. The College has four departments: Accounting & Finance, Marketing & Business Information Systems, Management, and Entrepreneurship. The School of Innovation & Entrepreneurship, housed in the College of Business, is anchored by the Rohrer Center for Innovation & Entrepreneurship and is repeatedly ranked among the best programs in the U.S. RCB recently launched a School of Financial Planning, with the goal of becoming a leading program for developing the next generation of financial advisors. To Apply: Applications should include the below listed items, assembled in the following order in a single PDF file: Cover letter summarizing qualifications and the applicant’s interest in the position Current detailed CV Transcripts (unofficial copies acceptable for initial review) Names and contact information for three to five references. Applications are only accepted on line at URL: https://jobs.rowan.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until suitable candidates have been identified. Applicants will need to submit the above materials via our online application system at https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ . BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents).\" For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ SALARY In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $170,000 to $190,000, with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. Appropriate start-up packages may be available. Please visit this link to view all respective salaries within the posted range. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the University will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Matthew Sarkees, Dean Rohrer College of business (sarkees@rowan.edu). A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor's through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to 25,000 students through its main campus in Glassboro, N.J., its medical school campuses in Camden and Stratford, and five others. The University has earned national recognition for innovation, commitment to high-quality, affordable education, and developing public-private partnerships. A Carnegie-classified R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan is the fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the nation's top 10, as reported by The Chronicle of Higher Education. For more information on Rowan University, click here . Advertised: Oct 5 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501854/assistant-dean-for-student-success-and-strategic-enrollment-college-of-education": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for Student Success and Strategic Enrollment, College of Education",
      "description": "Assistant Dean for Student Success and Strategic Enrollment, College of Education Apply now Job no: 501854 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Assistant Dean for Student Success and Strategic Enrollment College of Education Rowan University Position Summary The Assistant Dean for Student Success and Strategic Enrollment serves as a senior member of the College of Education leadership team and provides strategic leadership for undergraduate student success, strategic enrollment management, recruitment, retention, selected academic affairs functions, and student engagement. Working collaboratively with the Dean, department chairs, faculty, university offices, and external partners, the Assistant Dean develops, implements, and assesses initiatives that promote enrollment growth, student persistence, academic success, and degree completion while advancing the College's educator workforce mission. Student Success and Academic Affairs Provide strategic leadership for undergraduate student success initiatives that promote persistence, engagement, academic achievement, and timely degree completion. Serve as the primary college-level administrator for undergraduate student matters requiring review or resolution. Oversee undergraduate academic administrative processes assigned by the Dean, including student appeals, petitions, academic exceptions, grade disputes, faculty grievances involving students, and Transition Point Committee eligibility and appeals. Review undergraduate academic probation and suspension matters and coordinate appropriate interventions. Collaborate with Advising, the Registrar, Financial Aid, the Academic Success Center, Rowan Global/Reach, department chairs, and program coordinators to support student success. Monitor undergraduate progression, retention, and graduation data and recommend evidence-based improvements. Coordinate communications regarding academic policies, deadlines, and student success resources. Oversee the College of Education Student Ambassador Program. Coordinate student recognition initiatives including the Pinning and Induction Ceremony, Distinguished Clinical Intern Awards, President's and Dean's List recognition, and commencement-related activities. Collaborate with Rowan Thrive to support ProfPal and related mentoring initiatives. Scholarship Access and Student Financial Success Lead the College's scholarship awareness strategy and serve as liaison for Scholarship Universe. Develop year-round scholarship communication campaigns for prospective, admitted, and continuing students. Integrate scholarship information into recruitment and orientation activities. Collaborate with University Advancement, Financial Aid, Communications, and academic departments to increase scholarship awareness and utilization. Monitor scholarship participation and recommend strategies to improve student access. Strategic Enrollment Management Lead strategic enrollment planning for undergraduate, transfer, and educator pipeline programs. Coordinate recruitment initiatives aligned with College enrollment priorities. Represent the College at recruitment events, including Open Houses, Accepted Student Days, Orientation, and community outreach. Develop partnerships with school districts, community colleges, high schools, and community organizations. Coordinate Teacher Preparation Academy recruitment and related educator pipeline initiatives. Collaborate with Admissions, Advising, Rowan Global/Reach, department chairs, and program coordinators to strengthen enrollment and yield. Analyze enrollment trends and prepare reports that inform strategic decision-making, and support continuous improvement. Ensure recruitment communications accurately reflect academic programs and curricular changes. Strategic Partnerships and College Initiatives Coordinate educator workforce pipeline initiatives and district partnerships (eg., Teacher Prep Academy, THRIVE and other pipeline programs). Support college-wide recruitment, career, and student engagement events. Collaborate with internal and external partners to strengthen pathways into educator preparation. Lead special projects assigned by the Dean that advance College strategic priorities. Leadership and University Service Serve as a member of the College leadership team. Represent the College on university committees related to enrollment, student success, and undergraduate education. Collaborate with the Dean's Office on strategic communications and operational planning. Perform other duties as assigned by the Dean. Qualifications: Required Doctoral degree (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in higher education, educational leadership, or a related field from an accredited institution. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in higher education administration, student success, enrollment management, academic affairs, or a related area. Experience supervising staff and managing initiatives across departments or offices. Demonstrated ability to lead initiatives that improve student persistence, engagement, and degree completion. Experience building partnerships across academic units and with schools, community colleges, or community organizations. Strong organizational, analytical, communication, and collaborative leadership skills. Demonstrated commitment to working with students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds and to fostering an environment of collegiality, professional development, and respect. Preferred Qualifications Experience developing recruitment or educator workforce pathways with schools, community colleges, or community partners. Evidence of program innovation informed by enrollment and student success data. Complete Applications will include: Cover letter addressing experiences related to student success, strategic enrollment, and partnerships Current, detailed curriculum vitae Copies of all graduate transcripts (unofficial accepted for initial review) Names and contact information for at least three (3) professional references (include name, title, institution/organization, email, and phone number). Confidential letters will be requested if an application is moved forward. Review of applications will commence on October 20, 2026 and continue until all suitable candidates have been identified. Applicants will need to submit the above materials via our online application system at https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ . Salary & Benefits In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $88,000 to $100,000 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10) For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Stacey Leftwich, leftwich@rowan.edu. Advertised: Oct 5 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501883/neurology-veterinary-assistants-and-veterinary-technicians-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Neurology Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Neurology Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501883 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Neurology Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Our Mission: Our top priorities are the development of an institution delivering excellent client and patient care in addition to training graduates who are competent, confident, and ready for practice from day one. Our goal is to do this through collaborative, education- and culture-focused practice creating continuity through the patient, client, student, faculty and employee journey. We anticipate our team, hospital and school will quickly grow, making this first year foundational in the structure of what the future school will look like. Position Summary: The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (SSVM) is seeking Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians to join our new veterinary program and teaching hospital. The hospital is located 1.5 miles from our main Glassboro campus. SSVM is a new and innovative veterinary teaching hospital for small animals, equipped with state-of-the-art equipment including a 3T MRI and 128-slice CT. The teaching hospital is designed to accommodate multiple specialty departments, including anesthesia, cardiology, dermatology, dentistry and oral surgery, diagnostic imaging, emergency/critical care, exotics, internal medicine, neurology, oncology, ophthalmology, primary care, and surgery. These positions will support the clinical services in the veterinary teaching hospital treating patients and educating students. Selected candidates will be able to: Provide comprehensive and quality care to clients and patients. Demonstrate a commitment to a collaborative and collegial work culture. Problem-solve and adapt to a fast-growing and changing environment with a growth mindset. Reporting Structure: The Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians will report directly to the Veterinary Technician Manager. Required Qualifications & Salary Information: The starting rate for each level is equivalent to the probationary rate listed below based on the collective bargaining unit guidelines. After completion of a six-month probationary period, the employee's pay can increase to the “Job Rate” for that position. Depending on experience, the candidate may be hired at the \"Job Rate\" to start. Veterinary Technicians (Credentialed, evidence of passing the VTNE) Level 1 Veterinary Technician Specialist (VTS) certification eligible or achieved, or equivalent specialty-level expertise Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $32.25/hour Job Rate: $35.40/hours Max Rate: $38.05/hour Level 2 Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $28.05/hour Job Rate: $31.00/hour Max Rate: $33.20/hour Level 3 Minimum 3 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $23.08/hour Job Rate: $26.55/hour Max Rate: $29.97/hour Veterinary Assistants (Non-Credentialed) Level 1 Associate degree or higher Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $23.08/hour Job Rate: $26.55/hour Max Rate: $29.97/hour Level 2 Associate degree or higher Minimum 3 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $19.87/hour Job Rate: $22.48/hour Max Rate: $24.86/hour *Hourly rates reflect each position’s pay post 7/1/25 per the collective bargaining agreement. *Employees must have 4+ years of applicable experience to be hired above the probationary rate per the collective bargaining agreement. Experience & Skills Requirements: -Has a minimum of 2 years’ experience as a veterinary technician working in Emergency, Urgent Care, or Specialty medicine. -Proficient with anesthesia and anesthetic patient monitoring of ASA I-III (preferred experience with ASA I-V) -Has experience in surgical assisting and post-operative care -Able to obtain blood pressure, interpret basic ECG, Sp02, and ETC02 and integrate clinical signs with disease processes to assist doctors in early and appropriate intervention of patient care -Available for future on-call rotation (required) -Has strong communication skills Preferred Qualifications: -CVT/LVT/RVT (active license) -Excellent problem-solving abilities (judgment, logic, creativity, conflict resolution) -Has experience running diagnostic imaging (MRI/CT/Radiology) -Strong attention to detail -Able to observe the behavior and condition of animals -Provide superior nursing care or emergency first aid to recovering or injured animals -Familiarity with the use of ventilators -Comfortable utilizing digital radiography machines to acquire images using proper technique and positioning -Comfortable utilizing advanced diagnostic equipment -Familiar with common neurologic disease, neurologic surgery and post-operative care Working Conditions Hazards Veterinary workers may be exposed to hazards like slips, trips, and falls. They may also be exposed to unpleasant odors, noises, and animal feces and urine. When working with animals that are frightened or in pain, veterinary workers risk being bitten, kicked, or scratched. Veterinary workers may be exposed to hazards like bloodborne pathogens, hazardous drugs, radiation, toxic waste, and chemical hazards such as disinfectants, pesticides, and latex. Animals The types of animals treated at a veterinary hospital can affect the working conditions. Our teaching hospital may consist, but is not limited to, the following types of animals: small mammals, large mammals, livestock, reptiles, avians, and other exotic animals. Information about the institution: A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to 22,000 students through its main campus in Glassboro, N.J., its medical school campuses in Camden and Stratford, and five others. The University has earned national recognition for innovation, commitment to high-quality, affordable education, and developing public-private partnerships. A Carnegie-classified R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan has been recognized as the third fastest-growing public research university, as reported by The Chronicle of Higher Education. For more information on Rowan University, click here The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on the Glassboro, New Jersey west campus, 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine's first class of DVM students were admitted in September 2025. Facilities include a 167,000 square foot building that is shared as an academic teaching facility aimed at the delivery of pre-clinical training, a small animal teaching hospital, and a research facility. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. As a state public University, Rowan employees are eligible to participate in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service. Benefits: While salary is one component of employment, Rowan offers a comprehensive and meaningful benefits package designed to support your professional growth, well-being, and long-term career development. As a veterinary technician within an academic teaching hospital, you will: Contribute directly to the education and mentorship of future veterinarians Work alongside board-certified specialists and faculty in a collaborative, team-focused environment Engage in continuing education and professional development opportunities Build leadership skills in an academic and evolving clinical environment Be part of a mission-driven institution committed to innovation, community engagement, and advancing veterinary medicine Comprehensive State health and dental benefits, state pension: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Extensive accrued time off/paid holidays: 22 vacation/float days per year 12 sick days per year 9 paid holidays per year Tuition waiver for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouses and dependents after one year of employment). At Rowan, you are not only supporting patient care — you are shaping the next generation of veterinary professionals while building a sustainable and rewarding career path. Notes: The job posting will remain active until all positions are filled. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Oct 5 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 31 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501874/adjunct-faculty-educational-technology-department-of-critical-literacies-technology-and-multilingual-education-cltm-college-of-education": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Educational Technology - Department of Critical Literacies, Technology, and Multilingual Education (CLTM), College of Education",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Educational Technology - Department of Critical Literacies, Technology, and Multilingual Education (CLTM), College of Education Apply now Job no: 501874 Work type: Temporary Part-Time, Regular Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Adjunct Faculty, Educational Technology - Department of Critical Literacies, Technology, and Multilingual Education (CLTM) College of Education Work Type: Temporary, Part Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to more than 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The College of Education as the oldest college at Rowan University has a long-held commitment to excellence in teaching, community engagement, and innovation in scholarship. It was recognized as having one of the best online graduate programs in the country and is fully accredited by the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP) and approved by the New Jersey Department of Education. The College of Education and the Department of Critical Literacy, Technology & Multilingual Education (CLTM) is searching for qualified and experienced Educational Technology Educators who demonstrate familiarity with emerging technologies and the standards of the International Society for Technology in Education. This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal on a term-by-term basis. Qualifications: Required Master's or doctoral degree in Educational Technology or closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education in a field directly or closely associated with STEM/CS education at the time of appointment Meets state licensure requirements for education A minimum of 3 years of public or private successful teaching in P-12 settings Demonstrated excellence in teaching and service in education in the area of Educational Technology Demonstrated ability in communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills Demonstrated commitment to fostering academic achievement, social and personal responsibility, and social justice Demonstrated commitment to working in an environment devoted to collaboration, collegiality, professional development, diversity, scholarly inquiry, student learning, civic responsibility, and respect for all people Demonstrated commitment to working with P-12 schools Familiarity with current teacher accountability requirements, research, and best practices in Educational Technology Demonstrated ability in using emerging instructional technologies and learning management systems or online platforms such as Canvas, etc. A teaching/learning philosophy consistent with the mission of the College of Education Preferred Experience with the Danielson Framework Experience with performance assessment measures Experience teaching in postsecondary settings Experience teaching content in educational technology and/or CS education Starting Date: Applications will be reviewed as needed. Contact: Questions regarding this position can be directed to Yu-Chun Kuo at kuo@rowan.edu. Procedure: The application must be submitted through our online applicant tracking system. All applications should include: a letter of application, which includes a description of teaching philosophy and interests, curriculum vita, graduate transcripts. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Oct 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501836/osteopathic-manipulative-medicine-physician-neuromusculoskeletal-institute-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine Physician, Neuromusculoskeletal Institute, Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine Physician, Neuromusculoskeletal Institute, Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501836 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a board-eligible/board-certified Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine physician to join the dynamic academic Neuromusculoskeletal Institute (NMI) that is comprised of the departments of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation and Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine. This is a full-time position with an academic faculty appointment. Depending on qualifications and experience, the candidate may be eligible for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to work as an integral part of an interdisciplinary team. Opportunities to teach the next generation of leaders in the medical field are a part of this position. In support of Rowan Medicine's mission and vision, the selected candidate will provide and manage direct patient care at one or more of the outpatient clinical offices located in the Southern New Jersey area. Working collaboratively with other Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine physicians as well as Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation physicians, the physician provides care to patients seeking osteopathic manipulative medicine. The physician provides consultation to clinical staff regarding patient care issues and may also provide patient education to meet the needs of the patient and families. Participates in a collegial relationship with the physicians, nurses, and other health care professionals. The candidate must hold the following: Valid NJ medical license MD/DO CDS license DEA license Salary: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is $160,000 to $205,000. Placement into the range is determined by the candidate’s qualifications, professional experience and other factors. Benefits : For eligible employees, benefits include comprehensive NJ state health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents attending Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. This faculty appointment is Tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. Faculty Rank of Assistant Professor is pending review and recommendation made by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Oct 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 4 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501876/primary-care-veterinarian-fulltime-open-rank-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Primary Care Veterinarian (Full-Time, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Primary Care Veterinarian (Full-Time, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501876 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Primary Care Veterinarian (Full-Time, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Position Summary The successful candidate will provide high-quality companion animal primary care while contributing to the continued development of a modern academic clinical service. Initial responsibilities will focus primarily on patient care, service development, and hospital operations. As our DVM program matures, this position will naturally evolve to include clinical teaching, with anticipated student participation beginning in approximately two years. Previous academic experience is welcome but not required. We are seeking clinicians with excellent medical skills, strong communication, adaptability, and a passion for collaborative practice. This role is ideal for veterinarians who: Thrive in hands-on clinical practice Value relationship-centered veterinary medicine Think thoughtfully about spectrum-of-care medicine Enjoy collaborating with specialists and colleagues Are energized by innovation, growth, and building new programs Want to help shape the future of veterinary education Why Join SSVM? Faculty joining SSVM at this stage have a unique opportunity to: Help build one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine Practice high-quality medicine in a modern Veterinary Teaching Hospital Collaborate with board-certified specialists across multiple disciplines Influence clinical protocols, hospital workflows, and service development Help create innovative models for clinical education Maintain an active clinical practice while preparing to teach future veterinarians Join a collaborative, mission-driven culture committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research About the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University is one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine and is committed to advancing veterinary education, patient care, research, and community engagement. Since welcoming its inaugural DVM class in 2025 and second class in 2026, SSVM has experienced rapid growth and continues to expand its academic programs, clinical services, research enterprise, and faculty. Our Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Our state-of-the-art Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital provides advanced diagnostic and therapeutic capabilities and continues to expand specialty services. Current services include: Primary Care Urgent Care Cardiology Neurology Ophthalmology Dentistry & Oral Surgery Anesthesia & Pain Management Exotics Clinical Pathology Pharmacy Advanced Diagnostic Imaging, including a GE 3 Tesla MRI and 128-slice CT scanner Faculty joining now will have an exceptional opportunity to influence clinical protocols, educational programs, and service development during an exciting period of institutional growth. Primary Care at SSVM Primary Care is central to SSVM's mission of graduating \"Day One Ready\" veterinarians. Our service is designed to: Deliver exceptional, relationship-centered veterinary care Provide students with an outstanding clinical learning environment Practice spectrum-of-care medicine that supports individualized patient needs Collaborate closely with specialty and emergency clinicians Strengthen relationships with referring veterinarians and the regional veterinary community The Primary Care Service is actively developing clinical workflows, standard operating procedures, and training programs while expanding patient services. Faculty joining now will have meaningful opportunities to shape how the service evolves for years to come. Key Responsibilities Deliver exceptional preventive, diagnostic, medical, and surgical care for companion animal patients Perform routine soft-tissue surgery and dentistry Collaborate with specialty and emergency clinicians to provide comprehensive patient care Develop and refine clinical protocols, standard operating procedures, and workflow processes Participate in quality improvement initiatives and service development Prepare for future clinical teaching and mentorship of veterinary students Engage in scholarly activity or clinical research consistent with individual interests Contribute positively to a collaborative and supportive hospital culture Required Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree Minimum of five (5) years of companion animal primary care experience Eligibility for veterinary licensure in New Jersey Demonstrated proficiency in preventive medicine, diagnostic evaluation, routine soft-tissue surgery, dentistry, and client communication Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to collaborate within a multidisciplinary team Adaptability, initiative, and enthusiasm for helping build a growing academic clinical service Preferred Qualifications Interest in spectrum-of-care medicine Interest in or pursuit of American Board of Veterinary Practitioners (ABVP) certification Interest in clinical research or scholarly activity Previous teaching, mentoring, or academic experience Experience developing clinical systems, protocols, or quality improvement initiatives Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $110,000–$140,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, and appointment track. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Benefits are administered in accordance with applicable collective bargaining agreements and University policies. For detailed benefits information, visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Faculty rank and appointment track will be determined at the time of appointment. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and a high quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note: Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Oct 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 28 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501567/nontenure-track-assistant-or-associate-teaching-professor-school-of-financial-planning": {
      "title": "Non-Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor - School of Financial Planning",
      "description": "Non-Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor - School of Financial Planning Apply now Job no: 501567 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Business Non-Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor Faculty Position School of Financial Planning Rohrer College of Business Rowan University Position Summary: The Rohrer College of Business at Rowan University invites applications for a non-tenure track faculty position with an emphasis on Financial Planning. This is a teaching-focused role responsible for delivering high-quality instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate financial planning courses. A strong candidate will bring relevant industry experience, a commitment to student success, and the ability to translate real-world financial planning practices into an engaging academic environment. Rowan University recently announced the creation of a School of Financial Planning powered by the support of Edelman Financial Engines. This is a unique opportunity to help build innovative curriculum and programming with the aim of becoming a nationally recognized hub for financial planning education. Primary Responsibilities: Teach up to 12 credit hours per semester in financial planning and related finance topics (e.g., investments, personal financial planning, retirement, estate, and tax planning, risk management). Develop and deliver course materials aligned with program learning objectives and industry standards. Incorporate applied, experiential learning techniques to enhance student engagement. Maintain regular office hours. Provide timely feedback and academic support to students. Participate in curriculum development and continuous program improvement initiatives. Stay current with developments in financial planning practice, regulation, and education. Engage in service activities that support the department, college, and university as appropriate for a teaching-focused appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience as a financial advisor or in a closely related role. Professional certification in financial planning. Prior teaching experience at the college or university level in financial planning or related topics. Evidence of teaching effectiveness and commitment to student-centered learning. Assistant or Associate non-tenure track Teaching Professors for this position are expected to hold a terminal degree or its professional equivalent. The teaching positions are 10-month or 12-month, depending upon responsibilities, full-time, non-tenure track appointments. Successful candidates will teach 24 credits over two semesters, with an option to teach overload and summer classes for additional compensation. Positions are renewable based on performance reviews and programmatic needs. Complete applications will include: Cover letter Current detailed CV Statement of teaching philosophy Evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available) Transcripts (unofficial copies acceptable for initial review) Names and contact information for at least three references; confidential letters will be requested if an application is moved forward NOTE: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the University will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until suitable candidates have been identified. Applicants will need to submit the above materials via our online application system at https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ . BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ SALARY In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is: Assistant Teaching Professor: Ranges 21-24 Associate Teaching Professor: Ranges 25-27 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. visit this link to view all respective ranges listed above: https://www.cnjscl.org/Library/CNJSCL_FT-PT_2023-2027_Salary_Charts-Approved.pdf Questions regarding the position should be directed to Jia Wang at wangji@rowan.edu Advertised: Oct 1 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501873/temporary-part-time-hourly-financeadmin-biomedical-sciences": {
      "title": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Finance/Admin (Biomedical Sciences)",
      "description": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Finance/Admin (Biomedical Sciences) Apply now Job no: 501873 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Administrative - Clerical Process all purchase requisitions according to university and department policies Ensure prompt receiving and invoice submission; research and resolve issues with purchase orders by following up with vendors and university accounts payable staff Process Non-PO payments, travel requests and travel reimbursements. Develop, foster, and maintain excellent relationships with faculty researchers, department management, university accounts payable/purchasing staff, and vendors Provide general administrative assistance Perform other miscellaneous tasks and projects related to operating and grant budgets as assigned by Director and Department Head Rate: $20 per hour Hours: This temporary, part-time position is assigned no more than twenty (20) hours per week and is not to exceed 944 hours per fiscal year. Work is contracted annually to coincide with the fiscal year and is contingent upon budget appropriations. Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Advertised: Oct 1 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501869/adjunct-faculty-ma-in-counseling-in-educational-setting-instructor-practicuminternship-supervisor": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – M.A. in Counseling in Educational Setting Instructor & Practicum/Internship Supervisor",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty – M.A. in Counseling in Educational Setting Instructor & Practicum/Internship Supervisor Apply now Job no: 501869 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Adjunct Faculty – M.A. in Counseling in Educational Setting Instructor & Practicum/Internship Supervisor, Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Adjunct Faculty – M.A. in Counseling in Educational Setting Instructor and Practicum/Internship Supervisor Rowan University A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education operates within the College of Education and offers programs including the following: Master of Arts in Special Education and Inclusive Practices; Learning Disability Teacher Consultant (LDTC) Certification; multiple Certificates of Graduate Study (COGS); Bachelor of Arts in Inclusive Education; Teacher of Students with Disabilities (TOSD) Endorsement (post-bac and graduate programs); Counseling in Educational Settings; Master of Arts in School Psychology; Educational Specialist in School Psychology; and School Nursing. The College of Education is seeking a qualified and experienced school counselor and/or Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) to supervise field experiences and/or teach professional courses within the M.A. in Counseling in Educational Settings program. The successful candidate should be familiar with the professional standards of the American Counseling Association (ACA) and American School Counselor Association (ASCA), including the ASCA National Model, as well as the 2024 Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs (CACREP) Standards. This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal. Qualifications Required Earned master’s degree in school counseling, counseling, or a closely related field, and/or hold an active Licensed Professional Counselor (LPC) credential. Effective use of learning management systems (e.g., Canvas). Ability to facilitate engaging online, hybrid, and face-to-face instruction. Strong interpersonal skills and ability to mentor and support students from diverse backgrounds. Ability to assess student learning outcomes and provide constructive feedback. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff. Ability to integrate relevant professional and human services experience into classroom instruction. Demonstrated commitment to working with P–12 schools and school communities. A teaching and learning philosophy consistent with the mission of the College of Education. Familiarity with counseling professional standards and ethical practices, including ACA/ ASCA standards, and 2024 CACREP Standards. Preferred PhD or EdD in counseling, counselor education, or a closely related field, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. At least two years of professional experience as a school counselor in New Jersey public schools. College teaching experience in school counseling, counseling, or a closely related area. Experience with CACREP-aligned curriculum, assessment, or program accreditation. Start Date: Sept. 1, 2026, End Date: 6/30/27 Applications must be submitted through our online applicant tracking system: http://jobs.rowan.edu/cw/en-us/listing/ All applications should include: a letter of application with a statement of teaching interests and experience with supervising/mentoring school counseling interns curriculum vita graduate transcripts two letters of recommendation All positions are contingent upon need for clinical supervisors and/or course instructors in a given semester and budget appropriations. For more information, contact: Cebrail Karayigit, Ph.D., LPC karayigit@rowan.edu Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501875/anatomic-pathology-post-graduate-residency-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-at-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Anatomic Pathology Post Graduate Residency - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University",
      "description": "Anatomic Pathology Post Graduate Residency - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501875 Work type: Temporary Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Anatomic Pathology Post Graduate Residency - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University Work type: Temporary Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Pre/Post-Doctoral, Laboratory, Research, School of Veterinary Medicine Anatomic Pathology Post Graduate Residency. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM) at Rowan University invites applications for one post-grad residency position in veterinary anatomic pathology that will begin July 1, 2027. The successful applicant will complete their diagnostic duty between the SSVM in Glassboro, NJ and the New Jersey Animal Health Diagnostic Laboratory (NJ AHDL) in Ewing under the primary guidance of 3 Rowan University ACVP-board certified anatomic pathologists with supplemental guidance from 2 NJ AHDL anatomic pathologists and 2 SSVM ACVP board-certified clinical pathologists. Pathology residents will be eligible for ACVP board-certification upon completion of the program. Residents will gain experience through hands-on training through the NJ AHDL and will be exposed to cases from dogs, cats, horses, small ruminants, backyard poultry, exotics and marine mammals. Residents engage in gross rounds, microscopic pathology rounds, specialty rounds, and clinical pathology rounds. Residents are also encouraged to present at regional and national meetings, teach fourth-year veterinary students, and have opportunities to conduct small research projects aimed at peer-reviewed publication. SSVM is New Jersey’s first veterinary school with the inaugural DVM class starting in Fall 2025. A 167k square foot building houses a full-service small animal teaching hospital, an academic facility with lab and classroom space, as well as research laboratory space. Services provided will include primary care, emergency, anesthesia, cardiology, critical care, dermatology, dentistry, exotics, internal medicine, neurology, oncology, ophthalmology, radiology, clinical pathology, anatomic pathology, and surgery. Applicants must have a DVM or equivalent degree from an AVMA accredited College of Veterinary Medicine and be eligible for a New Jersey veterinary license. Applications should include veterinary college transcripts, curriculum vitae, a statement of professional goals, three letters of recommendation, and class rank. The application deadline is October 28, 2026, or until a suitable candidate is identified. Candidates will be interviewed by Zoom. The starting salary is $45,000 with comprehensive university benefits. Send application materials directly to: Dr. Chrissy Eckstrand via email ( eckstrand@rowan.edu ). Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 28 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501861/overnight-emergency-veterinarian-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Overnight Emergency Veterinarian - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Overnight Emergency Veterinarian - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501861 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Overnight Emergency Veterinarian – Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Regular Full-Time OR Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Position Summary: The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University is seeking full and part-time Overnight Emergency faculty to join our program as part of our inaugural veterinary program and teaching hospital. Selected candidates will be integral in the development of the companion animal emergency/critical care (ECC) service housed within our new Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital. The hospital is located 1.5 miles from our main Glassboro campus. The ECC service will operate 24/7 and is responsible for small animal emergency cases including intake, management of hospitalized patients, and of the isolation facilities located within ECC. The new teaching hospital is designed to accommodate primary care and multiple specialty departments including anesthesia, diagnostic imaging (GE Revolution Ascend 128-slice CT and GE Signa Hero 3T MRI), dentistry and oral surgery, internal medicine, neurology, oncology, ophthalmology, cardiology, exotics, dermatology, and surgery, and a full pharmacy with sterile compounding capabilities. The veterinary teaching hospital will function as a fully operational primary care and referral center and will be staffed appropriately to provide support and balance to both clinical and educational responsibilities. Our top priorities are delivering excellent patient care and training graduates who are competent, confident, and ready from day one. This position supports an important clinical service in the veterinary teaching hospital and significantly contributes to both client satisfaction and revenue generation. The selected candidates will be responsible for providing emergency care to small animals and pet exotics– including intake, treatment, emergency procedures and/or soft tissue surgeries, and the management of the hospitalized patients. They will have direct responsibility for teaching and evaluation of veterinary students, interns, and residents in the clinical setting. Teaching veterinary students within the pre-clinical years and coordination of hands-on training experiences are essential components of the role. They will demonstrate commitment to a positive practice culture and values aligned with the mission, vision, and values of the SSVM. Successful candidates will have demonstrated expertise in caring for small animals in an emergency/urgent care setting. Although prior experience with exotic emergencies is not required, the candidate should be willing to learn and see exotics through the emergency service. These positions are open-rank and candidates are eligible for appointment at the Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor roles, either in a clinical or tenure track, based upon qualifications and professional goals. Academic rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Information about the Institution: A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to 22,000 students through its main campus in Glassboro, N.J., its medical school campuses in Camden and Stratford, and five others. The University has earned national recognition for innovation, commitment to high-quality, affordable education, and developing public-private partnerships. A Carnegie-classified R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan has been recognized as the fourth fastest-growing public research university, as reported by The Chronicle of Higher Education. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on the Glassboro, New Jersey west campus, 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine plans to admit its first class of DVM students in 2025, pending accreditation approval. Facilities will include an academic teaching facility aimed at the delivery of pre-clinical training, a small animal teaching hospital, and a research facility. Rowan University celebrates diversity and is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. As a state public University, Rowan employees are eligible to participate in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service. Required Qualifications : DVM or equivalent degree. A minimum of three (3) years of experience in an emergency setting OR completion of a structured ER training program for 6 months or more (such as emERge, VEG) OR completion of a small animal rotating internship Demonstrated teaching or training experience in a clinical setting (veterinary students, veterinary technicians, or mentees) Currently licensed in or eligible for licensure in NJ. NJ CDS permit or obtained upon hire. DEA registration or obtained upon hire. Preferred Qualifications: Experience performing emergency soft tissue surgery Experience and/or interest in pet exotic emergencies Salary Range: In compliance with the State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $170,000 to $220,000. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. Benefits: For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents).” For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Please Note: Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Sep 28 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 28 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501862/small-animal-surgery-section-head-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Small Animal Surgery Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Small Animal Surgery Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501862 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Small Animal Surgery Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM) of Rowan University invites applications for the position of Small Animal Surgery Section Head within the Veterinary Teaching Hospital. This is a full-time, 12-month academic appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. Appointment may be in the clinical or tenure track, depending on the qualifications and professional goals of the successful candidate. This position represents a unique opportunity to serve as a founding faculty member of a new veterinary school and to play a leadership role in shaping clinical services, education, and culture as the Veterinary Teaching Hospital and the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine continue to grow. Position Summary The Small Animal Surgery Section Head serves as the clinical, operational, and academic leader for the Small Animal Surgery section overseeing surgery, anesthesia, neurology, and dentistry services. In addition to fulfilling the responsibilities of a Clinical Assistant Professor (or higher rank), the Section Head acts as the primary liaison between the service and hospital leadership, ensuring alignment of clinical operations, teaching, and institutional priorities. The successful candidate will contribute to the delivery of an integrated, organ-systems–based veterinary curriculum, provide clinical service in the SSVM Veterinary Teaching Hospital, and foster a collaborative, high-functioning surgical service that supports patient care, student learning, and hospital growth. Key Responsibilities Clinical & Operational Leadership Represent the Small Animal Surgery section to Hospital Leadership and communicate leadership priorities to the section. Coordinate with other Section Heads to support interdepartmental collaboration and integrated clinical operations. Participate in and/or lead section meetings and clinical service check-ins. Oversee clinician scheduling, including PTO, CE requests, holiday and on-call schedules, and timesheet approvals. Ensure timely completion of medical records (within 24 hours) in compliance with hospital and state standards. Troubleshoot clinical, organizational, and interpersonal issues within the section, escalating concerns as appropriate to the Department Head. Serve as a liaison to the referring veterinarian community to promote strong DVM relationships and client satisfaction. Operational Development & Oversight Collaborate with the Clinical Services Department Head to develop and implement clinical SOPs, templates, forms, and operational tools. Assist with troubleshooting service operations including scheduling workflows, equipment maintenance, inventory stock, and clinical protocols. Interface with the Veterinary Technician Manager regarding technician staffing, training, and service support needs. Maintain responsibility for inventory management, including inventory lists, supply ordering, and vendor coordination. Adhere to and assist in managing the section budget, as applicable. Faculty & Team Development Actively participate in recruitment, onboarding, and integration of new faculty and staff within the section. Support the Clinical Services Department Head with corrective discussions, performance improvement plans (PIPs), annual clinical faculty reviews, salary recommendations, and hiring or termination processes. Promote a collaborative, respectful, and accountable team culture. Teaching, Scholarship & Service Provide clinical instruction and mentorship to veterinary students in a teaching hospital setting. Engage in scholarly activity that advances the discipline of veterinary surgery; the scope of scholarship will depend on appointment track and may include collaborative or independent research. Perform additional duties as needed to support the growth and success of the Small Animal Surgery service and the School. Facilities Clinical service will be delivered in SSVM’s 50,000-square-foot, state-of-the-art Veterinary Teaching Hospital located on Rowan University’s Glassboro Campus. The hospital provides primary and specialty care for companion, food, and fiber animals throughout New Jersey and surrounding states. Required Qualifications DVM or equivalent degree. Completion of a residency with board certification or board eligibility in surgery, anesthesia, neurology or dentistry . Demonstrated experience in leadership/management Demonstrated experience in teaching veterinary students in a clinical setting (strongly preferred). Licensed in or eligible for licensure in the State of New Jersey. NJ CDS permit (or obtained upon hire). DEA registration (or obtained upon hire). Salary Range In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $150,000 to $200,000 . Salary will be commensurate with experience, qualifications, scope of responsibilities, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits Rowan University offers a comprehensive benefits package including: NJ State health, dental, and retirement benefits Generous accrued time off and paid holidays Tuition reimbursement for employees and eligible family members Eligibility for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program For detailed benefits information, visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ About Rowan University & SSVM Rowan University is a top 100 national public research institution serving over 22,000 students across multiple campuses. Classified as an R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, access, and public-private partnerships. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan’s west campus in Glassboro, NJ—approximately 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. SSVM is developing comprehensive academic, clinical, and research facilities to support its innovative veterinary education model. Rowan University values diversity and inclusion and is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to protected characteristics. Advertised: Sep 28 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 28 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
