    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501845/digital-business-solutions-analyst-pss2-information-resources-technology": {
      "title": "Digital Business Solutions Analyst (PSS2), Information Resources & Technology",
      "description": "Digital Business Solutions Analyst (PSS2), Information Resources & Technology Apply now Job no: 501845 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Professional Digital Business Solutions Analyst, PSS2 Digital Business Solutions/Enterprise Applications, within the division of Information Resources & Technology Position Description: The Digital Business Solutions Analyst will work with the functional areas across the University, including but not limited to Finance, to assist with eliciting requirements for the creation/development of new solutions, integrations, and reports; make changes to existing solutions, integrations, and reports; and, help diagnose and resolve issues. In this role, the Digital Business Solutions Analyst will develop extensive knowledge of Rowan University's applications, systems of records, and database. Responsibilities: Develop and maintain understanding of internal customer requirements, workflows and departmental business support needs. Deliver precise functional specifications to include functional requirements, hierarchy, workflow, business rules, interface design and definitions, outstanding issues, data analysis, and data mapping to clients and development staff. Gather comprehensive business requirements and use cases and recommend appropriate solutions. Evaluate business processes, gather requirements, help establish and document specifications for development. Work with the Technical team to develop high level labor estimates to develop and deploy functionality. Conduct gap analysis between application and stated customer requirements and collaborate with Developers to estimate project impact. Work with Development, QA, and Production Support teams to communicate, verify, and test the desired functionality changes. Provide general technical support for various administrative applications throughout campus, including travel software, procure-to-pay software, and student advising software. Work with the clients to demonstrate the changes to the system to ensure all relevant business needs are addressed. Act as an interface with IRT to communicate and advocate for longer term improvements, and ensure that technical solutions are aligned with Rowan’s technology direction. Manage multiple competing priorities through effective organization and communication. Guide clients through the System/Software, Development, Life Cycle and IT Acquisition Process. Process monitoring, analysis, and improvement (i.e. Appman processes) Required: Understanding of business analysis principles, processes, and techniques. Three (3) years of professional experience (SQL, Query, basic table joins, aggregate functions, data mapping, rollback, etc.) Ability to develop and prepare use cases, functional specifications, and technical requirements. Ability to understand and represent the needs of the end user in a software development environment. Strong consultative and advisory skills. Strong technology, analytical, and communication skills (written and verbal). Proficient in standard query tools such as SQL. Knowledge of databases, database relationships, interfaces, and integration techniques Bachelor's Degree or higher in a business or technology-related field or relevant work experience Preferred qualifications: Experience with reporting on Higher Education, Financial, HR, or Payroll data; or, Medical systems. Experience with API’s. Salary & Benefits: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is AFT: Range 24 ($76,486 to $87,954), with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10). For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: Rowan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diverse people and abilities. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted will be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. #Dice Advertised: Sep 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501846/licensed-psychologist-ad1-wellness-center": {
      "title": "Licensed Psychologist (AD1), Wellness Center",
      "description": "Licensed Psychologist (AD1), Wellness Center Apply now Job no: 501846 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Professional The Wellness Center at Rowan University serves students in ways that support and affirm all their abilities and identities. Our ideal candidate possesses an understanding of intersectionality and how it impacts the daily lives of students. Under the direction of the Director of The Wellness Center and the Associate Directors of Counseling and Psychological Services, the Psychologist is responsible to provide the following services for University students: mental health intake assessments; triage evaluations; psychological evaluations; treatment planning; individual and group mental health psychotherapy; crisis intervention; psychological first aid; case management; referral services; and, supervision of staff as well as graduate and doctoral level trainees. The Psychologist works with university and Student Life staff across the following areas: the Student Success Programs, ASCEND, Campus Recreation and the Center for Student Belonging and Student Engagement; as well as community agencies to assist or lead the development and delivery of relevant programs, presentations, and events. The Psychologist hired for this position will be responsible for services at the Glassboro campus. The Psychologist may, at times, be required to work beyond regular business hours and participate in on-call services as assigned by the Director or Associate Directors. The Psychologist provides confidentiality, accuracy and integrity of client interactions, treatment protocols and records. The Psychologist will provide direct clinical care, supervision to trainees, and may coordinate a specific program as identified by the Director. Functional Areas of Responsibility: Direct clinical care through mental health intake assessments, triage evaluations, psychological evaluations, treatment planning, individual and group psychotherapy, crisis intervention, case management, and, as designated by an associate director, supervision of graduate trainees. Commitment to culturally responsive, identity affirming, trauma-informed care. Program development as identified by the Director and Associate Directors. Community service with events and collaborations both on and off campus Ongoing professional development with a focus on best practice models. Qualifications: Ph.D./Psy.D. in Counseling or Clinical Psychology is required. Minimum of three (3) years clinical experience in a mental health outpatient setting with demonstrated experience working with diverse student population; performing risk assessments; intake evaluations; individual, couples, family and group psychotherapy; psychological testing; and supervision of other professionals and/or trainees. Licensed as a Psychologist for a minimum of two (2) years in the State of New Jersey and able to supervise graduate and doctoral level trainees. Salary & Benefits: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is AFT: Range 26, (Step 1 $84,326.96 - Step 4 $96,981.52) with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10). For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Rowan University is an equal opportunity employer and makes employment decisions on the basis of merit. We want to have the best available persons in every job. Rowan University prohibits unlawful discrimination based on race, color, creed, gender, gender identity, religion, marital status, registered domestic partner status, age, national origin or ancestry, physical or mental disability, medical condition, sex, genetic information, sexual orientation, military and veteran status, or any other consideration made unlawful by federal, state, or local laws. All such discrimination is unlawful and prohibited by Rowan University. It is also our policy to comply with all applicable state and federal laws respecting consideration of unemployment status in making hiring decisions. Advertised: Sep 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 20 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501817/tenuretrack-faculty-position-orchestral-program-department-of-music": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position, Orchestral Program, Department of Music",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position, Orchestral Program, Department of Music Apply now Job no: 501817 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of the Arts Tenure-Track Faculty Position Department of Music College of the Arts Rowan University The Department of Music at Rowan University is seeking to hire a tenure-track faculty member to lead the university’s orchestral program with an appointment to begin September 1, 2027. The successful candidate is expected to develop and maintain an active, highly visible, practice of creative activity that is based in conducting, teach at the undergraduate level, and contribute to the various service endeavors in the Department, College, and University. Opportunities for collaborations exist within the Department, College, as well as with George Family Center for Arts and Healing. We anticipate hiring at the Assistant Professor level, but outstanding candidates may be considered at the Associate or Full Professor levels. The tenure-track faculty member to lead the university’s orchestral program will demonstrate conducting abilities at the highest artistic standard; a successful track record as an orchestra director (preferably at the collegiate level); a comprehensive knowledge of standard and contemporary orchestral repertoire; proven rehearsal techniques; and excellent pedagogical skills. In addition, this person will provide a vision for the future of Rowan University’s orchestral program, serve as a leader in recruiting outstanding students, and maintain active and collaborative relationships with public schools in the region. A master’s degree in music is required and professional experience is expected; a doctorate and/or at least three years of teaching or equivalent experience is preferred. The successful candidate should possess administrative skills, show promise for significant scholarly/creative achievement, and have an ongoing commitment to advancing the profession, both as a teacher and guest conductor outside of Rowan University. In addition to conducting the University Orchestra, teaching duties will include Instrumental Conducting and courses that match the candidate's qualifications, background, and interests. The Department of Music is a vibrant community which has 400 students and 22 full-time faculty members. Degrees offered include the Bachelor of Arts, Bachelor of Music (composition, jazz studies, music therapy, music education, performance) and Bachelor of Science (Music Industry). The campus is located in a suburban, residential setting in southern New Jersey and is near the vibrant musical scenes in Philadelphia (20 miles) and New York City (100 miles). Complete applications will include: Cover letter Current detailed CV Links to videos of both orchestral rehearsal and performance (10 – 15 minutes of each, with the camera in the back of the ensemble facing the conductor) Graduate transcripts (unofficial copies acceptable for initial review) Names and contact information for at least three references; confidential letters will be requested if an application is moved forward Review of applications will commence on November 15, 2026 and continue until suitable candidates have been identified. Applicants will need to submit the above materials via our online application system at jobs.rowan.edu. BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ SALARY In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is: Assistant Professor: AFT: Range 22-25 Associate Professor: AFT: Range 26-29 Full Professor: AFT: Range 30-33 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. Appropriate start-up packages may be available. Please visit this link to view all respective ranges listed above: https://www.cnjscl.org/Library/CNJSCL_FT-PT_2023-2027_Salary_Charts-Approved.pdf Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Timothy Schwarz, Associate Professor, (schwarzt@rowan.edu). A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . Advertised: Sep 17 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501828/tenuretrack-faculty-position-in-statistics-and-data-science-department-of-mathematics": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Statistics and Data Science, Department of Mathematics",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Statistics and Data Science, Department of Mathematics Apply now Job no: 501828 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Science and Mathematics Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Statistics and Data Science The Department of Mathematics at Rowan University is seeking to hire a 10-month Tenure-Track Faculty Position with an appointment to begin on September 1st, 2027. The Department of Mathematics is specifically interested in candidates who will develop a research program in statistics and data science applied to health and life sciences, including biostatistics, epidemiology, statistical genomics, bioinformatics, computational biology, health informatics, and AI methods applied to biomedical data. The successful candidate's research program must have a clearly defined application domain in the health and life sciences. A Ph.D. or equivalent in Statistics, Biostatistics, Data Science, or a related field is required; postdoctoral experience is expected. Preference will be given to candidates with a track record and/or potential to establish and sustain a strong research program with health-related applications. We anticipate hiring at the Assistant Professor level, but outstanding candidates may be considered at the Associate or Full Professor levels. The successful candidate is expected to develop and maintain an active, highly visible, extramurally funded research program with outstanding scholarship, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and contribute to the various service endeavors in the Department, College, and University. Opportunities for research collaboration exist within the Department, as well as with Rowan’s two medical schools — the Cooper Medical School of Rowan University (CMSRU) and the Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (SOM) — and with the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine, the first veterinary school in New Jersey, as well as Rowan’s health-related research centers and clinical partners. The Department of Mathematics is one of six departments in the College of Science & Mathematics, which is also home to the School of Earth & Environment. It is a dynamic and rapidly growing unit offering undergraduate and graduate degrees, including a B.A., B.S., and M.A. in Mathematics, as well as a B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. in Data Science (jointly with the Department of Computer Science). We also contribute to multiple degree programs across campus and serve nearly 6,000 students each year. Faculty in the department lead active, externally funded research programs, build strong partnerships with industry, and collaborate broadly across disciplines. The department maintains strong ties with Rowan’s two medical schools (CMSRU and SOM), the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine, and regional health partners, creating exceptional opportunities for collaborative research in health and life sciences. Complete applications will include: Cover letter Current detailed CV Statement of research interests, including applicant’s future research goals Statement of teaching philosophy that includes the candidate’s commitment to inclusive teaching and mentoring practices Graduate transcripts (unofficial copies acceptable for initial review) Names and contact information for at least three references; conﬁdential letters will be requested if an application is moved forward Review of applications will commence on November 1, 2026 and continue until suitable candidates have been identiﬁed. Applicants will need to submit the above materials via our online application system at https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ . BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, beneﬁts include comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement beneﬁts, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/beneﬁts/ SALARY In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is : Assistant Professor: AFT: Range 22-25 Associate Professor: AFT: Range 26-29 Full Professor: AFT: Range 30-33 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. Appropriate start-up packages may be available. Please visit this link to view all respective ranges listed above: https://www.cnjscl.org/Library/CNJSCL_FT-PT_2023-2027_Salary_Charts-Approved.pdf All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Umashanger Thayasivam, Head of Department of Mathematics, at (thayasivam@rowan.edu). A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to more than 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . Advertised: Sep 17 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501835/tenuretrack-faculty-position-in-organic-chemistry-department-of-chemistry-and-biochemistry": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Organic Chemistry, Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Organic Chemistry, Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry Apply now Job no: 501835 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Science and Mathematics Tenure-Track Faculty Position Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry College of Science and Mathematics Rowan University The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Rowan University is seeking to hire a 10 month Tenure-Track Professor (open rank) with an appointment to begin September 2027 . The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry is specifically interested in candidates who will develop a research program in the areas of synthetic organic chemistry, organic materials, or organometalics. Outstanding candidates with research programs outside of these areas may also be considered. A Ph.D. or equivalent in Chemistry or related field is required; postdoctoral experience is expected. Preference will be given to candidates with a track record and/or potential to establish and sustain a strong research program. We anticipate hiring at the Assistant Professor level, but outstanding candidates may be considered at the Associate or Full Professor levels. The successful candidates are expected to develop and maintain an active, highly visible, extramurally funded research program with outstanding scholarship, teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and contribute to the various service endeavors in the Department, College, and University. Opportunities for research collaboration exist within the Department, as well as with Departments of Biological and Biomedical Sciences, Physics and Astronomy, Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering, Cooper Medical School of Rowan University, Rowan Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine, Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine, and others. Faculty in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry have diverse expertise including drug synthesis and characterization, pharmacology, protein biochemistry, material synthesis and characterization. The department includes three active NSF Career awardees as well as faculty who are recipients of major research grants/awards from NIH (MIRA, R01), NSF, and several other private foundations/industries. The ideal candidates will provide complementary and synergistic expertise to our research efforts and develop an independent, externally funded research program in the broad discipline of their expertise. The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry is one of six departments in the College of Science & Mathematics, which is also home to the School of Earth & Environment. The department serves >450 graduate and undergraduate students in programs such as Ph.D. in Pharmaceutical Chemistry; M.S. in Pharmaceutical Sciences; B.S. in Chemistry (ACS Accredited); B.A. in Chemistry, B.S. in Biochemistry (ASBMB Accredited), several certificate programs and accelerated degree programs (4+1 B.S. & M.S., 3+4 B.S & M.D., 3+4 B.S. & D.O.) etc. The department also contributes to multiple degree programs on campus including MS and PhD in Material Sciences and Engineering, BS and MS in Bioinformatics, MS in Medical Lab Sciences, & BS in Molecular and Cellular Biosciences. Complete applications will include: Cover letter Current detailed CV Statement of research interests, including applicants' future research goals and plans for obtaining external funding to achieve those goals Statement of teaching philosophy Graduate transcripts (unofficial copies acceptable for initial review) Names and contact information for at least three references from whom the applicant has requested letters of support Review of applications will commence on October 15 and continue until suitable candidates have been identified. Applicants will need to submit the above materials via our online application system at https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ . BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ SALARY In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is: Assistant Professor: AFT: Range 22-25 Associate Professor: AFT: Range 26-29 Full Professor: AFT: Range 30-33 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. Appropriate start-up packages may be available. Please visit this link to view all respective ranges listed above: https://www.cnjscl.org/Library/CNJSCL_FT-PT_2023-2027_Salary_Charts-Approved.pdf Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Questions regarding the position should be directed to Dr. Subash Jonnalagadda, Department Head, (jonnalagadda@rowan.edu). About Rowan University A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to more than 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . Advertised: Sep 17 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501765/assistant-professor-medical-education-scholarship": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Medical Education & Scholarship",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Medical Education & Scholarship Apply now Job no: 501765 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine The Department of Medical Education and Scholarship at Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (SOM) is seeking a faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor to teach physiology and/or biochemistry content, facilitate in-person small groups of problem-based learning (PBL), and provide large group lectures. This position will cover faculty duties as assigned in the Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine, Physician Assistant program, and the School of Translational Biomedical Engineering and Sciences as their expertise allows. Expectations: The faculty member will be based at either the Stratford, NJ or Sewell, NJ campus, with some travel between campuses as needed. Facilitate weekly PBL small group sessions and/or large group lectures as needed. Be available to answer students’ questions in content areas of expertise. Complete mid-block (formative) and end-of-block (summative) student evaluations. Ensure all evaluations are executed using the specified template to maintain consistency and adherence to established guidelines. Contribute to case review, case-writing, case-enhancement, item writing for exams, faculty development, and medical education research. Faculty should be fully committed to learning how to facilitate problem-based learning, which includes participating in training for PBL and ongoing faculty development programs provided. You are not expected to be an expert in all content of the case. Ensure support for student learning through collaboration with the Center for Student Success (CSS) and/or Office of Faculty Development Know curriculum policies and procedures related to pre-clerkship delivery. Participate in academic committees as assigned. Whenever possible, vacations should be scheduled during the students’ time off in the winter, spring, and summer. When you have conferences or vacation, prior notification will be required so that a substitute can be provided for your group. Other duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department of Medical Education and Scholarship. Qualifications: Terminal degree (PhD, DO, or MD) with expertise in physiology and/or biochemistry. For physician applicants, clinical duties and/or teaching in the simulation center may be required. At least 3 years experience teaching medical students and small group facilitation, specifically PBL experience, is preferred. Salary: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is $104,00 to $124,000. Placement into the range is determined by the candidate’s qualifications, professional experience and other factors. Benefits : For eligible employees, benefits include comprehensive NJ state health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents attending Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTE: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the University will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. NOTE: This faculty appointment is Tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. NOTE: Faculty Rank of Assistant Professor is pending review and recommendation made by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Sep 11 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 13 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501798/associate-dean-campbell-library": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, Campbell Library",
      "description": "Associate Dean, Campbell Library Apply now Job no: 501798 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Managerial Associate Dean, Campbell Library The Associate Dean, Campbell Library, is the senior administrator responsible for the vision, leadership, and effective operation of Rowan University's main library in Glassboro. Reporting to the Chief Information Officer and Senior Vice Chancellor for Information Resources and Technology, the Associate Dean leads Campbell Library as an academic, cultural, research, student-success, and technology hub and ensures that its people, spaces, collections, services, and systems advance the University's mission. The Associate Dean is accountable for coordinating performance across Campbell Library's leadership and service portfolio, including Teaching & Learning, Access Services and Facilities Operations, Collection Services, Discovery Services, Library Technology Services, and related programs and administrative functions. The role leads through Campbell Library's leadership structure and establishes clear priorities, decision rights, service expectations, and accountability for results. Campbell Library’s technology, discovery, collection, licensing, and service functions support users across Rowan University. The Associate Dean is responsible for Campbell's delivery of those shared functions and works in close collaboration with libraries serving Cooper Medical School of Rowan University (CMSRU), Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (Rowan-Virtua SOM), and the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM). Strategic Leadership & System Integration Champion a clear, user-centered vision for Campbell Library grounded in student success, faculty teaching and research, access, and collaboration. Position Campbell Library as a cultural and technological center of the University by integrating its physical spaces, digital presence, collections, academic services, and partnerships. Represent Campbell Library in executive planning, accreditation, compliance, and institutional effectiveness activities, and advocate for the resources needed to fulfill its mission. Lead complex organizational, service, technology, and space transitions while maintaining continuity of critical operations. Lead strategic and annual planning, goal-setting, assessment, performance measurement, and resource planning aligned with University and IRT priorities. Build a culture of transparent communication, evidence-informed decision-making, shared purpose, professional standards, inclusion, accessibility, and accountability. Administrative & Organizational Oversight Provide strategic and operational oversight for Campbell Library's leadership and service portfolio, including Teaching & Learning, Access Services and Facilities Operations, Collection Services, Discovery Services, Library Technology Services, and other functions assigned to the position. Set priorities, decision parameters, service standards, and performance expectations; oversee evaluation, professional development, succession planning, and cross-training. Develop and maintain clear policies, procedures, workflows, documentation, governance practices, and service standards. Develop and administer operating and collection budgets, forecasts, procurement, contracts, licenses, renewals, and vendor performance. Use cost and use data, service metrics, and lifecycle information to guide investments, reductions, and resource allocation, and to ensure that contracted tools are implemented and delivering value. Collections, Discovery, & Archives Oversee Campbell-managed collection strategy, licensing, budget allocation, and assessment, using cost, use, and impact data to support sustainable and equitable decisions. Guide the lifecycle management of print and digital collections, including selection, access, rightsizing, weeding, storage, preservation, and transparent consultation with faculty and other stakeholders. Advance bibliographic and metadata integrity and effective discovery across Alma/Primo and related platforms, using relevant frameworks and standards. Collaborate with Archives & Special Collections to support responsible stewardship of Rowan's institutional memory, rare materials, and born-digital content. Ensure that Campbell-managed collection, discovery, and system services are delivered on a shared basis with input from the other Rowan library directors. Teaching, Learning, and Research Support Guide the evolution of research support, instruction, and information literacy initiatives, especially through the Teaching & Learning Team. Promote inclusive student-facing services and engagement, including outreach programs, digital learning objects, and liaison programs. Support integration of digital scholarship services and the growth of the Digital Scholarship Center and Center for Digital Humanities Research. Technology & Innovation Define and lead the strategic direction for Campbell Library technology and systems, ensuring that Library Technology Services advances the Library's goals and user experience. Align library systems and services with IRT architecture and operations, including affiliate access, EZproxy, OpenAthens, Primo, LibApps, metadata pipelines, and other shared platforms. Ensure that library technologies and digital services are reliable, accessible, secure, interoperable, and sustainable. Evaluate systems and tools based on user value, implementation readiness, interoperability, lifecycle requirements, and total cost, while promoting process documentation, cross-training, and continuous improvement. Advocacy & Representation Collaborate with the directors of the CMSRU, Rowan-Virtua SOM, and SSVM libraries to coordinate shared technology, discovery, licensing, collection strategy, standards, procurement, and institutional initiatives within the framework of each library's local governance and reporting structure. Establish or sponsor cross-library forums and working groups as appropriate to surface operational issues, coordinate changes, and improve shared services. Engage with regional and national consortia and external partners, including PALCI, VALE, LibraryLinkNJ, NJEdge, HathiTrust, DPLA, and other organizations as appropriate. Advance open access, open educational resources, diversity, equity, inclusion, accessibility, public scholarship, and related University priorities in partnership with academic and administrative stakeholders. Qualifications Required Master’s degree in Library and Information Science (ALA-accredited) or other related field, or equivalent experience. 7+ years of progressive leadership in academic or research libraries Demonstrated expertise in cross-campus service coordination and infrastructure leadership Proven record in strategic planning, budget oversight, and team development Deep knowledge of academic library operations across public services, collections, systems, and metadata Preferred Additional graduate degree in a related field (e.g., education, public administration, health sciences) Experience managing services in a multi-campus or health sciences academic environment Familiarity with national standards for archives, discovery, and bibliographic control (e.g., MARC, RDA, BIBFRAME, DACS) Key Competencies Strategic, analytical, and systems thinking Transparent, empathetic, and accountable leadership Organizational design, change leadership, and sound judgment Financial, operational, and contract stewardship Cross-functional team development and collaboration Clear communication, advocacy, and executive presence Initiative, adaptability, and the ability to translate strategy into operational execution Salary & Benefits In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $130,000 to $150,000 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10) For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted will be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Advertised: Sep 10 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501810/clinical-pathology-faculty-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Clinical Pathology Faculty - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Clinical Pathology Faculty - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501810 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Clinical Pathology Faculty - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Position: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Position Summary: The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University invites applications for a faculty position in Clinical Pathology. This is a full-time, 12-month academic position at the rank of Instructor, Assistant, Associate or Full Professor. Appointment may be in a tenure or clinical track depending on the qualifications and goals of the successful candidate. Candidates must possess a DVM or equivalent degree, be eligible for licensure in the State of New Jersey, and be ACVP or ESVCP board-certified or board-eligible in Clinical Pathology. The successful candidate will be a founding faculty member of the SSVM and play an integral role in the development and delivery of an integrated veterinary curriculum constructed around organ systems. Clinical service duties include diagnostic service conducted at the SSVM teaching hospital. This 50,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility located on the Glassboro Campus provides both primary and specialized care for companion, food and fiber animals throughout New Jersey and surrounding states. Creative scholarly activity is expected to advance the discipline of clinical pathology though the creation and dissemination of new knowledge, but the extent will depend on the candidate’s appointment and may include collaborative or independent research. Salary is commensurate with the applicant’s experience and qualifications. Rowan University offers a generous benefit package which can be viewed at https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ . Salary Range: In compliance with the State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $130,000 to $197,600. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. Benefits: For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Information about the institution: A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to 22,000 students through its main campus in Glassboro, N.J., its medical school campuses in Camden and Stratford, and five others. The University has earned national recognition for innovation, commitment to high-quality, affordable education, and developing public-private partnerships. A Carnegie-classified R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan has been recognized as the fourth fastest-growing public research university, as reported by The Chronicle of Higher Education. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on the Glassboro, New Jersey west campus, 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine plans to admit its first class of DVM students in 2025. Facilities will include an academic teaching facility aimed at the delivery of pre-clinical training, a small animal teaching hospital, and a research facility. Rowan University celebrates diversity and is committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. As a state public University, Rowan employees are eligible to participate in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service. Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Sep 8 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 7 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501811/associate-dean-for-academic-and-faculty-affairs-school-of-veterinary-medicine-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs, School of Veterinary Medicine, Rowan University",
      "description": "Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs, School of Veterinary Medicine, Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501811 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Sewell, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Associate Dean, Academic and Faculty Affairs, Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine, Rowan University (SSVM) Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, Sewell, New Jersey Categories: Managerial Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs The Rowan University School of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an administrative leader for the position of Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs. The selected candidate will lead the continued development of a fully integrated, pass/fail, spiral curriculum aligned with the competency based education framework while providing support for college graduate programs. The program is focused on early, robust exposure to clinical and professional skills and preparing students to confidently enter the workforce at graduation. The Associate Dean will assist in the recruitment, educational development and retention of talented faculty dedicated to preparing confident graduates. The selected candidate will play a critical role in participation in the School’s accreditation process and should have demonstrated expertise in outcomes assessment. The Associate Dean works closely with the Dean, other Associate/Assistant deans, Directors, Department Heads, central university administration, and human resources on a range of faculty affairs issues, including promotion and tenure, work-life balance policies, annual evaluations and merit, and compliance with the Faculty Handbook and other university requirements. Essential Role and Position Responsibilities: · Create mechanisms and programs for faculty educational development in partnership with the Department Heads and other related committees/groups at Rowan University · Coordinate faculty recommendations for new hires, merit programs and other recognition and reward programs to ensure equity and parity across scientific and clinical disciplines · Coordinate faculty leaves (including parental leaves, etc.) including retirement planning in coordination with the department chairs · Work in close partnership with the other Associate Deans, Department Chairs, and Directors to implement process improvements, planning and program decisions · Leads Committee on Curriculum, Committee on Appointments and Promotions. · Serves as contact person for related search committee policies and processes. · Lead and guide administrative team (especially Department Heads and Directors) on implementation of faculty driven curricular decisions · Serves as the Dean’s proxy to represent the SVM on academic matters, upon request. Qualifications for the position include: · DVM or equivalent degree (required) · MS or PhD in a related field (preferred) · Experience in higher education administration, academic program management, and faculty affairs · An established record of excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service appropriate for appointment to the rank of Full Professor with tenure · Interest in working in a dynamic budding veterinary program with the flexibility to adapt to new and innovative methods of delivery of veterinary education · Ability to mentor junior faculty, and collaborate with mid-career and senior faculty · Experience with promotion and tenure and faculty career progression · Evidence of interdisciplinary, collaborative leadership and partnerships with external agencies · Outstanding leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills · Experience with strategic planning and an understanding of faculty needs with a view toward enhancing pedagogy, growth and clinical collaboration · Experience in policy development and implementation · An understanding of the intersection of teaching, research, outreach, and patient care · Proven commitment to and knowledge of shared governance · Ability to lead teams, communicate with multiple and diverse audiences and individuals, and complete tasks in a complex organizational environment · Ability to inspire others to high levels of performance and foster collaboration and trust Salary Range: In compliance with the State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $170,000 to $260,000. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. Information about the institution: A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to 22,000 students through its main campus in Glassboro, N.J., its medical school campuses in Camden and Stratford, and five others. The University has earned national recognition for innovation, commitment to high-quality, affordable education, and developing public-private partnerships. A Carnegie-classified R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan has been recognized as the third fastest-growing public research university, as reported by The Chronicle of Higher Education. For more information on Rowan University, click here The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on the Glassboro, New Jersey west campus, 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine's first class of DVM students were admitted in September 2025. Facilities include a 167,000 square foot building that is shared as an academic teaching facility aimed at the delivery of pre-clinical training, a small animal teaching hospital, and a research facility. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. As a state public University, Rowan employees are eligible to participate in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service. Advertised: Sep 8 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 7 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501724/environmental-services-worker-parttime-stratford-andor-sewell-campus": {
      "title": "Environmental Services Worker, Part-Time (Stratford and/or Sewell Campus)",
      "description": "Environmental Services Worker, Part-Time (Stratford and/or Sewell Campus) Apply now Job no: 501724 Work type: Regular Part-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Facilities - Maintenance, Professional SUMMARY: The primary purpose of the Environmental Services Worker position is to perform various tasks to maintain a clean, safe, sanitary and attractive environment in the Rowan-Virtua SOM. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include the following. Other duties may be assigned. Performs proper cleaning to insure cleanliness of the assigned areas. Performs routine and general cleaning to prevent the spread of infection and keeps areas orderly and attractive. Performs isolation cleaning procedures as instructed in order to prohibit the spread of infection. Performs hard floor care and various levels of carpet care. Renders moving services throughout the University. Performs daily collection, storage and disposal of various waste generated within the University. Understands and adheres to Rowan-Virtua SOM’s compliance standards as they appear in Rowan-Virtua SOM's Corporate Compliance Policy, Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy. Exhibit good customer service skills by cultivating and maintaining report with customers. Performs functional set ups according to request. Performs various grounds cleaning tasks. Performs snow removal tasks. Operates University vehicles and vehicular equipment. Presents a clean uniform appearance. Performs final check and clean up at end of shift. Interacts with persons of all ages in a diverse, multicultural environment with respect and consideration. Complies with all applicable attendance policies and the Environmental Services Department in order to fulfill the responsibilities of the position. Performs job related duties effectively in team settings. Maintain valid driving license. Performs other related duties as assigned. JOB REQUIREMENTS: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed must be representative of the knowledge, skills, minimum education, training, licensure, experience, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Ability to read, write, speak, understand and communicate in English sufficiently to carry out the duties of the position; prior experience in institutional environmental services is preferred. Valid New Jersey driver’s license is required. Keep copies of the ADA Physical Demands and Work Environment Documentation Check Off Lists in your files. Position is considered to be Essential Personnel. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The person in this position must be physically active. Position requires climbing or balance, taste or smell less than 1/3 of the time; stand, stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl, talk or hear up to 2/3 of the time; walking 2/3 of the time; reaching with hands and arms over 2/3 of the time. Position requires lifting up to ten (10) pounds over 2/3 of the time, lifting or exerting force of 25 pounds up to 2/3 of the time, lifting or exerting force of fifty (50) or more pounds under 1/3 of the time. Position requires Close vision, Distance vision, Color vision and Depth Perception. Ability to hear pager alerts, overhead pager radio messages. WORK ENVIRONMENT: Up to 2/3 of the time, the position requires exposure to wet or humid conditions (non-weather), exposure to bloodborne pathogens that requires the use of Personal Protective Equipment, exposure to dust, fumes or airborne particles, and exposure to toxic or caustic chemicals that require the use of Personal Protective Equipment, exposure to outdoor weather conditions. Less than 1/3 of the time the position requires exposure to risk of electrical shock, exposure to risk of radiation, exposure to hazardous waste. The position requires work near moving mechanical parts up to 2/3 of the time, work in precarious places less than 1/3 of the time. The typical amounts of noise for the position are moderate to loud noise. WORK SHIFT: This position will be assigned one of several available shift assignments. Assigned shift and continued availability of same are subject to change to meet the operational needs of the department. In addition to regularly scheduled work shifts, the successful candidate must possess the ability to workdays, nights, weekends, holidays, and overtime hours when required. SALARY: The starting rate is $17.96 per hour ( Probationary Rate ). After completion of a six-month probationary period, the employee's pay will increase to the Job Rate of $18.59 . Depending on experience, candidate may be hired at the \"Job Rate\" to start. This position is Part-Time, 20 hours a week guaranteed. Opportunity for more hours per week may be available based on departmental need. Position location may be in Stratford or Sewell (will be informed during interview). Notes: Accrued vacation, sick, and float time available based on a 20 hour work week. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position(s) is filled. Only completed, online applications will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Sep 1 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 5 2026 05:00 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501786/anesthesiology-faculty-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Anesthesiology Faculty, Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Anesthesiology Faculty, Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501786 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Anesthesiology Faculty, Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Regular Full-Time, Regular Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine (SSVM) at Rowan University is seeking an experienced Veterinary Anesthesiologist to join our growing Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital. Full-time and part-time appointments will be considered , offering flexibility for candidates seeking a clinical, academic, or blended professional role. This is an exciting opportunity to join a thriving Anesthesiology Service within one of the nation's newest veterinary schools. The successful candidate will become part of an active specialty practice with a growing clinical caseload while contributing to the continued development of SSVM's clinical education mission. As a member of the Anesthesiology Service, you will provide advanced patient care, collaborate with a multidisciplinary team of specialists, and play an important role in educating future veterinarians while helping shape the culture and educational approach of a new veterinary program. Whether you are an experienced academic Anesthesiologist, a private specialty practitioner seeking a collaborative academic environment, or a clinician interested in a flexible faculty appointment, SSVM offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on patients, students, and the veterinary profession. Position Summary The successful candidate will provide comprehensive veterinary anesthesiology services within the SSVM Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital while contributing to clinical teaching, student mentorship, and continued service excellence. The Anesthesiology Service is actively seeing patients and has established clinical workflows, referral relationships, and hospital support systems. The successful candidate will join a functioning specialty service with the opportunity to contribute to continued growth, expanded clinical capabilities, and educational excellence. SSVM recognizes that exceptional faculty bring diverse career goals and practice models. We welcome applications from candidates interested in full-time or part-time appointments and are committed to working with successful applicants to develop schedules that support both institutional needs and individual professional interests. As the DVM program matures, this position will include increasing opportunities for structured clinical teaching and supervision, with anticipated student involvement throughout the clinical curriculum. Previous academic experience is welcome but not required. We are seeking a collaborative ophthalmologist with excellent clinical skills, strong communication abilities, and enthusiasm for mentoring the next generation of veterinarians. This role is ideal for veterinarians who: Thrive in a collaborative specialty practice Enjoy delivering advanced anesthesiology care Value teaching and mentorship Appreciate multidisciplinary patient management Enjoy building relationships with colleagues and referring veterinarians Are energized by innovation and contributing to a growing academic community Why Join SSVM? Faculty joining SSVM have a unique opportunity to: Become part of one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine Join an established Anesthesiology Service with a growing clinical caseload Practice advanced Anesthesiology in a modern Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Collaborate with board-certified specialists across multiple disciplines Contribute to the continued growth and evolution of specialty services Help develop innovative approaches to veterinary clinical education Teach and mentor veterinary students, interns, residents, and veterinary technology students Maintain an active clinical practice while participating in academic medicine Benefit from flexible appointment options, including consideration of part-time faculty appointments Join a collaborative, mission-driven culture committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research About the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University is one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine and is committed to advancing veterinary education, patient care, research, and community engagement. Since welcoming its inaugural DVM class in 2025 and second class in 2026, SSVM has experienced rapid growth and continues to expand its academic programs, clinical services, research enterprise, and faculty. Our Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Our state-of-the-art Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital provides advanced diagnostic and therapeutic capabilities and supports collaborative specialty and primary care. Current services include: Primary Care Urgent Care Ophthalmology Cardiology Neurology Dentistry & Oral Surgery Anesthesia & Pain Management Exotics Clinical Pathology Pharmacy Advanced Diagnostic Imaging, including a GE 3 Tesla MRI and 128-slice CT scanner The hospital is designed to support comprehensive multidisciplinary care, allowing ophthalmology patients to benefit from collaboration with specialists across multiple disciplines. Faculty joining SSVM have access to advanced diagnostic capabilities, specialty support, and a growing clinical environment designed to optimize patient care and educational opportunities. Anesthesia and Pain Management at SSVM The Anesthesia and Pain Management Service provides comprehensive perioperative care for companion animals and exotic patients while supporting SSVM’s mission to develop confident, practice-ready veterinarians. The service is designed to: Deliver individualized, evidence-based anesthetic and analgesic care Provide preanesthetic evaluation, anesthetic planning, advanced monitoring, and postanesthetic management Support acute and chronic pain management using multimodal approaches Collaborate closely with surgical, dental, diagnostic imaging, and other clinical services Promote patient safety through standardized protocols, quality improvement, and thoughtful case review Provide outstanding clinical learning experiences for students and trainees Advance clinical scholarship and innovation in veterinary anesthesia and analgesia The Anesthesia and Pain Management Service is supported by: Experienced veterinary technicians and clinical support staff Advanced anesthesia delivery and patient-monitoring equipment Multidisciplinary specialty consultation On-site pharmacy services Clinical pathology and advanced diagnostic imaging support A collaborative hospital team committed to patient safety and continuous improvement The successful candidate will have opportunities to contribute to continued clinical growth, educational programming, protocol development, and advancement of anesthesia and pain management within an innovative academic environment. Key Responsibilities Provide comprehensive anesthesia, analgesia, and perioperative care for patients across hospital services Perform preanesthetic evaluations, develop individualized anesthetic plans, and oversee advanced physiologic monitoring and recovery Provide consultation for acute and chronic pain management Support anesthetic care for routine, complex, and high-risk procedures Collaborate with primary care and specialty clinicians to provide integrated patient care Develop, implement, and evaluate anesthesia, analgesia, patient-safety, and perioperative protocols Participate in clinical teaching and mentorship of veterinary students, interns, residents, and veterinary technology students Contribute to anesthesia curriculum development, simulation, clinical skills instruction, and assessment Support the professional development and clinical training of veterinary technicians and other hospital colleagues Participate in quality improvement initiatives, morbidity and mortality review, and service development Engage in scholarly activity or clinical research consistent with individual interests Contribute positively to a collaborative and supportive hospital culture Required Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree Completion of a veterinary anesthesia and analgesia residency or comparable specialty training program Board certification or board eligibility through the American College of Veterinary Anesthesia and Analgesia (ACVAA) or equivalent Eligibility for veterinary licensure in New Jersey Demonstrated expertise in veterinary anesthesia, analgesia, and perioperative patient management Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate within a multidisciplinary specialty hospital Strong interest in clinical teaching and mentorship Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching, mentoring, or academic experience Experience managing complex or high-risk anesthesia cases Interest in anesthesia and analgesia education, simulation, or clinical skills instruction Interest in clinical research or scholarly activity Experience developing clinical protocols, patient-safety programs, or quality improvement initiatives Interest in advancing academic specialty practice within a collaborative environment Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $150,000–$200,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, appointment track, and appointment percentage. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits eligibility is based on appointment percentage and applicable University policies. Benefits may include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Both full-time and part-time appointments will be considered. Faculty rank, appointment track, responsibilities, and effort allocation will be determined at the time of appointment based on the successful candidate's qualifications, career interests, and the needs of the School. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and an outstanding quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note: Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Aug 27 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501790/psychiatry-nurse-practitioner-risn-rowanvirtua-som-sewell-nj": {
      "title": "Psychiatry Nurse Practitioner, RISN, Rowan-Virtua SOM (Sewell, NJ)",
      "description": "Psychiatry Nurse Practitioner, RISN, Rowan-Virtua SOM (Sewell, NJ) Apply now Job no: 501790 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Sewell, New Jersey Categories: Clinical, Professional Psychiatry Nurse Practitioner Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Location: Sewell, NJ Department: Regional Integrated Special Needs Center (RISN) Reports to: Director, RISN Summary: The Rowan-Virtua Regional Integrated Special Needs (RISN) Center is seeking a compassionate and collaborative Psychiatry Nurse Practitioner to join our multidisciplinary team dedicated to caring for individuals with complex intellectual, developmental, physical, and behavioral health needs. This unique opportunity combines direct patient care, interdisciplinary collaboration, teaching, and research within an innovative academic healthcare environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Provide compassionate accessible patient care, focused on quality and value-based care while developing models that will add to value-based care for the population. Provides longitudinal health relationships which allow patients with complex conditions and their families to thrive in their communities. Participates in a collegial relationship with physicians, psychologists, social workers, nurses and other health care professionals and prescribes or recommends drugs or other forms of treatment for the patient's psychiatric care. Provides consultation to clinical staff regarding patient care. Work with and present cases to a multidisciplinary team caring for patients with complex intellectual, physical, and developmental disabilities and their families. Participate in collaborative research with faculty, residents, and students. Teach medical students and residents in their clinical skills development in the office while seeing patients. Participates in a rotating on-call schedule and provides timely clinical response and follow-up in accordance with departmental policies and procedures. Maintains appropriate client records in a timely manner. Other tasks as assigned. Qualifications: Experience working with patients with intellectual and physical disabilities, complex medical needs, traumatic brain injury, or lifespan care preferred. Valid NJ nursing license. An advanced nursing degree with a concentration in psychiatric medicine. CDS license. DEA license. Salary: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is $107,965.64-$146,543.76. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as, but not limited to, scope of responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. Benefits : For eligible employees, benefits include comprehensive NJ state health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents attending Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTE: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US. The university will not sponsor an applicant's work visa for this position. Advertised: Aug 26 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 26 2026 03:45 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501726/small-animal-internist-fulltime-or-parttime-faculty-open-rank-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Small Animal Internist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Small Animal Internist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501726 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Small Animal Internist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Regular Full-Time of Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Position Summary The successful candidate will provide advanced internal medicine consultation and patient care while contributing to the continued development of a modern academic referral service. Initial responsibilities will focus on service development, caseload growth, collaboration with hospital services, and relationship-building with regional referring veterinarians. SSVM recognizes that exceptional faculty bring diverse career goals and practice models. We welcome applications from candidates interested in full-time or part-time appointments and are committed to working with successful applicants to develop schedules that support both institutional needs and individual professional interests. As our DVM program matures, this position will naturally evolve to include structured clinical teaching and supervision, with anticipated student participation beginning in approximately two years. Previous academic experience is welcome but not required. We are seeking collaborative clinicians with outstanding diagnostic skills, strong communication abilities, and enthusiasm for helping build an exceptional academic Internal Medicine Service. This role is ideal for veterinarians who: Thrive in collaborative specialty practice Enjoy solving complex diagnostic and medical challenges Value longitudinal patient care and spectrum-of-care decision-making Appreciate collaboration with primary care and specialty colleagues Enjoy teaching and mentoring future veterinarians Are energized by innovation, growth, and developing new programs Why Join SSVM? Faculty joining SSVM at this stage have a unique opportunity to: Help build one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine Develop a comprehensive Internal Medicine Service from the ground up Practice high-quality medicine in a modern Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Collaborate with board-certified specialists across multiple disciplines Influence clinical protocols, workflows, and service development Help create innovative models for clinical education Maintain an active referral medicine practice while preparing to teach future veterinarians Benefit from flexible appointment options, including consideration of part-time faculty appointments Join a collaborative, mission-driven culture committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research Small Animal Internal Medicine at SSVM The Small Animal Internal Medicine Service is central to SSVM's mission of delivering exceptional patient care while preparing graduates who are confident in managing complex medical cases through collaborative, evidence-based practice. Our service is designed to: Deliver advanced internal medicine consultation and care for companion animal patients Provide comprehensive diagnostic evaluation and longitudinal case management Collaborate closely with primary care, urgent care, and specialty clinicians Strengthen relationships with referring veterinarians throughout the region Provide students with outstanding educational experiences in internal medicine Advance clinical scholarship, research, and innovation The Internal Medicine Service is housed within the SSVM Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital and is supported by advanced diagnostic and therapeutic capabilities, including: GE 3 Tesla MRI 128-slice CT scanner Digital radiography Ultrasonography Endoscopy capabilities In-house clinical pathology On-site pharmacy with sterile compounding capabilities Multidisciplinary specialty consultation Faculty work closely with colleagues in Diagnostic Imaging, Surgery, Neurology, Cardiology, Ophthalmology, Dentistry & Oral Surgery, Primary Care, Urgent Care, Anesthesia & Pain Management, and expanding specialty services including Oncology and Dermatology. Faculty joining now will have meaningful opportunities to establish clinical standards, referral pathways, educational experiences, and service development that will define the Internal Medicine Service for years to come. Key Responsibilities Provide advanced internal medicine consultation and medical management for companion animal patients Perform comprehensive diagnostic evaluations and develop individualized treatment plans Collaborate with primary care and specialty clinicians to provide integrated patient care Build relationships with regional referring veterinarians Develop and refine clinical protocols, standard operating procedures, and workflow processes Participate in development of the internal medicine curriculum and pre-clinical educational experiences Prepare for future clinical teaching and mentorship of veterinary students Engage in scholarly activity and collaborative clinical research Contribute positively to a collaborative and supportive hospital culture Required Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree Board certification or board eligibility through the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM) or equivalent Eligibility for veterinary licensure in New Jersey Demonstrated expertise in companion animal internal medicine Strong communication skills and enthusiasm for collaboration with referring veterinarians and interdisciplinary teams Adaptability, initiative, and enthusiasm for helping build a growing academic Internal Medicine Service Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching, mentoring, or academic experience Interest in clinical education and curriculum development Interest in clinical research or scholarly activity Experience developing clinical protocols, workflows, or quality improvement initiatives Interest in advancing academic internal medicine within a collaborative referral environment Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $140,000–$250,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, appointment track, and appointment percentage. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits eligibility is based on appointment percentage and applicable University policies. Benefits may include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Benefits are administered in accordance with applicable collective bargaining agreements and University policies. For detailed benefits information, visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Both full-time and part-time appointments will be considered. Faculty rank, appointment track, responsibilities, and effort allocation will be determined at the time of appointment based on the successful candidate's qualifications, career interests, and the needs of the School. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and an outstanding quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note Position posting will remain active until the position is filled. Advertised: Aug 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501727/small-animal-surgeon-fulltime-or-parttime-faculty-open-rank-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university-fulltime-or-parttime": {
      "title": "Small Animal Surgeon (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) -  Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (Full-Time or Part-Time)",
      "description": "Small Animal Surgeon (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (Full-Time or Part-Time) Apply now Job no: 501727 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Small Animal Surgeon (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (Full-Time or Part-Time) Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Position Summary The successful candidate will provide advanced small animal surgical care while contributing to the continued development of a modern academic referral surgery service. Initial responsibilities will focus on clinical service development, caseload growth, hospital collaboration, and strengthening relationships with regional referring veterinarians. SSVM recognizes that exceptional faculty bring diverse career goals and practice models. We welcome applications from candidates interested in full-time or part-time appointments and are committed to working with successful applicants to develop schedules that support both institutional needs and individual professional interests. As our DVM program matures, this position will naturally evolve to include structured clinical teaching and supervision, with anticipated student participation beginning in approximately two years. Previous academic experience is welcome but not required. We are seeking collaborative surgeons with outstanding technical skills, excellent communication, and enthusiasm for helping build an exceptional academic surgery service. This role is ideal for surgeons who: Thrive in a collaborative specialty practice Enjoy complex soft tissue and orthopedic surgery Value clinical excellence and innovation Appreciate building relationships with referring veterinarians Enjoy teaching and mentoring future veterinarians Are energized by growth and developing a new academic referral service Why Join SSVM? Faculty joining SSVM at this stage have a unique opportunity to: Help build one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine Develop a comprehensive referral-based Small Animal Surgery Service from the ground up Practice in a modern Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital with state-of-the-art surgical and diagnostic capabilities Collaborate with board-certified specialists across multiple disciplines Influence surgical protocols, workflows, and service development Help create innovative models for surgical education Maintain an active referral surgical practice while preparing to teach future veterinarians Benefit from flexible appointment options, including consideration of part-time faculty appointments Join a collaborative, mission-driven culture committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research Small Animal Surgery at SSVM The Small Animal Surgery Service is central to SSVM's mission of providing exceptional specialty care while preparing graduates to confidently manage surgical patients within collaborative healthcare teams. Our service is designed to: Deliver exceptional referral-based surgical care Provide advanced soft tissue and orthopedic surgery Collaborate closely with Primary Care, Urgent Care, and specialty clinicians Strengthen partnerships with referring veterinarians throughout the region Provide students with outstanding educational experiences in surgery Advance clinical innovation, scholarship, and evidence-based surgical practice The Surgery Service is supported by a modern Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital featuring advanced diagnostic and surgical resources, including: Dedicated surgical suites Advanced anesthesia and pain management GE 3 Tesla MRI 128-slice CT scanner Digital radiography Ultrasonography Clinical pathology laboratory On-site pharmacy Comprehensive specialty consultation Faculty joining now will help establish surgical protocols, referral pathways, educational experiences, and service standards that will define the Surgery Service for years to come. Key Responsibilities Provide advanced soft tissue and orthopedic surgical care for companion animal patients Perform elective and emergency surgical procedures Collaborate with Primary Care, Urgent Care, and specialty clinicians to provide comprehensive patient care Build relationships with regional referring veterinarians Develop clinical protocols, quality improvement initiatives, and workflow processes Participate in development of the surgical curriculum and pre-clinical educational experiences Prepare for future clinical teaching and mentorship of veterinary students Engage in scholarly activity and collaborative clinical research Contribute positively to a collaborative and supportive hospital culture Required Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree Board certification or board eligibility through the American College of Veterinary Surgeons (ACVS) or equivalent Eligibility for veterinary licensure in New Jersey Demonstrated expertise in companion animal soft tissue and orthopedic surgery Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to collaborate within a multidisciplinary specialty hospital Adaptability, initiative, and enthusiasm for helping build a growing academic surgery service Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching, mentoring, or academic experience Interest in surgical education and curriculum development Interest in clinical research or scholarly activity Experience developing surgical protocols or quality improvement initiatives Interest in advancing academic referral surgery within a collaborative environment Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $150,000–$290,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, appointment track, and appointment percentage. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits eligibility is based on appointment percentage and applicable University policies. Benefits may include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Benefits are administered in accordance with applicable collective bargaining agreements and University policies. For detailed benefits information, visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Both full-time and part-time appointments will be considered. Faculty rank, appointment track, responsibilities, and effort allocation will be determined at the time of appointment based on the successful candidate's qualifications, career interests, and the needs of the School. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and an outstanding quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note Position posting will remain active until the position is filled. Advertised: Aug 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
