      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of History",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of History Apply now Job no: 501704 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Department of History in the Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities, and Social Sciences at Rowan University seeks to create a pool of adjunct faculty qualified to teach survey-level courses in Western Civilization, World History, and United States History. Some of these courses are offered online, but candidates who can teach in-person with morning to afternoon availability are preferred. Qualifications: M.A. or Ph.D. in History with field of expertise appropriate to the course; college-level teaching experience preferred. Procedure: Please include a letter of interest and CV in your online application. Please note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States, the University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Aug 5 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
