    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501725/veterinary-ophthalmologist-fulltime-or-parttime-faculty-open-rank-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Veterinary Ophthalmologist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Veterinary Ophthalmologist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501725 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Ophthalmologist (Full-Time or Part-Time Faculty, Open Rank) - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Position Summary The successful candidate will provide comprehensive veterinary ophthalmology services within the SSVM Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital while contributing to clinical teaching, student mentorship, and continued service excellence. The Ophthalmology Service is actively seeing patients and has established clinical workflows, referral relationships, and hospital support systems. The successful candidate will join a functioning specialty service with the opportunity to contribute to continued growth, expanded clinical capabilities, and educational excellence. SSVM recognizes that exceptional faculty bring diverse career goals and practice models. We welcome applications from candidates interested in full-time or part-time appointments and are committed to working with successful applicants to develop schedules that support both institutional needs and individual professional interests. As the DVM program matures, this position will include increasing opportunities for structured clinical teaching and supervision, with anticipated student involvement throughout the clinical curriculum. Previous academic experience is welcome but not required. We are seeking a collaborative ophthalmologist with excellent clinical skills, strong communication abilities, and enthusiasm for mentoring the next generation of veterinarians. This role is ideal for veterinarians who: Thrive in a collaborative specialty practice Enjoy delivering advanced ophthalmic care Value teaching and mentorship Appreciate multidisciplinary patient management Enjoy building relationships with colleagues and referring veterinarians Are energized by innovation and contributing to a growing academic community Why Join SSVM? Faculty joining SSVM have a unique opportunity to: Become part of one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine Join an established Ophthalmology Service with a growing clinical caseload Practice advanced ophthalmology in a modern Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Collaborate with board-certified specialists across multiple disciplines Contribute to the continued growth and evolution of specialty services Help develop innovative approaches to veterinary clinical education Teach and mentor veterinary students, interns, residents, and veterinary technology students Maintain an active clinical practice while participating in academic medicine Benefit from flexible appointment options, including consideration of part-time faculty appointments Join a collaborative, mission-driven culture committed to excellence in patient care, education, and research About the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University is one of the nation's newest colleges of veterinary medicine and is committed to advancing veterinary education, patient care, research, and community engagement. Since welcoming its inaugural DVM class in 2025 and second class in 2026, SSVM has experienced rapid growth and continues to expand its academic programs, clinical services, research enterprise, and faculty. Our Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital Our state-of-the-art Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital provides advanced diagnostic and therapeutic capabilities and supports collaborative specialty and primary care. Current services include: Primary Care Urgent Care Ophthalmology Cardiology Neurology Dentistry & Oral Surgery Anesthesia & Pain Management Exotics Clinical Pathology Pharmacy Advanced Diagnostic Imaging, including a GE 3 Tesla MRI and 128-slice CT scanner The hospital is designed to support comprehensive multidisciplinary care, allowing ophthalmology patients to benefit from collaboration with specialists across multiple disciplines. Faculty joining SSVM have access to advanced diagnostic capabilities, specialty support, and a growing clinical environment designed to optimize patient care and educational opportunities. Ophthalmology at SSVM The Ophthalmology Service provides advanced diagnostic and therapeutic care for companion animal patients while supporting SSVM's mission to develop confident, practice-ready veterinarians. The service is designed to: Deliver compassionate, evidence-based ophthalmic care Provide advanced diagnostic evaluation and treatment of ocular disease Collaborate closely with primary care and specialty clinicians Support referring veterinarians throughout the region Provide outstanding clinical learning experiences for students and trainees Advance clinical scholarship and innovation in veterinary ophthalmology The Ophthalmology Service is supported by: Dedicated ophthalmology equipment and clinical support Advanced diagnostic imaging capabilities Multidisciplinary specialty consultation Anesthesia and pain management support On-site pharmacy services Clinical pathology support The successful candidate will join an established service and have opportunities to contribute to continued clinical growth, educational programming, and advancement of ophthalmology within an innovative academic environment. Key Responsibilities Provide comprehensive ophthalmology consultation and treatment for companion animal patients Perform advanced ophthalmic diagnostics and procedures Collaborate with primary care and specialty clinicians to provide integrated patient care Support communication and relationships with referring veterinarians Participate in clinical teaching and mentorship of veterinary students, interns, residents, and veterinary technology students Contribute to ophthalmology curriculum development and clinical skills training Participate in quality improvement initiatives and service development Engage in scholarly activity or clinical research consistent with individual interests Contribute positively to a collaborative and supportive hospital culture Required Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) or equivalent degree Completion of an ophthalmology training program Board certification or board eligibility through the American College of Veterinary Ophthalmologists (ACVO) or equivalent Eligibility for veterinary licensure in New Jersey Demonstrated expertise in companion animal ophthalmology Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to collaborate within a multidisciplinary specialty hospital Strong interest in clinical teaching and mentorship Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching, mentoring, or academic experience Interest in veterinary ophthalmology education Interest in clinical research or scholarly activity Experience developing clinical protocols or quality improvement initiatives Interest in advancing academic specialty practice within a collaborative environment Salary and Benefits In accordance with the New Jersey Pay Transparency Act, the anticipated salary range for this position is $150,000–$200,000 annually , commensurate with qualifications, experience, clinical expertise, academic rank, appointment track, and appointment percentage. Final salary will be determined at the time of offer. Faculty at Rowan University are represented by the AAUP and receive a comprehensive benefits package in accordance with collective bargaining agreements and State of New Jersey benefit programs. Benefits eligibility is based on appointment percentage and applicable University policies. Benefits may include: Comprehensive medical, prescription, and dental insurance Participation in New Jersey retirement and pension plans Generous paid vacation, holidays, and leave benefits Professional development and continuing education support Tuition benefits for eligible employees and dependents Faculty governance participation and union representation Eligibility for the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program Academic Appointment This is an open-rank faculty appointment (Instructor through Full Professor) available on either the Clinical Track or Tenure Track , depending on qualifications, experience, and professional goals. Both full-time and part-time appointments will be considered. Faculty rank, appointment track, responsibilities, and effort allocation will be determined at the time of appointment based on the successful candidate's qualifications, career interests, and the needs of the School. Living in Southern New Jersey Located in Glassboro, New Jersey, SSVM offers convenient access to Philadelphia, New York City, Washington, D.C., and more than 130 miles of Atlantic coastline. The region offers affordable communities, excellent schools, abundant outdoor recreation, professional sports, wineries, beaches, hiking, and an outstanding quality of life for individuals and families. About Rowan University Rowan University is a Carnegie-classified R2 public research institution and one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities. Serving more than 23,000 students across multiple campuses, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, affordability, research excellence, and public-private partnerships. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan University's Glassboro campus. The School's 167,000-square-foot academic and clinical complex includes modern instructional space, a Veterinary Medical Teaching Hospital, and research facilities supporting education, discovery, and patient care. Equal Opportunity Employer All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability status, military status, genetic information, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity, affirmative action, and providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. As a public institution, Rowan employees may also be eligible to participate in the Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service . Employment Eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire. Rowan University will not sponsor applicants for employment-based visas for this position. Please Note: Position posting will be active until the job is filled. Advertised: Jul 31 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501712/adjunct-faculty-department-of-health-and-exercise-science": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Health and Exercise Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Health and Exercise Science Apply now Job no: 501712 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Nursing & Health Professions The Department of Health & Exercise Science at Rowan University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions. Courses may be face-to-face and/or online undergraduate and graduate level courses in Athletic Training, Exercise Science, Nutrition & Dietetics, and Public Health related areas. Programs within The Department of Health and Exercise Science can be found here: https://academics.rowan.edu/shp/departments/hes/programs/index.html Qualified candidates must have previous experience teaching in the above areas or experience related areas. Previous teaching experience at the college level is preferred. An MA or MS degree in a closely related field is required for undergraduate courses. A PhD or other terminal degree is required for any MA/MS course. The Department of Health and Exercise Science will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy occurs, the Department will consider the submitted applications to staff courses. Candidates must submit the following items: application curriculum vita three references graduate transcripts any other relevant material (including previous teaching and student evaluations) Positions are dependent on funding and current need; thus, applications will be screened on a rolling basis. Applications will be retained for future need if immediate openings are not available. Please contact Dylan Klein, PhD, Chair, Health & Exercise Science at 856-256-4785 or email at kleind@rowan.edu . Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 29 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501710/adjunct-faculty-department-of-geography-planning-sustainability": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Geography, Planning, & Sustainability",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Geography, Planning, & Sustainability Apply now Job no: 501710 Work type: Regular Part-Time, Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Science and Mathematics The Department of Geography, Planning, and Sustainability is seeking dedicated adjunct instructors in topics served by our degree programs, including the: * Bachelor of Science in Geographic Information Science * Bachelor of Science in Community and Environmental Planning * Bachelor of Arts in Environmental and Sustainability Studies * Bachelor of Arts in Geography * Master of Urban and Regional Planning A hallmark of the programs in our department is small class sizes that integrate disciplinary theory, practical skills and techniques, and career preparedness. Courses may be offered during daytime, evening, online, or mixed modalities, with consideration of curricular need and resource availability. Candidates for adjunct positions must hold a Master’s degree, with scholarly expertise or work experience in the proposed topics. Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Previous applications to positions in the Department of Geography, Planning, and Sustainability are eligible for consideration, and updates or inquiries may be sent to gps@rowan.edu Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 28 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501702/adjunct-faculty-eds-in-school-psychology-instructorinternship-supervisor-department-of-wellness-and-inclusive-services-in-education": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – EdS in School Psychology Instructor/Internship Supervisor, Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty – EdS in School Psychology Instructor/Internship Supervisor, Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education Apply now Job no: 501702 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Adjunct Faculty – EdS in School Psychology Instructor/Internship Supervisor Rowan University A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education operates within the College of Education and offers programs including the following: Master of Arts in Special Education and Inclusive Practices; Learning Disability Teacher Consultant (LDTC) Certification; multiple Certificates of Graduate Study (COGS); Bachelor of Arts in Inclusive Education; Teacher of Students with Disabilities (TOSD) Endorsement (post-bac and graduate programs); Counseling in Educational Settings; Master of Arts in School Psychology; Educational Specialist in School Psychology; and School Nursing. The College of Education is searching for a qualified and experienced school psychologist to supervise field experiences and/or teach professional courses within the EdS in School Psychology program. The successful candidate is expected to be familiar with the National Association of School Psychologists (NASP) professional standards including the comprehensive NASP practice model This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal. Qualifications: Required Graduate of a NASP accredited EdS in School Psychology program Holds an active NJ state and/or national certification as school psychologist Minimum of 3 years of experience in teaching graduate level courses in school psychology, including supervising school psychology interns Demonstrated excellence in teaching and service in education in the area of school psychology Demonstrated ability in communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills Demonstrated commitment to fostering academic achievement, social and personal responsibility, and social justice Demonstrated commitment to working in an environment devoted to collaboration, collegiality, professional development, diversity, scholarly inquiry, student learning, civic responsibility, and respect for all people Demonstrated commitment to working with P-12 schools A teaching/learning philosophy consistent with the mission of the College of Education Preferred PhD/PsyD in School Psychology Work experience as school psychologist in NJ public schools Start Date: Sept. 1, 2026 End Date: 6/30/27 Applications must be submitted through our online applicant tracking system: http://jobs.rowan.edu/cw/en-us/listing/ All applications should include: a letter of application with a statement of teaching interests and experience with supervising/mentoring school psychology interns curriculum vita graduate transcripts two letters of recommendation University values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. All positions are contingent upon need for clinical supervisors and/or course instructors in a given semester and budget appropriations. For more information, contact: Carmelo Callueng Ph.D. callueng@rowan.edu Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501703/emergency-and-critical-care-section-head-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Emergency and Critical Care Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Emergency and Critical Care Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501703 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Emergency and Critical Care Section Head - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type : Regular Full-Time Location : Glassboro, NJ Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Department of Clinical Sciences The Department of Clinical Sciences is seeking an experienced, collaborative, and forward-thinking veterinarian to serve as Section Head of Emergency and Critical Care . This leadership position provides an exciting opportunity to help shape and grow a developing academic veterinary medical center while maintaining an active role in clinical service, teaching, and mentorship. Position Summary The Emergency and Critical Care Section Head will provide leadership for the ECC service, fostering a culture of clinical excellence, teamwork, patient safety, and continuous improvement. The successful candidate will work closely with departmental and hospital leadership to advance clinical operations, support faculty and staff development, and ensure exceptional patient care and client service. This position is ideal for a candidate who enjoys building programs, mentoring colleagues, and developing innovative approaches to delivering emergency and critical care within a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment. Primary Responsibilities: Clinical Leadership Provide strategic and operational leadership for the Emergency and Critical Care service. Promote high-quality, evidence-based patient care and a culture of safety. Collaborate with hospital leadership to optimize service delivery, workflow, and resource utilization. Support quality improvement initiatives and participate in the development of standard operating procedures and clinical guidelines. Foster strong working relationships with specialty and primary care services. Faculty and Team Development Recruit, mentor, and support ECC faculty and clinical team members. Promote a positive, inclusive, and collaborative workplace culture. Assist with onboarding, performance development, and professional growth of faculty and staff. Encourage engagement, accountability, and shared ownership of service goals. Teaching and Mentorship Participate in clinical instruction of veterinary students, interns, and residents. Support the development of future veterinary professionals through mentorship and coaching. Contribute to educational initiatives and curriculum development as appropriate. Program Growth and Innovation Identify opportunities to expand and enhance ECC services. Collaborate with leadership on strategic planning and program development. Utilize data and performance metrics to guide decision-making and improve outcomes. Advance initiatives that improve patient care, client experience, and operational efficiency. Scholarship and Professional Engagement Engage in scholarly activities consistent with academic appointment expectations. Participate in professional organizations and contribute to the advancement of emergency and critical care medicine. Qualifications: Required DVM or equivalent veterinary degree. Board certification by the American College of Veterinary Emergency and Critical Care (DACVECC) or equivalent specialty certification. Eligibility for veterinary licensure in the state of New Jersey. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in clinical service, teaching, and teamwork. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Preferred Prior leadership, supervisory, or administrative experience. Experience in an academic veterinary medical center or specialty referral hospital. Track record of mentoring faculty, house officers, or clinical staff. Interest in program development and service growth. Salary Range: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $150,000 to $200,000 . Salary will be commensurate with experience, qualifications, scope of responsibilities, internal equity, and market considerations. Benefits Rowan University offers a comprehensive benefits package including: NJ State health, dental, and retirement benefits Generous accrued time off and paid holidays Tuition reimbursement for employees and eligible family members Eligibility for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program For detailed benefits information, visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ About Rowan University & SSVM Rowan University is a top 100 national public research institution serving over 22,000 students across multiple campuses. Classified as an R2 (high research activity) institution, Rowan is nationally recognized for innovation, access, and public-private partnerships. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on Rowan’s west campus in Glassboro, NJ—approximately 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. SSVM is developing comprehensive academic, clinical, and research facilities to support its innovative veterinary education model. Rowan University values diversity and inclusion and is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to protected characteristics. Advertised: Jul 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501678/adjunct-faculty-department-of-art": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Art",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Art Apply now Job no: 501678 Work type: Temporary Full-Time, Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of the Arts Adjunct Faculty – Rowan University The Department of Art at Rowan University is seeking qualified adjuncts to teach undergraduate courses in Studio Art, Drawing, Painting, 2 and 3-d Design, Graphic Design and Digital Media, Ceramics, Sculpture, Jewelry/Metals, and Art History. The position will be based on the main campus in Glassboro, New Jersey. Qualifications: Master’s degree in a related field Relevant professional or academic experience Track record of successful teaching is desirable Application Instructions: Submit application materials through the Rowan employment application website. Materials must be submitted online. Required Materials (in a single PDF file if possible): Cover letter Resume Names of three references and/or letters of recommendation 2 previous teaching evaluations, if available All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501693/adjunct-faculty-inperson-and-online-bs-in-healthcare-management-and-administration-and-ms-in-healthcare-management-hcm": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty (In-person and Online), BS in Healthcare Management and Administration and MS in Healthcare Management (HCM)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty (In-person and Online), BS in Healthcare Management and Administration and MS in Healthcare Management (HCM) Apply now Job no: 501693 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - University College/School of Professional Studies Adjunct Faculty (In-person and Online) For Programs: BS in Healthcare Management and Administration and MS in Healthcare Management (HCM) Positions Position Description: Rowan University is seeking skilled adjunct faculty to join our team to deliver both in-person and online courses for the BS in Healthcare Management and Administration (BS in HCM) (in-person and online modes of delivery) and the MS in Healthcare Management programs (MS in HCM) (fully online). These roles provide a unique opportunity to engage students across various formats, enhancing their educational journey with dynamic and engaging content. Both programs will accept applications year-round to maintain an ongoing pool of candidates. Faculty for both modes of delivery in the BS in HCM program will support first-year students, transfer students, and 3+1 students. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff courses such as: Introduction to Healthcare Management, Healthcare Informatics, Healthcare Marketing, Healthcare Law and Ethics, Research Methods, Healthcare Delivery and Quality, Healthcare Finance and Decision Making, Strategic Management in Health Care, Healthcare Operations Management, Healthcare Organization Leadership, AI in Healthcare Management, Risk Management in Healthcare, and related courses. In-Person Faculty: Our in-person faculty will have the opportunity to deliver lectures, facilitate discussions, and provide hands-on guidance, creating an inspiring and interactive learning environment that complements our online offerings. You'll be instrumental in students' growth by bringing healthcare management concepts to life through dynamic in-class interactions. Online Faculty: As an online faculty member teaching asynchronously, you will play an essential role in offering a rich online learning experience. You will work closely with the School of Professional Studies, as well as the Rowan Online Advising and Operations teams, ensuring a successful learning experience for our students. Qualifications: Candidates must possess at least a Master’s Degree in Healthcare Management, Business Management, or a related Public Health Management degree, as well as clinical experience. Strong skills in the areas of critical thinking, emotional intelligence, leadership, diversity, and inclusion. Strong communication skills, ensuring that course objectives, expectations, and feedback are clearly provided to support student success. Preference for applicants with teaching experience at the collegiate level. A doctoral-level degree in a relevant field, such as healthcare administration or management, is preferred for the MS in HCM program. Additional for online faculty Strong technical skills, including proficiency with a learning management system (LMS), video conferencing platforms, and collaboration tools. A strong record of excellence in asynchronous instruction and facilitating digital learning environments. Familiarity with Canvas LMS is preferred. Expectations: Comply with mandated policies and regulations; adhere to all university-wide policies. Engage actively with students, offering timely support, expert knowledge, and virtual office hours where applicable. Recognize and accommodate diverse learning needs, including offering flexible evening and weekend availability. Participate in retention initiatives and assist students with academic, attendance, and behavioral matters. Provide timely feedback and guidance on course assignments, assessments, and grades. Submit final grades within five business days as per university policy. Exhibit a positive, accepting learning environment, supporting a diverse group of students. Maintain current knowledge in your field and complete all necessary training, orientation, and administrative tasks. REQUIRED Documents: Current and complete curriculum vitae or resume Cover letter detailing courses of interest, previous teaching experience, availability, and references. Teaching philosophy statement (1-2 pages long) Unofficial transcripts for all listed degrees. Please note that successful candidates will be asked to submit official transcripts. Optional Documents: Professional license(s) for all listed. Syllabus sample Previous course evaluations Note: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Candidates must reside in the US. Salary and Benefits: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 (after 9/1/2026) per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501691/adjunct-faculty-special-education-instructors-supervisors-of-field-experiences": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Special Education Instructors - Supervisors of Field Experiences",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Special Education Instructors - Supervisors of Field Experiences Apply now Job no: 501691 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Adjunct Faculty - Special Education Instructors - Supervisors of Field Experiences Rowan University A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . The Department of Wellness and Inclusive Services in Education operates within the College of Education and offers programs including the following: Master of Arts in Special Education and Inclusive Practices; Learning Disability Teacher Consultant (LDTC) Certification; multiple Certificates of Graduate Study (COGS); Bachelor of Arts in Inclusive Education; Teacher of Students with Disabilities (TOSD) Endorsement (post-bac and graduate programs); Counseling in Educational Settings; Master of Arts in School Psychology; Educational Specialist in School Psychology; and School Nursing. The College of Education is searching for qualified and experienced special education/inclusive education specialists to supervise field experiences and/or teach in person or online classes at the undergraduate and graduate level. The successful candidate will demonstrate familiarity with the accreditation standards of national associations in special education, such as the Council for Exceptional Children. This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal. The position requires availability during the regular school day. Qualifications: Required Master's degree in special education or closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education in a field directly or closely associated with special education at the time of appointment Meets state licensure requirements for special education A minimum of 3 years of public or private successful teaching (pre-K-12 th grade) Demonstrated excellence in teaching and service in education in the area of special education Demonstrated ability in communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills Demonstrated commitment to fostering academic achievement, social and personal responsibility, and social justice Demonstrated commitment to working in an environment devoted to collaboration, collegiality, professional development, diversity, scholarly inquiry, student learning, civic responsibility, and respect for all people Demonstrated commitment to working with pre-K-12 schools Familiarity with current teacher accountability requirements, research, and best practices in special education A teaching/learning philosophy consistent with the mission of the College of Education Preferred Experience with supervision Experience with teaching in higher education settings Starting Date: 9/1/26 Ending Date: 6/30/27 Applications must be submitted through our online applicant tracking system: http://jobs.rowan.edu/cw/en-us/listing/ All applications should include: a letter of application with a statement of teaching interests, experience with supervising/ mentoring other teachers curriculum vita graduate transcripts two letters of recommendation University values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. All positions are contingent upon need for clinical supervisors and/or course instructors in a given semester and budget appropriations. For more information, contact: Nicole Edwards, PhD edwardsn@rowan.edu Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
