    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501680/adjunct-faculty-philosophy-department-of-philosophy-and-world-religions": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Philosophy - Department of Philosophy and World Religions",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Philosophy - Department of Philosophy and World Religions Apply now Job no: 501680 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Department of Philosophy and World Religions seeks qualified adjunct faculty for various philosophy classes, including: Logic of Everyday Reasoning (informal logic), Philosophical Perspectives on Science (a general education philosophy of science course for non-majors), Intro to Philosophy, Intro to Ethics, Social & Political Philosophy, and Intro to Symbolic Logic. Some of these courses are offered online, but candidates who can teach in person are preferred. Please see the department website – https://www.rowan.edu/ric-edelman-college/departments/phwr/ – for information on our majors and other programs. Qualifications: Candidates must have at least a Master’s degree in philosophy (or a closely related field). Previous college-level teaching experience is strongly preferred. Applications submitted through this process will be screened on a rolling basis, as the need for new instructors arises. Applications will be retained for possible future semesters of employment. Required application materials: * cover letter * curriculum vitae * evidence of teaching effectiveness * graduate transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable) Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 20 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 3