    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501562/nurse-practitioner-endocrinology-department-of-medicine-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner, Endocrinology, Department of Medicine, Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "Nurse Practitioner, Endocrinology, Department of Medicine, Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501562 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a dynamic full-time Nurse Practitioner to join our growing Endocrinology Team. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to be part of our collaborative, patient-centered Endocrine practice dedicated to providing comprehensive outpatient care. As a Nurse Practitioner, you will work alongside an experienced Endocrinologist and multidisciplinary care teams while managing a diverse patient population with complex endocrine and metabolic conditions. * Adrenal disorders, including Addison's disease * Hormone replacement therapy * Low testosterone (Low-T) * Metabolic syndrome, including Hypertension, Hypothyroidism, Diabetes, Hyperlipidemia, Sleep apnea, Central obesity * Osteoporosis * Parathyroid disorders * Pituitary disorders, including tumors and hypopituitarism In support of Rowan Medicine's mission and vision, the selected candidate will provide and manage comprehensive care at our Stratford and Sewell, New Jersey locations. The candidate must hold the following Qualifications: * Graduate of an accredited Nurse Practitioner Program * Valid New Jersey Licensure * CDS and DEA for New Jersey * Endocrinology experience preferred: motivated new graduates may be considered Our clinical campus is located in Southern New Jersey, which is within the Philadelphia metropolitan area approximately eight miles from Center City Philadelphia, one hour from the Jersey Shore, an hour and a half from NYC, and two hours from Washington, DC. Rowan University and the School of Osteopathic Medicine promote a diverse community that begins with students, faculty, staff and administration who respect each other and value each other's dignity. By identifying and removing barriers and fostering individual potential. Rowan will cultivate a community where all members can learn and grow. SALARY: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000 to $135,000. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. BENEFIT INFORMATION: For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTE: Only completed, online applications submitted on or before the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the University will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Jul 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501674/adjunct-faculty-department-of-electrical-and-computer-engineering": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Apply now Job no: 501674 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering Adjunct Faculty Positions in All Areas of Electrical and/or Computer Engineering If you have prior academic or industrial experience, a passion for hands-on, project-based teaching, and would like to share your knowledge and wisdom with an enthusiastic group of students and indeed shape the next generation of our nation’s workforce, we want you in our classrooms and laboratories . The Electrical and Computer Engineering Department ( www.rowan.edu/ece ) at Rowan University is growing, with the brand-new B.S. in Electrical Engineering Technology and M.S. in Systems Engineering programs added to our flagship B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. programs in Electrical and Computer Engineering. To support this robust growth, we seek energetic and innovative teacher-scholars as Adjunct Professors who are interested in sharing their knowledge and wisdom with our students and share our commitment to excellence in engineering education. Our Adjunct Professors, who are typically active or retired academic or industry professionals, are an important part of the fabric of the Rowan ECE community, bringing their unique experiences and perspectives to our department. The successful candidates will be responsible for teaching innovative, project-based courses primarily in the electrical and computer engineering and electrical engineering technology programs. These courses may be core or elective, depending on the applicant’s area of expertise. We welcome qualified and dedicated individuals with a background in all areas of ECE, including but not limited to: Core topics Digital and embedded systems, Computer architecture, Circuits, electronics, power electronics, Programmable logic controllers, automation design VLSI design, chip design, advanced chip manufacturing, solid-state systems Control systems, Signal and image processing, Communication systems, including traditional, modern, and industrial communication systems Electromagnetics and modern antenna systems Electives RF /microwave systems Systems engineering Power systems, renewable and alternative energy systems, and modern battery systems Robotics Machine learning / artificial intelligence Cybersecurity, cyber-physical systems Project management Reliability and quality engineering Your favorite emerging topic in any area that relates to ECE, EET, or Systems Engineering As a department, we greatly value experiential and project-based learning, integrating emerging topics and technologies into the curriculum, and providing an outstanding, state-of-the-art array of equipment, instruments, rapid prototyping, fabrication and computational resources to support such activities. Our dedication to project-based learning is reflected in both of our ECE and EET curricula, as all our courses include lab/project components. As a result, we seek individuals who share this dedication, possess the skills and passion to develop innovative hands-on lab projects or other experiential learning activities using appropriate modern tools, and have the ability to integrate such projects/activities into the course content. Applicants must have earned at least a Master of Science degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or a related discipline. Individuals with industry and/or academic experience are particularly encouraged to apply. 10 years or more of relevant industry experience, along with a Bachelor's degree, may, in some cases, be used in lieu of the Master of Science degree requirement. Effective communication skills, the capacity to collaborate with multi-disciplinary student and faculty teams, and the capability to teach in a project-based environment are essential. The position is part-time, non-tenure-track, with renewable contracts contingent upon performance (including student evaluations), departmental needs, and university and budgetary approvals. The review of applications will commence immediately and continue as new needs arise. For full consideration, applications should include the following items: A cover letter summarizing qualifications and the applicant’s interest in the position Current and detailed CV Statement of teaching interests, including the list of courses the applicant feels most qualified to teach, and teaching philosophy. Names and contact information for two professional references (an optional personal reference may also be added) Unofficial transcripts. Please note that successful candidates will be asked to submit official transcripts. Therefore, submitting an official transcript at the time of application, if available, will expedite the hiring process. Transcripts issued to the applicant are acceptable. Optionally, additional relevant documentation (such as student evaluations from former teaching engagements, examples of innovative curricular components developed by the applicant, examples of industrial design experience that may be leveraged in class, etc.) may be submitted in an Appendix as a separate file. The application must be submitted through our online application system. https://go.rowan.edu/adjunct4RowanECE Questions can be directed to polikar@rowan.edu , Dr. Robi Polikar, Department Head, Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering. Additional departmental information can be found at http://www.rowan.edu/ece All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 15 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501675/adjunct-faculty-inperson-department-of-psychology": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty (In-Person) - Department of Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty (In-Person) - Department of Psychology Apply now Job no: 501675 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Science and Mathematics Rowan University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Psychology for undergraduate and graduate courses. We have a strong preference and need for faculty who can teach classes in person, although applicants may be invited to teach either in person or online as needs arise. If you are only interested in and available for teaching online, please see our ad recruiting for online instructors for additional application details. We offer courses on our main campus in Glassboro and also on campuses in Camden, Burlington and Gloucester Counties. Most classes run Monday through Friday throughout the day into the evening, depending on the program. Please indicate your preferred campus(es) and general availability for in person teaching in your cover letter. The applicants must be committed to excellence in the teaching of psychology. The Psychology Department offers a range of graduate and undergraduate programs including a BA in Psychology (with online and in-person degree opportunities), a BS in Psychological Science, and a minor in Psychology. The Psychology Department also offers MA degrees in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, School Psychology and Applied Behavior Analysis, a Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology, and is launching a graduate program in Human Factors. In addition to these, we offer several certificate programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. You can find a full list of our current programs on our website . Interested individuals must have at least a master’s degree. The Psychology Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. The application must be submitted via our online career site – jobs.rowan.edu . To access our online application system PageUp, please visit jobs.rowan.edu . Click on the position for which you would like to apply, then click the “Apply Now” button. Required Documents: A current and complete curriculum vitae Graduate transcripts A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the following information: the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching and qualified to teach; your preferred campus(es) and general availability for teaching; detailed information about previous teaching experience and qualifications in teaching college courses, and the names and the contact information of three references in case additional information is required. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents (e.g., previous student evaluations or colleague observations), they may submit them online in conjunction with the application but these are not Note: Only completed, online applications submitted on or before the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 15 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501660/adjunct-faculty-developmental-reading-department-of-critical-literacies-technology-and-multilingual-education-cltm-college-of-education": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Developmental Reading - Department of Critical Literacies, Technology, and Multilingual Education (CLTM) College of Education",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Developmental Reading - Department of Critical Literacies, Technology, and Multilingual Education (CLTM) College of Education Apply now Job no: 501660 Work type: Regular Part-Time, Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education Adjunct Faculty, Developmental Reading - Department of Critical Literacies, Technology, and Multilingual Education (CLTM) College of Education Work type: Temporary, Part Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Education This is a part-time, adjunct position with the possibility of renewal on a term-by-term basis. We are particularly interested in candidates who can teach courses in our reading/literacy programs. We offer two developmental reading courses for Rowan students depending on their Accuplacer score, Improving Personal Reading Skills and Critical Thinking and Reading of Academic Texts . Both courses focus on comprehension strategies, vocabulary development, study skills, and decision making across a broad spectrum of academic majors. Qualifications: Required Master’s degree or higher in literacy or reading A minimum of 3 years of successful teaching in P-12 settings or working with adult literacy Demonstrated commitment to fostering academic achievement, social and personal responsibility, and social justice Demonstrated commitment to working in an environment devoted to collaboration, collegiality, professional development, diversity, scholarly inquiry, student learning, civic responsibility, and respect for all people A teaching/learning philosophy consistent with the mission of the College of Education Starting Date: Open, Continuous Contact: Questions regarding this position can be directed to Bob Eisberg eisberg@rowan.edu . Procedure: The application must be submitted through our online applicant tracking system: https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ All applications should include: A letter of application with a statement of teaching interests, experience with supervising/ mentoring other teachers Curriculum vita Graduate transcripts Three letters of recommendation (at least one of which speaks to teaching ability) All positions are contingent upon need for instructors in a given semester and budget appropriations. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 10 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
