    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501666/omm-lab-instructor-per-diem-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "OMM Lab Instructor- Per Diem, Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "OMM Lab Instructor- Per Diem, Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501666 Work type: Per Diem Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a Per Diem Instructor who would be available to teach in OMM/SGL 1 & 2 or OMM/PBL 1 & 2 labs with the Department of OMM within the NMI. They will be responsible for the first and second year medical students as they rotate through the OMM lab under the direction of the Course Director(s). Rowan University and the School of Osteopathic Medicine is a community that begins with students, faculty, staff and administration who respect each other and value each other’s dignity. The Rowan University community is committed to a safe environment that encourages intellectual, academic, and social interaction and engagement. The candidate must hold a D.O. and have experience practicing osteopathic manipulative medicine. Our clinical campuses are in Southern New Jersey, which is within the Philadelphia metropolitan area, one hour from the Jersey Shore, an hour and a half from NYC, and two hours from Washington, DC. This is an hourly paid position and total hours per week will be under 19 hours based on academic need. In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the hourly rate for this position is $75/hr. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as, but not limited to, scope of responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. This is a non-benefit eligible position. NOTE: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US. The university will not sponsor an applicant's work visa for this position. Advertised: Jul 10 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 13 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501656/adjunct-faculty-department-of-computer-science": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Computer Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Computer Science Apply now Job no: 501656 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of Science and Mathematics The Computer Science Department invites applications for adjunct faculty positions. As one of six departments in the College of Science & Mathematics, the department offers both undergraduate and graduate programs in Computer Science, Data Science, Computing & Informatics, Computer Systems Technology, and Cybersecurity. It is among the largest departments on campus and delivers courses in both in-person and online formats. Applicants must hold a master’s degree in computer science or a closely related technical field. Preferred qualifications include prior teaching experience, relevant industry experience, and/or professional certification or licensure. Application materials should include: A cover letter outlining teaching experience, qualifications, educational background, and areas of teaching interest A current resume Graduate transcripts (unofficial copies are acceptable for initial review) A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here . Please be aware that this is an instructor pool position. Your completed application will enable hiring officials to contact you at some point in the future if and when the need arises for future semesters. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 9 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501615/adjunct-faculty-diversity-and-inclusion-masters-degree-program-center-of-interdisciplinary-studies": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Diversity and Inclusion Master's Degree Program, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Diversity and Inclusion Master's Degree Program, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies Apply now Job no: 501615 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Diversity and Inclusion Master’s Degree program at Rowan University seeks qualified adjunct faculty to teach a graduate capstone seminar for students completing the master’s degree program. This course provides an integrative and practical learning experience where faculty will serve as a mentor and guide for students to complete an original and impactful community project that reflects and upholds the principles of diversity, equity, and inclusion. Please see the program website for more information about the Diversity and Inclusion Master’s Program at Rowan University: https://www.rowan.edu/ric-edelman-college/centers/inter_majors/graduate_programs/cogs_hge/ma-cogs-hge.html Qualifications: Master’s degree in social science or related field with practical experience in applied qualitative research. The candidate will preferably have at least two years of experience with the design, analysis, and presentation of participatory research projects that integrate the voices and positions of diverse stakeholders as well as experience in the use of qualitative research in a variety of organizational structures. Procedure: Please include a letter of interest, a CV, and an unofficial transcript of the highest degree in your online application. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 9 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
