    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501637/adjunct-faculty-disaster-preparedness-and-emergency-management": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Management Apply now Job no: 501637 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Program in Disaster Science, Emergency Management & Homeland Security within the Department of Sociology & Anthropology in the Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences at Rowan University seeks applicants for a talent pool of candidates for adjunct instructors to fill adjunct teaching positions as they become available , with a minimum of one course with a maximum of two courses per semester. Typical undergraduate courses will include: Introduction to Emergency Management & Homeland Security, Research Methods, Borders and Ports of Entry, Homeland Security, Critical Infrastructure, Incident Command, and upper-division courses. Sample graduate courses include: All-Hazards Threat Response Management, Cybersecurity, Cyber Defense, Advanced Exercise Design, and Public Budgeting and Finance in Emergency Management. Candidates must have earned a master’s degree or beyond, from a regionally accredited university, in emergency management, public administration, public health, management, or related field deemed necessary to meet the program’s needs. Experience in the field is desirable. A terminal degree is expected for graduate-level teaching. All applications must be submitted through our online application system for consideration for any current or future online or in-person adjunct instructor positions. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College/School & Department on an as-needed basis. Note: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered Advertised: Jul 6 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501636/adjunct-faculty-department-of-social-work": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Social Work",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Social Work Apply now Job no: 501636 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Social Work Department in the Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities and Social Sciences at Rowan University is seeking applicants qualified to teach Bachelor's level and Master's level generalist courses (e.g., practice, policy, research and clinical/ mental health courses) as well as courses related to our specialization in Mental Health, Equity, and Well-being. Depending upon scheduling needs, adjunct faculty may teach up to two courses per semester. Current needs for Fall '26 are: -BSW Introduction to Social Work on Tuesdays and Thursdays 11am-12:15pm -MSW Research Methods with sections at 3:30pm-4:45pm, 5pm-6:15pm, and 6:30pm-7:45pm. Qualifications: MSW and two years of practice experience required. DSW/ PhD in Social Work or related discipline and college-level-teaching experience preferred. All applications must be submitted through our online application system. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501634/clinical-adjunct-facultydepartment-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Clinical Adjunct Faculty-Department of Nursing",
      "description": "Clinical Adjunct Faculty-Department of Nursing Apply now Job no: 501634 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Nursing & Health Professions Clinical Adjunct Faculty – Nurse Practitioner Programs Position Summary The Department of Nursing at the Salva School of Nursing & Health Professions seeks qualified Clinical Adjunct Faculty to support Graduate Nurse Practitioner (NP) programs and Undergraduate Community Health Clinical through clinical instruction, student mentorship, and assessment of advanced practice nursing and undergraduate nursing competencies. Clinical adjunct faculty are educators who provide oversight of students during clinical rotations, facilitate the integration of didactic and clinical learning, and contribute to the preparation of future baccalaureate and advanced practice registered nurses. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in nursing education, evidence-based practice, and the development of professional competencies required for advanced nursing practice and national certification. Essential Responsibilities Oversee Nurse Practitioner/Community Health students in approved clinical practice settings. Facilitate student learning through clinical teaching, coaching, and mentoring. Evaluate student clinical performance and provide timely, constructive feedback. Complete clinical evaluation documentation and competency assessments. Conduct site visits and maintain communication with clinical preceptors and agencies as required. Support students in achieving program outcomes and specialty-specific competencies. Grade clinical assignments and other course-related activities as assigned. Participate in course meetings and faculty development activities as appropriate. Utilize university learning management systems and other educational technologies to support instruction. Promote professional standards, ethical practice, patient safety, and evidence-based care. Required Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution. Active, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license. Graduate Faculty Qualifications Active, unencumbered Advanced Practice Nurse (APN)license in New Jersey and the state of practice for Graduate Nursing Programs. National board certification in the specialty area being taught (e.g. AGACNP, FNP, PMHNP) for Graduate Nursing Programs. Minimum of three years of recent advanced practice clinical experience Demonstrated expertise in the applicable nurse practitioner specialty. Eligibility to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) or PhD in Nursing or a related field. Previous clinical teaching or precepting experience in undergraduate or graduate nursing education. Experience with online teaching platforms and learning management systems. Strong communication, leadership, and mentoring skills. About Rowan University Rowan University is a nationally recognized public research institution serving more than 25,000 students across multiple campuses. As one of the nation's fastest-growing public research universities, Rowan is committed to excellence in education, research, innovation, and community engagement. The Virtua Health School of Nursing & Health Professions prepares future nurses and advanced practice providers through high-quality, student-centered educational programs. Application Process Applicants should submit: Current curriculum vitae (CV). Cover letter describing: Areas of teaching interest and specialty expertise. Previous teaching and clinical experience. Availability for instruction. Contact information for three professional references. Nursing licensure and certification information. Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire). Applications will be reviewed as clinical teaching needs arise. Positions are contingent upon budget approval and program needs. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501617/adjunct-faculty-american-studies-center-of-interdisciplinary-studies": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, American Studies, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, American Studies, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies Apply now Job no: 501617 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The program in American Studies is seeking adjuncts to teach Introduction to American Studies, and other courses in the American Studies program as necessary. This course introduces students to the interdisciplinary practice of American Studies in an engaging way, with special emphasis on the application of American cultural studies to a variety of future careers. Other courses include Interdisciplinary Research and Writing, American Studies in the Classroom, and Senior Seminar. A successful candidate must have an appropriate graduate degree and experience teaching in American Studies or a related field. Prospective adjunct faculty should send a copy of their curriculum vitae, sample syllabi or course outlines, graduate school transcripts (or an unofficial transcript with a list of courses completed in graduate school), one letter of recommendation, a list of at least two additional references, and any other supporting materials the candidates believe might be helpful. For more information please contact Tiffany Tillman, Program in American Studies at samsel@rowan.edu Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
