      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - International Studies, Center for Interdisciplinary Studies Apply now Job no: 501614 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The International Studies program at Rowan University seeks qualified adjuncts to teach intermediate and upper-level special topics courses in International Studies. Please see the program website for more information about International Studies at Rowan. Qualifications: Master’s degree or Ph.D. in international studies, international relations, international affairs, or a closely related field; experience with online teaching preferred. Procedure: Please include letter of interest and CV in your online application. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
