      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Africana Studies, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Africana Studies, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies Apply now Job no: 501616 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Africana Studies program at Rowan University seeks a qualified adjunct to teach an undergraduate course entitled Introduction to Africana Studies. The applicant should have a Ph.D. in the humanities, preferably with a major or minor in Africana Studies or Black Studies. The applicant will be required to teach the course from a global Black perspective. Qualifications: Ph.D. in Africana Studies or Black Studies or a closely related field. Procedure: Please include a letter of interest, CV, and unofficial transcript of your highest degree in your online application. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 2 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
