    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501613/adjunct-faculty-holocaust-and-genocide-education-center-of-interdisciplinary-studies": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Holocaust and Genocide Education, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Holocaust and Genocide Education, Center of Interdisciplinary Studies Apply now Job no: 501613 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Program in Holocaust and Genocide Education/Center for Interdisciplinary Studies seeks qualified adjuncts to teach pedagogy courses within our interdisciplinary Masters and Certificate in Holocaust and Genocide Education. These courses explore best practices in Holocaust and Genocide Education, program evaluation, program creation, and innovative and effective strategies for teaching hard histories across a range of contexts. Please see the program website for more information about the MA and COGS in Holocaust and Genocide Education at Rowan. Qualifications: Master’s degree or Ph.D. in Teacher Education, Holocaust and Genocide Studies, History Education, or a closely related field. Individuals with experience teaching or running public education programs about the Holocaust, genocide, or other hard histories are particularly welcome to apply. For further information, contact MA/COGS HGE coordinator Jenny Rich at richj@rowan.edu . Applications submitted through this process will be screened on a rolling basis, as additional sections of courses, as well as new course offerings, are added over time. Thus, we request that applicants not contact the department to inquire if openings have been filled. Applications will be retained for possible future semesters of employment. Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 1 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501605/adjunct-faculty-technical-and-professional-writing-department-of-writing-arts": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Technical and Professional Writing, Department of Writing Arts",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Technical and Professional Writing, Department of Writing Arts Apply now Job no: 501605 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Ric Edelman College of Communication, Humanities & Social Sciences The Department of Writing Arts seeks qualified adjuncts to teach courses in technical and professional writing, which may include Introduction to Technical Writing, Writing for the Workplace, Writing as Managers, Writing for Nonprofits, or Editing for Publication. Please see the department website for more information about our Writing Arts major and our minor in Technical and Professional Writing. A master’s degree is required in an appropriate field, such as Composition/Rhetoric, Communication Studies, Business Administration, Strategic Communication, or Human Factors. Preference will be given to applicants with previous experience teaching technical writing or professional writing, favorable recommendations from references, and favorable previous student evaluations. Experience or expertise in usability, user experience, and/or accessible design is particularly desired. Starting Date: September 1, 2026 For further information, contact Amy Woodworth (woodworth@rowan.edu). Applications submitted through this process will be screened on a rolling basis, as additional sections of courses are added over time. Thus, we request that applicants not contact the department to inquire if openings have been filled. Applications will be retained for possible future semesters of employment. Required application materials (in a single PDF file, if possible): -Cover letter -Resume -Names of or letters from references -1-2 page statement of your philosophy, guiding principles, and teaching practices concerning writing or communication -1 or 2 previous teaching evaluations, if available Note: Candidates must be eligible to work in the United States. The University will not sponsor a visa for this position. In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act , and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester and 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned to instructors by College & Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: Jul 1 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
