    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501505/web-operations-specialist-pss1-division-of-marketing-communication": {
      "title": "Web Operations Specialist (PSS1), Division of Marketing & Communication",
      "description": "Web Operations Specialist (PSS1), Division of Marketing & Communication Apply now Job no: 501505 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Professional This position will specifically and comprehensively support the infrastructure and operations for the Rowan University website(s). This role requires a high degree of technical autonomy and deep knowledge of server administration. The position reports to the Director of Web Strategy and Development in the Rowan University Division of Marketing & Communication. Some evening, weekend, and holiday work is to be expected. Candidates must follow the residency requirements outlined by the New Jersey AFT . Essential Position Responsibilities/Functions Configure and perform routine maintenance to ensure optimal performance of Rowan's CMS and web server cluster. Remediate server performance or outage notices in a timely fashion. Build and maintain reliable development, staging, and test environments to support the Web Services team, ensuring parity with production systems. Implement industry web standards and best practices throughout the Rowan University website, with particular awareness for performance. Work collaboratively on various projects with developers, other departments, and external vendors/service providers. Serve as the team's liaison for university-wide operations. Regularly attend Change Management meetings to align with upcoming maintenance, network outages, and current technology events. Work with Rowan’s Information Security Office to address and remediate vulnerabilities. Create and maintain technical documentation regarding back-end processes. Manage several projects simultaneously. Provide support for other, various Rowan University projects and initiatives. Qualifications Required: A master’s degree in web development, computer science, information technology, or related degree. Five (5) to seven (7) years of professional experience working as an web or dev ops specialist, full-stack developer, programmer, or similar role. Familiarity with LAMP web application stack development. Knowledge administering Linux web servers running Apache, PHP, MySQLand other backend server technologies. Comfortability with regular expressions. Experience supporting the CI/CD pipeline utilizing Git and GitHub. Understanding of the entire web development process (design, development, testing, and deployment). Familiarity with content management systems such as Cascade, Drupal, or WordPress. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills. Be able to work independently to solve problems with minimal supervision. Preferred: Experience with AlmaLinux, CentOS, or RHEL Experience with Linux shell scripting to automate server and development processes. Experience supporting Apache Tomcat applications Back-end or full-stack development experience. Knowledge of front-end technologies, including HTML, CSS, Sass, JavaScript, and modern JavaScript frameworks. Experience with Apache Velocity. Experience using Cascade Content Management System by Hannon Hill. Experience working in an Agile/Scrum development environment. Experience using project management tools. Experience supporting web systems in a higher education environment. Proven ability to stay current with rapidly-changing technologies. Salary: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is AFT: Range 27, ($85,550.86 to $98,388.88), with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10). Benefits: For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Rowan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diverse people and abilities. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Advertised: May 22 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501475/adjunct-instructor-of-organ-department-of-music": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Instructor of Organ, Department of Music",
      "description": "Adjunct - Instructor of Organ, Department of Music Apply now Job no: 501475 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - College of the Arts The Department of Music at Rowan University invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Organ (part-time, non-tenure track), beginning September 2, 2026. This endowed position is supported by a $2 million gift from the Storer family in 2015. The Storer Endowment also funded the 2023 renovation of the organ and provides scholarship support for organ majors. The successful candidate will join a thriving program of nearly 400 music majors with a long-standing tradition of excellence in music education and performance. We seek a dynamic teacher-performer with demonstrated excellence in organ pedagogy and an active record of artistic achievement. Responsibilities include teaching applied organ lessons, recruiting and mentoring students, and leading efforts to develop and sustain a vibrant organ studio. The ideal candidate will articulate a clear vision for growing and advancing an organ program within a comprehensive university music department. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in music (or closely related field) Demonstrated excellence in organ performance and teaching Evidence of artistic engagement and professional activity Preferred Qualifications: Experience in recruiting and retaining students Collegiate teaching experience Experience in sacred, liturgical, or collaborative performance settings Salary: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, and in accordance with the current MOA, Rowan University adjuncts are provided with a minimum of $2,225 (after 9/1/2026) per credit for all courses taught, with a maximum teaching load of 8 credits per semester, 12 credits in an academic year. Courses will be assigned by the College and Department on an as-needed basis. Advertised: May 19 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jun 30 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501443/omm-lab-instructor-per-diem-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "OMM Lab Instructor- Per Diem, Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "OMM Lab Instructor- Per Diem, Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501443 Work type: Per Diem Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a Per Diem Instructor who would be available to teach in OMM/SGL 1 & 2 or OMM/PBL 1 & 2 labs with the Department of OMM within the NMI. They will be responsible for the first and second year medical students as they rotate through the OMM lab under the direction of the Course Director(s). Rowan University and the School of Osteopathic Medicine is a community that begins with students, faculty, staff and administration who respect each other and value each other’s dignity. The Rowan University community is committed to a safe environment that encourages intellectual, academic, and social interaction and engagement. The candidate must hold a D.O. and have experience practicing osteopathic manipulative medicine. Our clinical campuses are in Southern New Jersey, which is within the Philadelphia metropolitan area, one hour from the Jersey Shore, an hour and a half from NYC, and two hours from Washington, DC. This is an hourly paid position and total hours per week will be under 19 hours based on academic need. In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the hourly rate for this position is $75/hr. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as, but not limited to, scope of responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. This is a non-benefit eligible position. NOTE : Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US. The university will not sponsor an applicant's work visa for this position. Advertised: May 18 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 20 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501427/psychiatrist-department-of-psychiatry-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "Psychiatrist, Department of Psychiatry, Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "Psychiatrist, Department of Psychiatry, Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501427 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Mount Laurel, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a psychiatrist to join our growing Department of Psychiatry located in Southern New Jersey. This is a full-time position with an academic faculty appointment with experience to obtain the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. The selected candidate will be expected to provide appropriate, comprehensive, and multidisciplinary care. Responsibilities include inpatient and outpatient psychiatric services within two health systems in South Jersey. This role will work closely with the clinical staff for the day-to-day treatment of patients as well as in an academic capacity to teach medical students, residents, and allied health professionals. This position is available for academic promotion within the university. The selected candidate must hold the following: Valid NJ Medical License CDS DEA Board Certified/Board Eligible in Psychiatry Salary: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is $260,000-$280,000. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as, but not limited to, scope of responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. Benefits : For eligible employees, benefits include comprehensive NJ state health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents attending Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Our main clinical campus is located in the Philadelphia metropolitan area approximately 8 miles from Philadelphia, 1 hour from the Atlantic Ocean and 2 hours from New York City. NOTE: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US. The university will not sponsor an applicant's work visa for this position. NOTE: This faculty appointment is Tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. NOTE: Faculty Rank of Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor is pending review and recommendation made by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Apr 17 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 11 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501359/temporary-part-time-hourly-instructor-english-language-program-international-center": {
      "title": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Instructor (English Language Program - International Center)",
      "description": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Instructor (English Language Program - International Center) Apply now Job no: 501359 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Administrative - Clerical Part-Time ESL Instructors - Multiple Locations The English Language Program at Rowan University seeks qualified part-time instructors to teach in our Program. The ELP is a university-based intensive academic English program with nearly 60 years of serving international and local immigrant students. Our primary goals are to prepare students for academic, professional, and personal success through the improvement of their English skills. Location-Specific Opportunities Please review the four distinct projects below. All positions are in-person . Camden Campus: Focus: College-readiness course for high school juniors, seniors, and recent graduates (ages 17+). Dates: July 6 – August 14, 2026. Schedule: Monday – Thursday, 9:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.. Notes: Potential for continued employment into fall/spring based on enrollment. 2. Glassboro Campus: Year-Round Pool Dates: Ongoing/Year-round. Schedule: Monday – Thursday, 18 hours per week: 9:00 a.m. – 10:30 a.m. 10:40 a.m. – 12:10 p.m. 1:05 p.m. – 2:35 p.m. Notes: Applicants should be available to teach all time blocks. 3. Trenton Project Focus: New program project starting in the fall. Dates: Starting Fall 2026; likely to be ongoing. Schedule: Details to be determined based on project needs. 4. Glassboro Campus: International High School Summer Program Focus: International high school students. Dates: July 7 – August 14, 2026 (6 weeks). Schedule: Monday – Thursday, 18 hours per week. Notes: Familiarity with Islamic culture and customs is preferred. Ideal candidates will have: A master’s degree in TESOL, Linguistics, English, or other closely related fields. A minimum of 2 years teaching academic ESL in an adult education environment is required. TEFL certificate holders with a bachelor’s degree and extensive teaching experience - may be considered. Please note: Having only a K-12 ESL teaching certification or endorsement is not applicable to this position. This position requires a passion for working with young adults from various socio economic and cultural backgrounds. Responsibilities include: Teach courses a dynamic curriculum that includes college readiness skills. Create course plans and syllabi based on provided curriculum. Attend all mandatory departmental and faculty meetings. Participate in program activities. Work closely with the Director and Lead Instructor to meet students’ needs. Fluency in another language (Spanish, Turkish, Vietnamese, or Arabic) is desirable. Required application materials: • Cover letter • Resume / CV Rate: $50 per hour Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Rowan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diverse people and abilities. Reasonable accommodation will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Advertised: Mar 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 17 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501353/research-computing-support-specialist-pss1-information-resources-technology": {
      "title": "Research Computing Support Specialist (PSS1), Information Resources & Technology",
      "description": "Research Computing Support Specialist (PSS1), Information Resources & Technology Apply now Job no: 501353 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Professional Research Computing Specialist (PSS1) Rowan University is seeking an experienced and adaptable System Administrator to join our Research Computing team. In this position, you will be responsible for supporting hardware and software needs related to scientific computing used in education and research at Rowan University. Reporting to the Director of Enterprise System Administration, and working closely with the Director of Operations of the Center for Scientific Computing (CSC), you will be a member of the Enterprise System Administration team as well as the CSC community. What you get to do: Collaborating with faculty and researchers to architect and estimate computational equipment requirements. Architecting and configuring computational equipment for both individual teaching/research labs and centralized computing facilities (High Performance Computing), as well as setting up user access, compiling, installing, and optimizing scientific computing software, and participating in the delivery of user training. Optimizing the enforcement of security configurations and standards for scientific computing equipment per the project-specific security level requirements. Contributing to the design and execution of dedicated research environments. Partnering with faculty and researchers to streamline the “Get Technology” procurement process for expedited approvals. Providing support and maintenance of scientific computing systems and software, including routine software and hardware monitoring and upgrades, and user access and usage management. Creating and maintaining an online user resource that includes implementation and support documentation for Information Technology Resources and Tools (IRT), such as Technical Design Documents (TDDs), support procedures, and knowledge articles. Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in a related discipline or Bachelor's degree and 2 years equivalent work experience. The ability to balance long-term projects and strategic initiatives with short-term emergent requests. Excellent troubleshooting skills. Commitment to customer service. Demonstrated ability to set goals and achieve them. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to support a 24x7 environment. Nice to have: Experience supporting Research Environments and High Performance Computing. At least one year of experience with system administration of Linux-based HPC systems. Hands-on experience managing Linux and Windows desktops. Experience working with networking, including subnets, VLANs, IP addressing. Experience working in a production data center environment. What we offer: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is AFT: Range 27 ($85,550 to $98,388), with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10). Excellent retirement benefits with 8% employer contribution. 22 days of vacation time allotted annually with the ability to carry over a full year of accrued time. 15 days of sick time allotted annually with unlimited carry over. Excellent Medical and Dental coverage - low contribution, low copay. Tuition benefits available to you, eligible dependents, spouse, and domestic or civil union partners. Wellness incentives and other programs to help support your work-life balance. Housing incentive for Glassboro residents. For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: Rowan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diverse people and abilities. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted will be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. #Dice Advertised: Mar 13 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501347/chair-department-of-medicine-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Medicine, Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "Chair, Department of Medicine, Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501347 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Clinical, Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Chair, Department of Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan Medicine, an affiliate of Virtua Medical Group Location: Stratford, NJ Department: Department of Medicine Reports to: Vice Dean of Clinical Affairs Summary: Rowan‑Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine invites applications for a Chair of the Department of Medicine, a leadership role ideal for a physician‑educator who thrives in a collaborative, outpatient‑focused environment and enjoys developing faculty, strengthening clinical programs, and shaping the future of osteopathic medical education. This role oversees a small, multi‑specialty faculty group (fewer than 20 clinicians) across General Internal Medicine, Endocrinology, Rheumatology, Infectious Disease, and Pulmonary Medicine. This role does not oversee inpatient services. The Chair works closely with supportive institutional leadership to advance high‑quality patient care, teaching, and scholarship. Essential Duties will include: Department Leadership Provide vision, direction, and mentorship to a small, multi‑specialty faculty team. Foster a culture of collaboration, professionalism, and continuous improvement. Advocate for departmental needs and represent Medicine within school leadership forums. Support faculty development, promotion pathways, and recruitment of mission‑aligned clinicians. Clinical Oversight Oversee ambulatory clinical operations across primary and specialty care sites. This role does not oversee inpatient services. Partner with other department chairs to strengthen quality, safety, and patient experience. Grow outpatient clinical programs in alignment with community needs and Rowan Medicine strategy. Ensure compliance with ethical practice standards, billing requirements, and regulatory expectations. Strong administrative support is provided through Rowan Medicine operations and a departmental business administrator, allowing the Chair to focus on quality, faculty development, and program growth. Academic Leadership Support faculty engagement in teaching medical students and residents. Ensure appropriate faculty effort and oversight for educational programs. Encourage scholarly activity suited to faculty interests and departmental capacity. Promote collaborative research opportunities across departments and schools. Strategic & Organizational Development Participate in strategic planning for clinical growth and academic innovation. Promote quality improvement initiatives and patient‑centered service enhancements. Administrative Responsibilities Manage departmental budget and resource allocation. Oversee grant‑funded programs and support faculty pursuing extramural funding. Direct and facilitate the recruitment, retention, and professional development of high‑quality faculty and staff, ensuring the department remains a strong, mission‑aligned team. Conduct timely performance evaluations and support faculty/staff professional growth. Serve on committees and task forces as appointed. Qualifications D.O. or M.D. with AOA or ABMS Board Certification in Internal Medicine. Demonstrated leadership experience in clinical, academic, or administrative roles. Evidence of excellence in teaching, clinical practice, and/or scholarly activity. Experience with grants or funded projects preferred. Academic credentials qualifying for Associate Professor or Professor. Must hold: NJ Medical License, CDS, DEA . Compensation & Benefits In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual salary range for this faculty position is $265,000 – $315,000 , commensurate with experience and qualifications. NJ State health, dental, and retirement benefits Generous paid time off and holidays Tuition reimbursement for employees, spouses, and dependents attending Rowan University (undergraduate programs) More details: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Additional Notes Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S.; visa sponsorship is not available. This is a tenure‑eligible faculty appointment. Final faculty rank is determined by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Mar 11 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 13 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501157/assistantassociate-professor-family-medicine-physician-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Family Medicine Physician - Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Family Medicine Physician - Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 501157 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Sewell, New Jersey, Hammonton, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a full-time family medicine physician to join the Department of Family Medicine. In support of SOM’s mission and vision, the selected candidate will provide and manage direct patient care at one or more of the outpatient clinical offices located in the Southern New Jersey area. The candidate will hold an academic title and have an active role in the training and education of medical students, interns, residents, and fellows. Additionally, the candidate will have the opportunity to participate in faculty development. Highlights include: Opportunity for collaborative research with faculty and residents Participate in the education and mentorship of medical students at Rowan-Virtua SOM Serve as a core faculty member in the Family Medicine Residency program at Sewell Being part of a dynamic team committed to excellence in patient care and education Comprehensive benefits package Competitive salary The selected candidate must hold the following: Valid NJ Medical License CDS DEA Board Certified/Eligible in Family Medicine or Internal Medicine Applicants need to submit an online application. Please submit a letter of interest and curriculum vitae as a single PDF document. Our main clinical campus is located in the Philadelphia metropolitan area approximately 8 miles from Philadelphia, 1 hour from the Atlantic Ocean and 2 hours from New York City. Salary: In compliance with the State of New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Act, the salary range for this position is $190,000 to $220,000. Placement into the range is determined by the candidate’s qualifications, professional experience and other factors. Benefits : For eligible employees, benefits include comprehensive NJ state health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents attending Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. This faculty appointment is Tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. Faculty Rank of Assistant Professor/Associate Professor is pending review and recommendation made by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Jan 5 2026 Eastern Standard Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501016/openrank-tenuredtenuretrack-faculty-immunology-department-of-biomedical-sciences-cmsru": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty, Immunology, Department of Biomedical Sciences (CMSRU)",
      "description": "Open-Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty, Immunology, Department of Biomedical Sciences (CMSRU) Apply now Job no: 501016 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Camden, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Cooper Medical School of Rowan University Open-Rank Tenured/Tenure-Track Faculty, Immunology, Department of Biomedical Sciences (CMSRU) The Department of Biomedical Sciences of Cooper Medical School of Rowan University (CMSRU) invites applicants for a full-time, 12-month, tenure-track position at the assistant /associate professor level in the area of immunology and related disciplines. This position will entail teaching immunology to first- and second-year medical students in an integrated curriculum. Teaching formats at CMSRU include lectures, small-group active learning sessions, and practical application sessions. Additional academic responsibilities will include advising and mentoring students in the development of scholarly projects; assessing, reviewing, and evaluating student educational activities and progress; and serving on university-wide, medical school, and/or departmental committees. The candidate will complement current areas of faculty expertise and be expected to develop and maintain an externally funded, sustainable program for independent research in the candidate’s area of interest. A start-up package and competitive salary are offered. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in immunology, microbiology, or related life sciences discipline from an accredited institution Post-doctoral experience Record of scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications commensurate with career stage Excellent written and spoken communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching in an undergraduate, graduate, and/or medical school setting Experience with case-based, team-based, or active learning methodologies Ability to work collaboratively with a team of multidisciplinary faculty The Department of Biomedical Sciences at CMSRU is committed to fostering excellence in teaching and multidisciplinary research. The department currently consists of 30 faculty members. Areas of faculty expertise include microbiology, immunology, cancer biology, molecular and cell biology, genetics/genomics, neurobiology, and physiology. Our goal is to advance learning and knowledge through multidisciplinary scholarship and delivery of the basic science curriculum for medical, graduate, and undergraduate students. CMSRU is the only four-year M.D. degree-granting medical school in southern New Jersey. Our medical education building is located in Camden, NJ, near Philadelphia, in the heart of the Cooper Health Sciences Campus. More information on CMSRU can be found at https://cmsru.rowan.edu/ . CMSRU is part of Rowan University, a Carnegie R2-classified Doctoral University with approximately 25,000 students. Rowan has been recognized as one of the top 100 public universities in the nation and is the 3rd fastest growing public institution in the U.S. by U.S. News & World Report. More information on Rowan can be found at https://www.rowan.edu/ . How to Apply: Interested applicants should apply online at Rowan University’s Career Site ( https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/listing/ ) and complete the online application and include the following: Cover letter Current curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy (1-2 pages) Statement of scholarly/research interests, including applicants' future research goals and plans for achieving external funding for achieving those goals (1-3 pages) Names and contact information of three references from whom the applicant has requested letters of support Application review will begin on January 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. For priority consideration, please apply by December 1, 2025. Although flexible, the expected start date for the position is July 1, 2026. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US. Rowan University is committed to equal opportunity in employment. For the complete Rowan University non-discrimination policy, see: https://sites.rowan.edu/equity/_docs/policies/eeo-statement.pdf Salary: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is: · Assistant professor: Ranges 24, 26, 29 · Associate professor: Ranges 32, 33, 36 · Full professor: Ranges 41, 42, 43 with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. Please visit this link to view all respective ranges listed above: https://www.cnjscl.org/Library/CNJSCL_FT-PT_2023-2027_Salary_Charts-Approved.pdf Benefits: For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Advertised: Nov 7 2025 Eastern Standard Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501064/temporary-part-time-hourly-security-officer-public-safety": {
      "title": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Security Officer (Public Safety)",
      "description": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Security Officer (Public Safety) Apply now Job no: 501064 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Camden, New Jersey, Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Public Safety/Security Provide assistance and protection to persons and property in and about the Rowan University Glassboro Campus or at the Camden Medical School Rowan University (CMSRU) in accordance with the Public Safety department rules, regulations and general operating procedures. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: · Measurement criteria are \"as observed by the Sergeant/Shift Supervisor\" for all performance standards, unless otherwise indicated. · Contributes to the University's positive public image by handling all of the public in a courteous and professional manner. · Contributes to the smooth and efficient operation of the Department by being punctual to work and for assignments and maintains an above average attendance. · Contributes to the professional image of the Department and the University by maintaining uniforms and equipment according to Department rules and regulations. · Performs fixed posts duties as required. · Patrols buildings and grounds taking necessary action to prevent fire, theft and vandalism of Rowan University Main Campus property, ensuring safe and orderly conditions. · Prepares and submits reports when required. · Manages day-to-day activities according to department standards. · Understands and adheres to Rowan University Public Safety compliance standards as they appear in Rowan University Public Safety’s Corporate Compliance Policy, Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy. · Performs other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily and must pass a police background investigation. Candidate will be required to possess a driver's license valid in New Jersey to perform the essential duties of the position. This position is subject to the residency requirements of the NJ First Act (N.J.S.A. 52:14-7, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any person hired to this position shall either have their principal residence in New Jersey or they have one year from the date of employment to establish, and then maintain, principal residence in the State of New Jersey. RATE: $18 EDUCATION: High school diploma or an equivalent is required. HOURS: This temporary, part-time position is assigned no more than twenty-five (25) hours per week and is not to exceed 944 hours per fiscal year. Work is contracted annually to coincide with the fiscal year and is contingent upon budget appropriations. NOTES: This posting is being used to collect resumes to fill part-time, hourly vacancies at the Glassboro Campus OR at the Camden Medical School Rowan University (CMSRU). Rowan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diverse people and abilities. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the University will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. LICENSE REQUIREMENT: Appointees will be required to possess a driver’s license valid in New Jersey. Advertised: Oct 14 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/500938/public-safety-telecommunicatorpublic-safety-telecommunicator-trainee-rowan-police-department": {
      "title": "Public Safety Telecommunicator/Public Safety Telecommunicator Trainee, Rowan Police Department",
      "description": "Public Safety Telecommunicator/Public Safety Telecommunicator Trainee, Rowan Police Department Apply now Job no: 500938 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Public Safety/Security Public Safety Telecommunicator and/or Public Safety Telecommunicator Trainee Position Summary: The Rowan University Police Department is looking for a reliable Dispatcher (Public Safety Telecommunicator/Public Safety Telecommunicator Trainee) to act as a communication point for emergency and non-emergency calls. The ideal candidate must be primarily an excellent communicator and able to remain calm and composed, especially in emergency situations. You must be able to multi-task as well as take the appropriate action with little supervision. The goal is to enable different parties to communicate well by ensuring the accurate and timely transmission of information. Major Duties: Receives emergency and non-emergency calls and efficiently gathers, evaluates, prioritizes, and documents information from callers. Dispatches police, security, EMS field units and other related services to specific locations using a computer aided dispatch system, multiple video display terminals, two-way radio dispatch console consisting of 7 radio channels and related equipment. Evaluates incoming reports of police, security, and EMS; immediately transmits complete and accurate information to appropriate field personnel. Monitors, coordinates and accurately maintains the status of incidents and record of dispatched emergency service personnel and apparatus. Receives and disseminates information from other law enforcement and emergency service computer networks related to jurisdictional requests for police, fire or medical service assistance, or to notices of wanted persons, stolen property, warrants and all points bulletins and maintains confidentiality of information. Maintains familiarity with area geography including additional campuses, campus buildings, and surrounding areas. Maintains up-to-date understanding of public safety policies and procedures for the Police Department at Rowan University. Responds to routine and non-routine inquiries regarding police, security, or EMS; properly classifies and prioritizes any report or complaint information and determines appropriate course of action; provides appropriate referrals as necessary. Preferred Qualifications and Skills: Valid Driver’s License Proficient in typing for quick paced data entry Organizational and multi-tasking abilities The ability to develop and maintain cooperative and professional relationships with fellow employees, representatives from other departments, and supervisors The ability to use judgment and decision-making skills to evaluate situations, establish priorities, and resolve matters The ability to think quickly The ability to work under stressful situations The ability to actively listen, communicate effectively through clear speech via radio and telephone The ability to follow instructions The ability to establish priorities and pass on information as needed Proven experience as a dispatcher or relevant position Basic 9-1-1 Certification EMD (Emergency Medical Dispatch) Certification CPR Certification NCIC/CJIS/AOC Requirements: Public Safety Telecommunicator: Available for current state employees in the competitive division. One (1) year of experience in work involving the receiving, transmitting, and relaying of video display and/or radio messages, and in the receiving, relaying, and recording of complaints and requests for emergency assistance which shall have included the use of video display, data processing, automatic number identification, automatic location identification, switching equipment, or other computer-oriented equipment. Public Safety Telecommunicator Trainee: Upon the successful completion of the twelve (12) month training period, appointee will be eligible for advancement under Civil Service Commission procedure to the title Public Safety Telecommunicator. The inability of an employee to attain a level of performance warranting advancement to the title listed above shall be considered as cause for separation. Salary & Benefits: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is as follows: Public Safety Telecommunicator Trainee: IFPTE : Range 99, $48,366.45 Public Safety Telecommunicator: IFPTE Range 16 (Step 1 $50,539 to Step 4 $57,393 ), with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Hours: This position works various 12-hour shifts or longer if needed. This includes days, nights, weekends, and/or holidays. Notes: Rowan University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diverse people and abilities. Reasonable accommodations will be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Please note that this position is subject to the NJ First Act, requiring public employees to establish residency in the State of New Jersey. See N.J.S.A. 52:14-7 (L. 2011, Chapter 70) for further information. Only completed, online applications submitted will be considered. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. SAME APPLICANTS: If you are applying under the NJ “SAME” program, your supporting documents (Schedule A or B letter), must be submitted with your application by the closing date indicated above. For more information on the SAME Program visit their Website at: https://nj.gov/csc/same/overview/index.shtml , email: SAME@csc.nj.gov , or call CSC at (833)691-0404. Advertised: Sep 17 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/500651/general-internal-medicine-physicianopen-rank-rowanvirtua-som": {
      "title": "General Internal Medicine Physician-OPEN RANK -Rowan-Virtua SOM",
      "description": "General Internal Medicine Physician-OPEN RANK -Rowan-Virtua SOM Apply now Job no: 500651 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine is currently seeking a General Internal Medicine physician to join our growing Department of Medicine located in Southern New Jersey. This is a full-time position with an academic faculty appointment. The selected candidate will be expected to provide appropriate, comprehensive, and multidisciplinary care. Responsibilities include office practice, off-site clinic sessions, call coverage and teaching students in all of these settings. The candidate selected for this position must hold the following: Valid NJ Medical License CDS DEA Board Certified/Board Eligible BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents).” For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this AAUP position is : Instructor: ($ 100,787 to $ 136,800) * Assistant Professor: ($ 123,083 to $ 167,264) * Associate Professor: ($ 146,089 to $ 198,535) * Full Professor: ($ 170,255 to $ 231,285) * *Placement within the range is determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, and other factors. For clinical faculty positions, additional compensation paid through supplemental funding based on regional benchmarking standards and internal equity by specialty. Our main clinical campus is located in the Philadelphia metropolitan area approximately 8 miles from Philadelphia, 1 hour from the Atlantic Ocean and 2 hours from New York City. NOTE: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US. The university will not sponsor an applicant's work visa for this position. NOTE: This faculty appointment is Tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. NOTE: Faculty Rank of Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor is pending review and recommendation made by the Faculty Affairs Committee. Advertised: Jul 7 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/500728/physician-department-of-geriatrics-rowanvirtua-som-open-rank": {
      "title": "Physician, Department of Geriatrics, Rowan-Virtua SOM, Open Rank",
      "description": "Physician, Department of Geriatrics, Rowan-Virtua SOM, Open Rank Apply now Job no: 500728 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine The New Jersey Institute for Successful Aging, Department of Geriatrics and Gerontology at Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine in Stratford, New Jersey is seeking a full-time clinical faculty member to join our pioneering and expanding team. The Rowan-Virtua New Jersey Institute for Successful Aging (NJISA) has a distinguished history dating back to its origins in the 1980’s. It is a designated Center of Excellence with a tripartite mission of clinical service, education and research. It is a multidisciplinary Center, providing team based care to older individuals. The Department consists of a diversified faculty and staff including geriatricians, geriatric psychiatrists, neurologists, neuropsychologists, behavioral researchers, neuroscientist researchers, nurse practitioners, social workers and health educators. It offers primary care services across the continuum of care, including acute care, ambulatory care, home and assisted living care, subacute and long-term care. Specialty programs include the Memory Assessment Program, Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment, and House Calls. NJISA physicians provide direct patient care and serve as Medical Directors at multiple long-term and subacute care facilities. NJISA’s research focuses on behavioral research, basic science/translational research, and research in primary care. NJISA is home to a Biomarker Discovery Center and is engaged in significant research on Alzheimer’s disease and digital neuropsychological screening. Funding is provided by the National Institutes of Health and private foundations. NJISA also either participates in or leads multi-institutional research projects. NJISA provides an array of educational offerings to families, caregivers, and health professionals. As a Department in Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine, NJISA is also committed to training the physicians of tomorrow. NJISA’s educational programs extend to other health professionals including nursing, pharmacy, public health, and biomedical sciences. Our goal is to create a healthcare workforce that is prepared to meet the needs of the growing generation of older individuals. As a clinical faculty member in our Department, you will provide primary care/geriatric clinical services in the ambulatory, acute, home, long-term care, and subacute settings and participate in the on call schedule. Additionally, you will participate in the training and education of medical students and residents. You will participate in faculty development and such other duties as assigned by the Department Chair to support the mission of the Department of Geriatrics and Gerontology, Rowan-Virtua New Jersey Institute for Successful Aging. The selected candidate must hold the following: Valid NJ Medical License CDS DEA Board Certification/Eligibility in Internal Medicine or Family Medicine required. Certificate of Added Qualification in Geriatrics preferred. Salary is competitive and accompanied by a comprehensive benefits package including Rowan undergraduate tuition for eligible dependents. Our main clinical campus is located in the Philadelphia metropolitan area approximately 8 miles from Philadelphia, 1 hour from Atlantic Ocean and 2 hours from New York City. Notes: All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. This faculty appointment is tenure eligible and may be granted upon successful completion of criteria listed in the Rowan-Virtua SOM Faculty Bylaws. Advertised: Jun 23 2025 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 6 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/499779/time-faculty-department-of-experiential-engineering-education-exeed": {
      "title": "¾ Time Faculty- Department of Experiential Engineering Education (ExEEd)",
      "description": "¾ Time Faculty- Department of Experiential Engineering Education (ExEEd) Apply now Job no: 499779 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering Position Description The Department of Experiential Engineering Education (ExEEd) in the Henry M. Rowan College of Engineering at Rowan University invites applications for temporary ¾ time teaching faculty position(s) for the 2025 Fall and 2026 Spring semesters. The successful candidate will be part of a highly collaborative team that is responsible for teaching our introductory First-year and Sophomore Engineering Clinic courses. The Engineering Clinic Sequence is the hallmark of Rowan’s innovative undergraduate engineering program and features multidisciplinary, hands-on, project-oriented courses. Main Responsibilities Engage in high-quality, evidence-based instruction in introductory undergraduate engineering courses (e.g., First-year and Sophomore Engineering Clinics) Foster a collegial and inclusive learning and working environment Required Qualifications A minimum of a Master’s degree in engineering or a closely related discipline. A strong interest in teaching hands-on, project-based engineering courses, particularly in the early years of the curriculum A commitment to working with students from diverse backgrounds including women, students of color, LGBTQ students, first­‐generation to college students, students with disabilities, students with low socioeconomic status, and veterans. About the Department of Experiential Engineering Education ExEEd was launched to catalyze the translation of educational innovations into the classroom, cultivate a collaborative environment for engineering education research, and to lead the College’s undergraduate engineering educational mission for first- and second-year students in all engineering disciplines. Our department also manages the B.S. Engineering Entrepreneurship program and offers a PhD in Engineering Education. Additional Information Start Date: September 1, 2025 A ¾ time appointment typically carries a 9-credit / semester teaching load (or 18 credits in one academic year), and pays ¾ of the applicable salary of a full-time instructor, with no other benefits. Applications must be submitted through our online applicant tracking system. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Applications should include the following, assembled in the following order in a single PDF file: 1) a cover letter summarizing qualifications, 2) detailed resume or CV, 3) statement of teaching interests and philosophy, 4) names and contact information for three references. Please name the file as _Application.pdf. Optionally, additional relevant documentation may be submitted in an Appendix as a separate file, named _Appendix.pdf. Rowan University values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. NOTES: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Advertised: Jul 29 2024 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/499622/per-diem-psychiatric-nurse-practitioner-rowanvirtua-som-department-of-psychiatry": {
      "title": "Per Diem Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner, Rowan-Virtua SOM, Department of Psychiatry",
      "description": "Per Diem Psychiatric Nurse Practitioner, Rowan-Virtua SOM, Department of Psychiatry Apply now Job no: 499622 Work type: Per Diem Location: Mount Laurel, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine The Department of Psychiatry is seeking experienced Advanced Practice Nurses (APN) that is able to admit patients, make rounds, write orders for medication, diagnostic studies, devices, and consultations on inpatient psychiatric unit or provide services to patients scheduled at contracted agencies. Candidate will work collaboratively with staff nurses, social workers and other staff physicians and agency staff. Location and time of assignments to be mutually agreed upon. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include the following. Provides coverage at inpatient sites. Services to include psychiatric evaluation, medication management, restraints and staff consultation as required. Provides appropriate documentation of care including chart notes and completion of required/requested forms. Provides additional coverage call for the Department’s hospital contract. Coverage will be on‑site face-to-face. Must ensure the possession of a functioning phone at all times while on-call. Must respond to any and all calls by telephone response within 15 minutes. Must be available and respond to any and all or direct service to patients within one hour of being called for restraint, sentinel event, near-miss or any other clinical situation that requires face-to-face clinical care by an independent clinical practitioner. Keeps abreast of agency, hospital and departmental policies and procedures. Submits appropriate billing information. Performs other related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE: Experience: One (1) year of experience as a practicing APN Licensure: Unrestricted Licensed as an APN with the State of New Jersey with a current CDS and DEA. Salary: Commensurable with experience Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. This is a non-tenure position. Advertised: Jun 10 2024 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/499245/physicians-and-advanced-practice-nurses-for-various-rowanvirtua-medicine-practices": {
      "title": "Physicians and Advanced Practice Nurses for various Rowan-Virtua Medicine Practices",
      "description": "Physicians and Advanced Practice Nurses for various Rowan-Virtua Medicine Practices Apply now Job no: 499245 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine Physicians and Advance Practice Nurses for various Rowan-Virtua Medicine Practices SUMMARY: The planned expansion of Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine and its clinical practice plan, Rowan-Virtua Medicine, is fueling a need to expand the faculty at one of America’s elite osteopathic medical schools. We are seeking several full-time faculty from the specialties of Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Med-Peds, Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine, Geriatrics, Pediatrics, Physician Medicine & Rehabilitation and Psychiatry to join our faculty in several integrated practices including the NeuroMusculoskeletal Institute (NMI) and Rowan-Virtua Regional Integrated Special Needs Center (RISN) . Rowan University is a rapidly growing Carnegie-classified national public research university. Its School of Osteopathic Medicine was established more than 40 years ago and enjoys a stellar reputation for clinical care, research and medical education. The selected candidates for these positions will provide and manage direct patient care at one or more of Rowan-Virtua Medicine’s out-patient clinical offices located in the Southern New Jersey area and will have an active role in training and educating the next generation of medical students, interns, residents and fellows. Additionally, successful candidates will enjoy opportunities for faculty development and collaborative research with colleagues specializing in multiple disciplines throughout the University. Most positions will offer an opportunity and dedicated time for teaching medical students in their first two years in a new satellite medical school campus. Most positions require a valid New Jersey medical license, CDS license and DEA license. All positions offer a comprehensive benefits package and competitive salary. Opportunities and expectations associated with specific positions include: Physicians and APNs Provide compassionate patient care focused on quality and value based care Work with a multidisciplinary team caring for patients, including those with complex intellectual, physical and developmental disabilities and their families Participate in collaborative research with faculty, residents and students NMI physicians would additionally provide care to patients seeking pain management and outpatient substance use treatment Teaching medical students and residents in their clinical skills development in the office while seeing patients Most positions will include an opportunity to teach medical students in their first 2 years with dedicated time allocated for a variety of teaching opportunities, which include: Problem-based Learning facilitation , assisting medical students to learn history-taking, physical exam, procedures and osteopathic manipulation skills in the lab setting May require participation in pre and post-doctoral training activities, education and staff development; involvement in department, school and university committees These positions require board certification/eligibility in the specialties listed above. Our main clinical campus is located in the Philadelphia metropolitan area approximately 8 miles from Philadelphia, 1 hour from the Atlantic Ocean and 2 hours from New York City. Experience with diverse populations. Record of respect and openness towards people whose social and cultural background is different from one’s own. Ability to recognize and manage one’s behaviors and communication to create an inclusive, equitable, and welcoming environment within the department/organization. Rowan University values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity employment. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Advertised: Jan 11 2024 Eastern Standard Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/493435/volunteer-faculty": {
      "title": "Volunteer Faculty",
      "description": "Volunteer Faculty Apply now Job no: 493435 Work type: Temporary Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Faculty - School of Osteopathic Medicine RowanSOM seeks to invite physicians and providers serving as preceptors to students and residents at our affiliated partner hospitals to apply for academic appointment as members of the volunteer faculty. Qualifications guidelines for academic appointment are: • Clinical Instructor: Shall be appropriately degreed and/or licensed and have developed the skills required for their clinical field. The candidate shall demonstrate a high level of ability in clinical practice and teaching in their field of expertise. • Clinical Assistant Professor, community-based: Shall hold a terminal professional degree, either MD, DO or PhD, and has completed all appropriate postdoctoral training and in addition, shall be certified by the appropriate specialty and/or subspecialty board. The candidate shall demonstrate a high level of ability in clinical practice and teaching in their field of expertise. Appointments for academic rank above Assistant Professor must be applied for separately by contacting the Rowan SOM Office of Faculty Affairs either by phone at 856-566-6870 or email SomFacultyAffairs@rowan.edu . Advertised: Dec 27 2018 Eastern Standard Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501899/veterinary-assistants-and-veterinary-technicians-emergency-and-critical-care-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians, Emergency and Critical Care  - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians, Emergency and Critical Care - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501899 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians, Emergency and Critical Care - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Our Mission: Our top priorities are the development of an institution delivering excellent client and patient care in addition to training graduates who are competent, confident, and ready for practice from day one. Our goal is to do this through collaborative, education- and culture-focused practice creating continuity through the patient, client, student, faculty and employee journey. We anticipate our team, hospital and school will quickly grow, making this first year foundational in the structure of what the future school will look like. Position Summary: The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (SSVM) is seeking Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians to join our Emergency Service veterinary program at our new veterinary teaching hospital! SSVM is a new and innovative veterinary teaching hospital for small animals, equipped with state-of-the-art equipment. The teaching hospital is designed to accommodate multiple specialty departments, including anesthesia, cardiology, dermatology, dentistry and oral surgery, diagnostic imaging, emergency/critical care, exotics, internal medicine, neurology, oncology, ophthalmology, primary care, and a full pharmacy with sterile compounding capabilities. These positions will support the clinical services in the veterinary teaching hospital treating patients and educating students. Selected candidates will be able to: Provide comprehensive and quality care to clients and patients. Demonstrate a commitment to a collaborative and collegial work culture. Problem-solve and adapt to a fast-growing and changing environment with a growth mindset. Reporting Structure: The Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians will report directly to the Veterinary Technician Manager. Required Qualifications & Salary Information: The starting rate for each level is equivalent to the probationary rate listed below based on the collective bargaining unit guidelines. After completion of a six-month probationary period, the employee's pay can increase to the “Job Rate” for that position. Depending on experience, the candidate may be hired at the \"Job Rate\" to start. Veterinary Technicians (Credentialed, evidence of passing the VTNE) Level 1 Veterinary Technician Specialist (VTS) certification eligible or achieved, or equivalent specialty-level expertise Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $32.25/hour Job Rate: $35.40/hours Max Rate: $38.05/hour Level 2 Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $28.05/hour Job Rate: $31.00/hour Max Rate: $33.20/hour Level 3 Minimum 3 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $23.08/hour Job Rate: $26.55/hour Max Rate: $29.97/hour Veterinary Assistants (Non-Credentialed) Level 1 Associate degree or higher Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $23.08/hour Job Rate: $26.55/hour Max Rate: $29.97/hour Level 2 Associate degree or higher Minimum 3 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $19.87/hour Job Rate: $22.48/hour Max Rate: $24.86/hour *Hourly rates reflect each position’s pay post 7/1/25 per the collective bargaining agreement. *Employees must have 4+ years of applicable experience to be hired above the probationary rate per the collective bargaining agreement. SHIFT DIFFERENTIAL: *Members of the Teamsters negotiations unit will also be eligible for a shift differential of $2.00 per hour. The shift differential will be paid to eligible employees for complete shifts only and provided that they work half or more of their regularly scheduled hours after 3:00 p.m. or before 6:00 a.m. Preferred Qualifications: Willing to work flexible hours (days, swing or overnight) and weekends as needed. Willing to assist as needed in other areas or departments within the hospital. Previous experience working in a teaching environment. Previous experience working in an emergency or urgent care veterinary practice. Adaptable to a fast-growing and developing workplace. Excellent understanding of medical terminology, medications, calculations, and common emergency procedures. Excellence and interest in developing interpersonal skills in relation to co-workers, clinicians, students, staff, and clients. **All hospital staff working clinical positions and handling live animals are required to be vaccinated against Rabies unless a medical or religious exemption is requested. Documentation may be required for approval of exemption. Costs associated with immunization and/or titer will be covered by the University for the employee.** Working Conditions Hazards Veterinary workers may be exposed to hazards like slips, trips, and falls. They may also be exposed to unpleasant odors, noises, and animal feces and urine. When working with animals that are frightened or in pain, veterinary workers risk being bitten, kicked, or scratched. Veterinary workers may be exposed to hazards like bloodborne pathogens, hazardous drugs, radiation, toxic waste, and chemical hazards such as disinfectants, pesticides, and latex. Animals The types of animals treated at a veterinary hospital can affect the working conditions. Our teaching hospital may consist, but is not limited to, the following types of animals: small mammals, large mammals, livestock, reptiles, avians, and other exotic animals. Information about the institution: A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. As a state public University, Rowan employees are eligible to participate in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service. Benefits: While salary is one component of employment, Rowan offers a comprehensive and meaningful benefits package designed to support your professional growth, well-being, and long-term career development. As a veterinary technician within an academic teaching hospital, you will: Contribute directly to the education and mentorship of future veterinarians Work alongside board-certified specialists and faculty in a collaborative, team-focused environment Engage in continuing education and professional development opportunities Build leadership skills in an academic and evolving clinical environment Be part of a mission-driven institution committed to innovation, community engagement, and advancing veterinary medicine Comprehensive State health and dental benefits, state pension: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Extensive accrued time off/paid holidays: 22 vacation/float days per year 12 sick days per year 9 paid holidays per year Tuition waiver for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouses and dependents after one year of employment). At Rowan, you are not only supporting patient care — you are shaping the next generation of veterinary professionals while building a sustainable and rewarding career path. Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. The job posting will remain active until all positions are filled. Advertised: Oct 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jan 25 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501910/primary-care-veterinary-assistants-and-veterinary-technicians-shreiber-school-of-veterinary-medicine-of-rowan-university": {
      "title": "Primary Care Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University",
      "description": "Primary Care Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Apply now Job no: 501910 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Primary Care Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians - Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University Work type: Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: School of Veterinary Medicine Our Mission: Our top priorities are delivering excellent patient and client care while developing competent, confident veterinarians who are ready to contribute to the profession from day one. We believe exceptional clinical training is built through collaborative, education- and culture-focused practice that connects the patient, client, student, faculty, and employee experience. As a new and growing veterinary school and teaching hospital, this is a unique opportunity to help shape how primary care is practiced and taught. Our team members are not only providing high-quality care today; they are helping prepare the next generation of veterinarians and contributing to the continued growth and strength of the veterinary profession. Position Summary: The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine of Rowan University (SSVM) is seeking Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians to join our Primary Care service within our new veterinary teaching hospital, located 1.5 miles from the main Glassboro campus. Primary Care is central to our mission of developing day-one-ready veterinarians. Team members in this role will help provide thorough, high-quality primary care, anesthesia, and surgical support while serving as clinical mentors and teachers for veterinary students on service. The ideal candidate enjoys both excellent patient care and helping learners develop sound clinical judgment, technical skills, confidence, and professional communication. SSVM is a new and innovative veterinary teaching hospital for small animals, equipped with state-of-the-art resources and designed to support collaboration across primary care and multiple specialty services. Selected candidates will be able to: • Provide comprehensive, compassionate primary care and perioperative nursing support to patients and clients. • Support routine surgical procedures, including patient preparation, anesthesia administration and monitoring, surgical assisting, recovery, and post-operative care within the scope of the position. • Teach, coach, and mentor veterinary students during clinical service, modeling strong technical skills, clinical reasoning, communication, and patient advocacy. • Work independently and take initiative while recognizing when collaboration, escalation, or additional support is needed. • Communicate clearly and respectfully with clients, students, faculty, and team members. • Contribute to a collegial, psychologically safe, team-focused culture through emotional intelligence, self-awareness, adaptability, and constructive feedback. • Problem-solve and adapt to a fast-growing and changing environment with a growth mindset. Reporting Structure: The Veterinary Assistants and Veterinary Technicians will report directly to the Veterinary Technician Manager. Required Qualifications & Salary Information: The starting rate for each level is equivalent to the probationary rate listed below based on the collective bargaining unit guidelines. After completion of a six-month probationary period, the employee's pay can increase to the “Job Rate” for that position. Depending on experience, the candidate may be hired at the \"Job Rate\" to start. Veterinary Technicians (Credentialed, evidence of passing the VTNE) Level 1 Veterinary Technician Specialist (VTS) certification eligible or achieved, or equivalent specialty-level expertise Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $32.25/hour Job Rate: $35.40/hours Max Rate: $38.05/hour Level 2 Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $28.05/hour Job Rate: $31.00/hour Max Rate: $33.20/hour Level 3 Minimum 3 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $23.08/hour Job Rate: $26.55/hour Max Rate: $29.97/hour Veterinary Assistants (Non-Credentialed) Level 1 Associate degree or higher Minimum 5 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $23.08/hour Job Rate: $26.55/hour Max Rate: $29.97/hour Level 2 Associate degree or higher Minimum 3 years clinical experience Probationary Rate: $19.87/hour Job Rate: $22.48/hour Max Rate: $24.86/hour *Hourly rates reflect each position’s pay post 7/1/26 per the collective bargaining agreement. *Employees must have 4+ years of applicable experience to be hired above the probationary rate per the collective bargaining agreement. Experience & Skills Requirements: • Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as a veterinary technician or assistant; primary care, general practice, urgent care, emergency, or specialty experience is valued. • Comfortable supporting a broad primary care caseload and routine surgical procedures. • Proficient with anesthesia administration and anesthetic patient monitoring within the scope of the position, including integration of patient status, monitoring data, and clinical signs to recognize changes and communicate concerns promptly. ASA I-III (preferred experience with ASA I-V) • Experience with surgical assisting, perioperative nursing, and post-operative recovery. • Able to obtain blood pressure and interpret basic ECG, SpO2, and ETCO2 monitoring data in the context of the patient’s clinical status. • Demonstrates initiative, accountability, sound judgment, and the ability to organize work independently in a dynamic clinical environment. • Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to teach, coach, and provide constructive feedback to learners. • Demonstrates emotional intelligence, including self-awareness, professionalism, adaptability, empathy, and effective conflict management. • Collaborative and team-oriented, with a commitment to a positive learning and working environment. • Willing to cross-training into other departments • Available to work a schedule that may include weekend and holiday rotations. ****All hospital staff working clinical positions and handling live animals are required to be vaccinated against Rabies unless a medical or religious exemption is requested. Documentation may be required for approval of exemption. Costs associated with immunization and/or titer will be covered by the University for the employee. Preferred Qualifications: • CVT/LVT/RVT credential (active and in good standing, as applicable). • Experience in primary care/general practice, including preventive care, dentistry, anesthesia, and routine soft-tissue surgery support. • Experience teaching or mentoring veterinary or veterinary technology students, interns, or team members. • Excellent problem-solving abilities, including judgment, logic, creativity, and conflict resolution. • Strong attention to detail and commitment to patient safety. • Comfort with digital radiography and other commonly used diagnostic equipment. • Interest in professional growth, education, and helping build an evolving academic clinical service. Working Conditions Hazards Veterinary workers may be exposed to hazards like slips, trips, and falls. They may also be exposed to unpleasant odors, noises, and animal feces and urine. When working with animals that are frightened or in pain, veterinary workers risk being bitten, kicked, or scratched. Veterinary workers may be exposed to hazards like bloodborne pathogens, hazardous drugs, radiation, toxic waste, and chemical hazards such as disinfectants, pesticides, and latex. Animals The types of animals treated at a veterinary hospital can affect the working conditions. Our teaching hospital may consist, but is not limited to, the following types of animals: small mammals, large mammals, livestock, reptiles, avians, and other exotic animals. Information about the institution: A top 100 national public research institution, Rowan University offers bachelor’s through doctoral and professional programs in person and online to nearly 25,000 students. The fastest-growing public research institution in the Northeast and among the country’s top 10 fastest-growing, Rowan offers a thriving multidisciplinary environment with a strong emphasis on practical research in health care, engineering, science and business, while ensuring excellence in undergraduate education. Nationally recognized for innovation, high-quality, affordable education and public-private partnerships, Rowan is one of two universities in the U.S. to offer M.D., D.O. and D.V.M. degree programs. For more information on Rowan University, click here. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine is located on the Glassboro, New Jersey west campus, 22 miles southeast of Philadelphia. The Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine's first class of DVM students were admitted in September 2025. Facilities include a 167,000 square foot building that is shared as an academic teaching facility aimed at the delivery of pre-clinical training, a small animal teaching hospital, and a research facility. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ethnicity, race, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, national origin, (dis)ability status, military status, and other NJ protected classes. Rowan University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its educational programs and activities, including employment as required by Title IX. Rowan is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with (dis)abilities. As a state public University, Rowan employees are eligible to participate in the federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness program. More information on this program is available at https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service. Benefits: While salary is one component of employment, Rowan offers a comprehensive and meaningful benefits package designed to support your professional growth, well-being, and long-term career development. As a veterinary technician within an academic teaching hospital, you will: Contribute directly to the education and mentorship of future veterinarians Work alongside board-certified specialists and faculty in a collaborative, team-focused environment Engage in continuing education and professional development opportunities Build leadership skills in an academic and evolving clinical environment Be part of a mission-driven institution committed to innovation, community engagement, and advancing veterinary medicine Comprehensive State health and dental benefits, state pension: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Extensive accrued time off/paid holidays: 22 vacation/float days per year 12 sick days per year 9 paid holidays per year Tuition waiver for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouses and dependents after one year of employment). At Rowan, you are not only supporting excellent patient care. You are helping shape day-one-ready veterinarians, strengthen the veterinary profession, and build a collaborative academic clinical program from the ground up. Notes: The job posting will remain active until all positions are filled. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Oct 22 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Jan 25 2027 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
