    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501901/temporary-part-time-hourly-parttime-admissions-recruiter-graduate-and-nontraditional-admissions": {
      "title": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Part-Time Admissions Recruiter (Graduate and Non-traditional Admissions)",
      "description": "Temporary Part Time Hourly Part-Time Admissions Recruiter (Graduate and Non-traditional Admissions) Apply now Job no: 501901 Work type: Temporary Part-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Administrative - Clerical The Part-Time Admissions Recruiter plays a key role in the recruitment and enrollment efforts of Rowan University Graduate and Non-traditional Admissions. This position is responsible for attracting and engaging prospective graduate and non-traditional students, guiding them through the admissions process, and supporting their transition to enrolled students. Key Responsibilities: Actively recruit prospective students through various channels, including phone calls, email/text campaigns, events, and other recruitment strategies. Provide personalized guidance to prospective students, answering questions about programs, admissions requirements, financial aid, and the application process. Maintain a high level of knowledge about Rowan University’s programs, policies, and procedures. Collaborate with admissions team members to develop and implement recruitment strategies to meet enrollment goals. Assist with admissions events, both on-campus and virtual, to engage with prospective students and provide information about the department’s programs and offerings. Participate in on-campus recruitment activities, including tabling events, information sessions, and outreach initiatives, to promote the department’s programs and engage with prospective students. Maintain accurate and up-to-date records of interactions with prospective students in the admissions database. Provide front-desk coverage by answering incoming phone calls, responding to general inquiries, greeting visitors, and assisting prospective students and other walk-in guests. Assist walk-in students and visitors by providing information, directing them to appropriate resources or departments, and helping facilitate a welcoming and positive experience. Perform other duties as assigned to support the goals and operations of the department. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required, preferably in a related field such as education, counseling, or communications. Previous experience in admissions, recruitment, sales, marketing, or a related field preferred. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to effectively engage with a diverse range of individuals. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Knowledge of higher education admissions processes and best practices preferred. Rate: $20 per hour Hours: This temporary, part-time position is assigned no more than twenty-five (25) hours per week and is not to exceed 944 hours per fiscal year. Work is contracted annually to coincide with the fiscal year and is contingent upon budget appropriations. Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Advertised: Oct 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 4 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501906/assistant-director-2-certification-specialist-office-of-clinical-experiences": {
      "title": "Assistant Director 2, Certification Specialist - Office of Clinical Experiences",
      "description": "Assistant Director 2, Certification Specialist - Office of Clinical Experiences Apply now Job no: 501906 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Professional The Office of Clinical Experiences is seeking to hire an Assistant Director II, Certification Specialist. The Assistant Director II, Certification Specialist provides leadership and oversight for educator certification services within the College of Education. The position is responsible for coordinating certification processes, ensuring compliance with New Jersey Department of Education (NJDOE) regulations, advising educator preparation candidates, maintaining certification records, and serving as the College’s primary resource on educator certification policies and procedures. The Assistant Director II, Certification Specialist collaborates with faculty, academic departments, University offices, and external partners to support candidate success, educator preparation program quality, accreditation, and continuous improvement initiatives. The position contributes to strategic planning related to certification, licensure, educator preparation, and regulatory compliance while ensuring timely and accurate certification recommendations. Qualifications: Required Educator Certification Administration Serve as the College of Education’s lead certification specialist for all educator preparation programs. Review, verify, and recommend eligible candidates for certification through the New Jersey Department of Education certification system. Ensure compliance with all applicable NJDOE certification regulations, policies, procedures, and reporting requirements. Maintain complete and accurate certification records, documentation, and candidate files. Interpret certification regulations and provide guidance regarding licensure pathways, endorsements, reciprocity, testing requirements, and eligibility. Monitor changes in state certification regulations and implement necessary operational and procedural updates. Develop, maintain, and continuously improve certification policies, procedures, timelines, and workflow processes. Candidate Advising and Support Advise undergraduate, graduate, post-baccalaureate, and alternate route candidates regarding certification requirements and timelines. Provide individualized consultation to candidates concerning certification eligibility, deficiencies, endorsements, testing requirements, and application procedures. Coordinate certification workshops, orientation sessions, information sessions, and communication initiatives. Respond to inquiries from current candidates, alumni, school districts, and external stakeholders regarding educator certification. Develop informational materials, guides, and online resources related to certification processes. Program Coordination and Regulatory Compliance Collaborate with department chairs, program coordinators, faculty, and administrative staff to verify completion of certification requirements. Monitor candidate progression toward certification, including completion of required coursework, clinical experiences, assessments, and state requirements. Coordinate certification clearance processes prior to institutional recommendation. Assist with implementation of changes resulting from new legislation, NJDOE regulations, and institutional policies. Support institutional reporting and compliance activities related to educator preparation. Accreditation, Assessment, and Data Management Support CAEP accreditation activities and New Jersey Department of Education program approval and review processes. Collect, analyze, maintain, and report certification-related data to support accreditation, assessment, and institutional effectiveness. Prepare certification reports, data summaries, and compliance documentation for internal and external stakeholders. Assist with continuous improvement initiatives through analysis of certification trends and candidate outcomes. Maintain databases and records necessary for state, institutional, and accreditation reporting. Collaboration and Partnership Development Serve as the primary liaison with the New Jersey Department of Education regarding educator certification matters. Collaborate with the Registrar, Admissions, Graduate School, Office of Clinical Experiences, academic departments, and other University offices to ensure accurate candidate records and timely certification processing. Establish collaborative relationships with school districts and educational partners regarding certification and licensure questions. Represent the College on University, State, and professional committees related to educator preparation and certification, as assigned. Operational Leadership Recommend improvements that increase efficiency, effectiveness, and quality of certification services. Develop and implement operational procedures that enhance service delivery and regulatory compliance. Utilize technology systems to improve certification tracking, record management, reporting, and communication. Assist with training faculty and staff regarding certification policies and procedural changes. Supervise certification-related operations, graduate assistants, student employees, or other support personnel, as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission and strategic priorities of the College of Education. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited institution. Three to five years of progressively responsible experience in higher education administration, educator certification, student services, academic affairs, or a closely related field. Demonstrated knowledge of educator preparation and New Jersey educator certification regulations. Experience interpreting and applying complex policies, regulations, and procedures. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and analytical skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and student information systems. Preferred Qualifications Experience working within educator preparation programs in higher education. Experience using New Jersey Department of Education educator certification systems. Knowledge of CAEP accreditation standards and educator preparation accountability requirements. Experience with data analysis, assessment, compliance reporting, and continuous improvement initiatives. Experience developing operational procedures and coordinating complex administrative processes. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Comprehensive knowledge of educator certification regulations, licensure pathways, and educator preparation requirements. Ability to interpret and communicate complex state and institutional policies. Strong commitment to candidate success and customer service excellence. Ability to establish productive working relationships with faculty, staff, administrators, state agencies, school districts, candidates, and alumni. Excellent organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills. Ability to analyze data and prepare reports that support institutional decision-making. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and manage sensitive information. Demonstrated commitment to equity, professionalism, and continuous improvement. Physical Demands and Work Environment Work is primarily performed in an office environment. Regular use of computers and standard office equipment. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required to support College events, candidate workshops, or certification activities. Occasional travel to university meetings, professional conferences, or state meetings may be required. Salary & Benefits: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is AFT: Range 24 ($76,486-$87,954), with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. For internal applicants, salary is determined per the Pay Adjustment formula (NJAC 4A:3-4.9 & 4.10). For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S., as the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. All positions are contingent upon budget appropriations. Only completed online applications submitted on or before the posted deadline will be considered. Advertised: Oct 21 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 11:55 PM Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501889/veteran-peer-recovery-coach-health-educator-iii-stratford-nj": {
      "title": "Veteran Peer Recovery Coach, (Health Educator III), Stratford, NJ",
      "description": "Veteran Peer Recovery Coach, (Health Educator III), Stratford, NJ Apply now Job no: 501889 Work type: Temporary Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Administrative - Clerical, Professional Veteran Peer Recovery Coach (Health Educator III) Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Location: Stratford, NJ (With travel throughout South Jersey) Department: NeuroMusculoskeletal Institute (NMI) Reports to: Director of Administration, NMI Updated : 10/13/2026 Summary: The Veteran Peer Recovery Coach provides non-clinical peer recovery support to veterans and other individuals impacted by Opioid Use Disorder (OUD), Substance Use Disorders (SUD), and co-occurring behavioral health conditions. Working within a Medication for Opioid Use Disorder (MOUD) program, the Coach uses lived experience to engage participants, reduce barriers to treatment, support recovery, and promote long-term wellness in alignment with SAMHSA grant objectives. *This is a temporary, grant-funded position with funding currently approved through September 2031. Employment in this role is contingent upon the continuation of grant funding. Essential Duties and Responsibilities • Conduct outreach and engagement activities to identify individuals who may benefit from MOUD and recovery support services. • Provide peer recovery coaching, mentoring, advocacy, and wellness support. • Assist individuals in accessing FDA-approved MOUD services and psychosocial supports. • Support participant engagement and retention in treatment and recovery services. • Provide recovery planning, goal setting, and self-advocacy support. • Coordinate referrals to housing, employment, transportation, education, healthcare, veteran, and social service resources. • Collaborate with providers addressing co-occurring mental health and substance use disorders. • Promote overdose prevention education and connect participants to opioid overdose reversal medication resources. • Support access to telehealth and innovative service delivery approaches. • Build relationships with veteran-serving agencies, recovery organizations, housing providers, and community partners. • Assist with infectious disease screening referrals and linkage to care as appropriate. • Maintain accurate documentation and grant-related data collection. • Participate in interdisciplinary meetings and quality improvement activities. Qualifications • Veteran status preferred. • High school diploma required; Associate or Bachelor degree preferred. • Peer Recovery Specialist/Recovery Coach certification preferred or ability to obtain. • Demonstrated personal recovery experience appropriate for peer support practice. • Knowledge of OUD, MOUD, harm reduction, and recovery support services. • Strong communication, advocacy, and engagement skills. Valid driver's license required. Regular travel within the community is required, including operating a Rowan University vehicle in support of outreach and program activities. Knowledge and Skills • Motivational interviewing. • Recovery-oriented systems of care. • Trauma-informed approaches. • Veteran cultural competency. • Community outreach and engagement. • Documentation and data collection. • Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Grant Program Alignment This position supports grant objectives to expand access to MOUD, increase treatment engagement and retention, reduce opioid misuse and overdose, strengthen recovery support services, improve access for underserved populations, and promote long-term recovery through coordinated community partnerships and evidence-based recovery support practices. Working Conditions Work is performed in office, clinic, community, outreach, and telehealth settings. Local travel and occasional evening or weekend hours may be required. SALARY INFORMATION In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $57,084.51-$59,612.39,000, with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents).” *Some benefits do not apply to temporary employees. For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ NOTES: Only completed, online applications submitted on or before the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Advertised: Oct 19 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 2 2026 05:00 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501892/director-of-administration-obgyn-surgery-rowanvirtua-school-of-osteopathic-medicine-stratford-nj": {
      "title": "Director of Administration - OBGYN & Surgery, Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (Stratford, NJ)",
      "description": "Director of Administration - OBGYN & Surgery, Rowan-Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine (Stratford, NJ) Apply now Job no: 501892 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Stratford, New Jersey Categories: Managerial, Professional Director of Administration - OBGYN & Surgery Rowan Medicine – Rowan ‑ Virtua School of Osteopathic Medicine Affiliate of Virtua Medical Group Location: Stratford, NJ (with travel required to all OBGYN & Surgery offices) Department: OBGYN & Surgery Reports to: Department Chair SUMMARY: The Director of Administration, in collaboration with the Department Chair and Rowan Medicine Administration (RMA), provides organizational leadership and operational oversight for the department. Reporting directly to the Department Chair, this role manages key operational, financial, compliance, human resources, and administrative functions that support the department's clinical, educational, and research missions. The Director of Administration supervises administrative personnel, ensures effective communication and collaboration across stakeholders, and develops systems and processes that support departmental goals. This position serves as a liaison between the department and university, Rowan Medicine, and external partners, while promoting operational excellence, regulatory compliance, financial stewardship, and strategic growth. Depending on departmental structure and needs, the Director may oversee clinical, educational, research, and business operations. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Other duties may be assigned in response to emerging and changing departmental needs. Clinical Operations Provides leadership and oversight of departmental clinical operations to ensure efficient, high-quality service delivery and achievement of organizational goals. Develops, standardizes, and monitors operational processes, workflows, and performance metrics; identifies opportunities for improvement and implements corrective actions as needed. Collaborates with clinical and administrative leadership to optimize patient access, scheduling, referral management, provider productivity, and overall practice performance. Oversees the integrity and effectiveness of clinical information systems, electronic medical records, billing systems, and related operational technologies, partnering with appropriate stakeholders to resolve issues. Leads quality improvement initiatives and supports departmental compliance with regulatory, accreditation, and organizational standards. Collaborates with departmental leadership and external partners to support clinical network development, care coordination, and practice growth initiatives. Financial Management Participates in the development, implementation, monitoring, and management of departmental budgets in collaboration with department leadership and institutional finance teams. Monitors financial performance, identifies variances, and recommends corrective actions to support fiscal responsibility and long-term sustainability. Oversees the administration and stewardship of departmental funding sources, including clinical revenue, academic budgets, grants, contracts, and discretionary funds, as applicable. Serves as a liaison with finance, accounting, compliance, legal, and other centralized administrative offices regarding departmental financial matters. Develops and analyzes financial reports, forecasts, and business plans to support strategic planning and operational decision-making. Strategic Planning and Business Development Collaborates with departmental leadership to develop and implement strategic initiatives that advance the department's clinical, educational, and research missions while monitoring industry trends, regulatory changes, and market conditions that may impact departmental objectives. Identifies opportunities for growth, operational enhancement, program development, and service expansion. Assists in the development, negotiation, implementation, renewal, and management of contracts, affiliations, and service agreements in partnership with institutional stakeholders. Participates in business planning, feasibility assessments, and implementation of new initiatives and services. Human Resources Management Supports departmental leadership in faculty and staff recruitment, hiring, onboarding, retention, and succession planning activities. Supervises administrative staff and may oversee managers and coordinators responsible for departmental operations. Develops position descriptions, conducts performance evaluations, and recommends personnel actions consistent with institutional policies. Coordinates credentialing, licensure, certifications, malpractice coverage, and clinical privileges, as applicable. Oversees workforce planning, scheduling, timekeeping, and staffing models to support departmental needs and operational efficiency. Fosters a positive, collaborative, and accountable work environment aligned with institutional values while supporting employee development and professional growth. Compliance, Policies, and Department Administration Ensures departmental compliance with applicable federal, state, accreditation, healthcare, and university regulations, policies, and standards. Develops, implements, reviews, and monitors departmental policies, procedures, and internal controls. Represents the department on institutional committees, task forces, and project teams as assigned. Coordinates departmental planning activities, communications, reporting requirements, and administrative operations. Supports faculty development, staff education, onboarding, and ongoing training initiatives. Performs other related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS : To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. EDUCATION AND/OR EXPERIENCE Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Healthcare Administration, Finance, Public Administration, or a related field required. Minimum of five (5) years of progressive leadership experience in healthcare administration, clinical operations, academic medicine, higher education, or a related healthcare environment. Equivalent combinations of education and directly related experience may be considered. Master's degree in Business Administration (MBA), Healthcare Administration (MHA), Public Administration (MPA), or related field preferred. Experience supporting clinical operations, physician practices, academic departments, or healthcare service lines preferred. Familiarity with healthcare operations, budgeting, compliance requirements, electronic medical records, revenue cycle processes, and performance improvement methodologies preferred. Demonstrated leadership, organizational, analytical, project management, and communication skills required. Ability to build collaborative relationships across multidisciplinary teams and effectively manage multiple priorities in a complex environment. SALARY INFORMATION In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $130,000 to $135,000.00, with placement within the range determined by candidate's qualifications, professional experience, internal equity, and other factors. BENEFIT INFORMATION For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents).” NOTES: Only completed online applications submitted by the deadline will be considered. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S.; Rowan University does not sponsor visas for this position. Advertised: Oct 19 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 2 2026 03:30 PM Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.rowan.edu/en-us/job/501850/director-of-software-development-information-resources-technology": {
      "title": "Director of Software Development, Information Resources & Technology",
      "description": "Director of Software Development, Information Resources & Technology Apply now Job no: 501850 Work type: Regular Full-Time Location: Glassboro, New Jersey Categories: Professional Director of Software Development Rowan University is seeking a Director of Software Development to shape the next generation of the University’s application and digital services and lead a team responsible for software development and application integrations. Working closely with partners across the University’s academic units, administrative, and operational, you will translate institutional needs into reliable, scalable solutions across Rowan’s enterprise application portfolio, with a particular focus on ERP and ERP-adjacent systems and services. Your critical software engineering leadership will require partnering with IRT business analysts, infrastructure, security, and other technology teams on shared platforms, cloud architecture, and enterprise standards. This role will also help shape how Rowan responds to a rapidly changing software-development landscape. You will drive the practical adoption of AI-enabled applications, AI-assisted software engineering, modern DevOps practices, and cloud-based application architectures while maintaining appropriate standards for security, maintainability, data stewardship, and reliable production operations. What you get to do: Lead and develop a key software development team, aligning staff resources, technical capabilities, and priorities with University needs while fostering accountability, professional growth, collaboration, and strong engineering practices. Work closely with IRT business analysts as a primary partner in translating business requirements into well-designed technical solutions, and collaborate directly with administrative, operational, and academic stakeholders throughout planning, design, implementation, and support. Lead the technical architecture and engineering direction for the enterprise applications within the team’s portfolio, establishing scalable approaches to application design, systems integration, AI adoption, reusable services, data exchange, and workflow automation. Drive the automation and modernization of University business processes through thoughtful application development, integration, configuration, and use of enterprise platforms. Oversee software development, application enhancements, upgrades, integrations, and modernization initiatives throughout their lifecycle, balancing new capabilities with operational priorities, system sustainability, and technical debt. Lead the practical adoption of AI-assisted software engineering and AI-enabled application capabilities, evaluating where these technologies can improve development productivity, application functionality, and business process automation while maintaining appropriate controls for validation, security, privacy, and data use. Drive modern software engineering and DevOps practices, including source code management, code review, automated testing, continuous integration and continuous delivery, repeatable deployment processes, observability, and secure development practices. Apply Agile delivery methods where appropriate to improve planning, feedback, and incremental delivery. Partner with IRT infrastructure, security, and other technical teams on cloud and hybrid application architecture. Evaluate the appropriate use of Microsoft Azure, Amazon Web Services, managed platforms, and other cloud technologies for applications within the portfolio. Oversee the reliable operation and support of enterprise applications and the application-layer components within the team’s responsibility, including monitoring, maintenance, patching, upgrades, troubleshooting, performance, automation, and production support. Lead complex, long-term initiatives involving technical team, vendors, business areas, and institutional stakeholders while maintaining the ability to respond effectively to emergent operational needs. Establish and continually improve software engineering and application support standards, including documentation, architecture, accessibility, data handling, lifecycle management, operational readiness, and service quality. Manage departmental budgets, vendor relationships, and technology investments, and forecast future staffing, platform, training, and resource requirements. We are looking for people who have: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related discipline. Minimum of six years of professional experience in software development, enterprise application services, or application administration. Substantial hands-on software engineering experience, including direct experience designing, developing, debugging, testing, deploying, and supporting production software. Candidates should have strong technical fluency in application architecture, programming languages, databases, source code management, testing, deployment, integration, and software design tradeoffs. Demonstrated experience designing, delivering, integrating, and supporting complex enterprise applications, including experience establishing scalable application architectures, integration patterns, reusable services, data exchange, and automation. Experience designing, integrating, and supporting enterprise application solutions across SaaS, cloud, and hybrid environments, including platforms such as Microsoft Azure and Amazon Web Services. Candidates should understand how applications interact with identity, security, integration services, data platforms, networking, and underlying infrastructure. Strong understanding of contemporary software engineering and delivery practices, including the software development lifecycle, DevOps principles, CI/CD, automated testing, observability, secure development practices, and modern application architecture approaches such as modular or service-oriented architectures, event-driven integration, managed services, containers, and serverless technologies. Working knowledge of AI technologies, including AI-assisted software development and the integration of AI capabilities into enterprise applications, together with an understanding of their implications for software quality, security, privacy, data protection, and operational support. Demonstrated experience managing and developing technical staff, leading technical teams, and successfully navigating organizational and technological change. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities, sound technical judgment, and the ability to establish priorities and balance long-term strategic initiatives with short-term operational and emergent needs. Excellent oral, written, and presentation communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts, architectural decisions, risks, tradeoffs, and business implications to technical and nontechnical audiences. Preferred but not required: Master’s degree in Computer Science or a related discipline. Experience supporting ERP or ERP-adjacent enterprise applications in a complex organization. Hands-on experience implementing AI-enabled applications, AI-assisted development practices, or intelligent business-process automation. Experience modernizing legacy or highly integrated enterprise applications. Experience developing technology roadmaps and presenting strategic planning materials or investment recommendations to senior leadership. Experience with ITSM support models and practices, including incident, problem, change, and service management. Demonstrated intellectual curiosity and a strong interest in emerging technologies. What we offer: Excellent retirement benefits with 8% employer contribution 22 days of vacation time allotted annually with the ability to carryover a full year of accrued time 15 days of sick time allotted annually with unlimited carryover Excellent Medical and Dental coverage - low contribution, low copay Full tuition benefits available to you, eligible dependents, spouse, and domestic or civil union partners Wellness incentives and other programs to help support your work-life balance Housing incentive for Glassboro residents For a full list of benefits see go.rowan.edu/benefits Salary & Benefits: In compliance with The State of New Jersey's Pay Transparency Act, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000 to $175,000. When extending any salary offer, Rowan University considers many factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, work experience, education, training, key skills, internal equity, as well as market and other organizational considerations. For eligible employees, benefits include: comprehensive NJ State health, dental and retirement benefits, extensive accrued time off/paid holidays, and tuition reimbursement for employee, spouse, and dependents to attend Rowan University, Glassboro. (Tuition reimbursement will apply to undergraduate degrees only for spouse and dependents). For more detailed information, please visit: https://sites.rowan.edu/hr/benefits/ Notes: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the US, and the university will not sponsor an applicant for a work visa for this position. Only completed online applications submitted will be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Advertised: Oct 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    }
  },
